WEBVTT

00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:12.388
4000 Essential English Words.

00:00:12.448 --> 00:00:13.209
One.

00:00:13.269 --> 00:00:14.919
Paul Nation.

00:00:14.979 --> 00:00:17.169
Copyright 2009.

00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:18.990
Compass Publishing.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:27.631
All rights reserved.

00:00:27.691 --> 00:00:35.832
Unit 1.

00:00:35.892 --> 00:00:37.483
Word List.

00:00:37.543 --> 00:00:39.255
Afraid.

00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:43.360
When someone is afraid, they feel fear.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.683
The woman was afraid of what she saw.

00:00:47.743 --> 00:00:49.866
Agree.

00:00:49.926 --> 00:00:54.748
To agree is to say yes or to think the same way.

00:00:54.808 --> 00:00:58.622
The food is very good in that restaurant.

00:00:58.682 --> 00:01:01.404
I agree with you.

00:01:01.464 --> 00:01:03.576
Angry.

00:01:03.636 --> 00:01:08.992
When someone is angry, they may want to speak loudly or fight.

00:01:09.052 --> 00:01:14.286
She didn't do her homework, so her father is angry.

00:01:14.346 --> 00:01:16.526
Arrive.

00:01:16.586 --> 00:01:21.270
To arrive is to get to or reach someplace.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:27.053
The bus always arrives at the corner of my street at four.

00:01:27.112 --> 00:01:29.204
Attack.

00:01:29.264 --> 00:01:33.606
To attack is to try to fight or to hurt.

00:01:33.666 --> 00:01:38.794
The man with the sword attacked the other man first.

00:01:38.854 --> 00:01:40.980
Bottom.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.111
The bottom is the lowest part.

00:01:44.171 --> 00:01:48.602
The bottom of my shoe has a hole in it.

00:01:48.662 --> 00:01:50.773
Clever.

00:01:50.832 --> 00:01:56.174
When someone is clever, they can solve a hard puzzle or problem.

00:01:56.233 --> 00:02:00.384
The clever boy thought of a good idea.

00:02:00.444 --> 00:02:02.515
Cruel.

00:02:02.575 --> 00:02:07.460
When someone is cruel, they do bad things to hurt others.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.586
The cruel man yelled at his sister.

00:02:11.646 --> 00:02:19.842
Finally, if something happens finally, it happens after a long time or at the end.

00:02:19.902 --> 00:02:25.596
He finally crossed the finish line after five hours of running.

00:02:25.656 --> 00:02:27.708
Hide.

00:02:27.768 --> 00:02:31.930
To hide is to try not to let others see you.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:36.622
The other children will hide while you count to 100.

00:02:36.682 --> 00:02:38.890
Hunt.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:43.853
To hunt is to look for or search for an animal to kill.

00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:48.676
Long ago, people hunted with bows and arrows.

00:02:48.736 --> 00:02:50.817
Lot.

00:02:50.876 --> 00:03:02.008
A lot means a large number or amount of people, animals, things, etc. There are a lot of apples in the basket.

00:03:02.068 --> 00:03:04.134
Middle.

00:03:04.194 --> 00:03:08.926
The middle of something is the center or halfway point.

00:03:08.986 --> 00:03:14.418
The Canadian flag has a maple leaf in the middle of it.

00:03:14.478 --> 00:03:16.588
Moment.

00:03:16.648 --> 00:03:20.820
A moment is a second or a very short time.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:25.502
I was only a few moments late for the meeting.

00:03:25.562 --> 00:03:27.712
Pleased.

00:03:27.772 --> 00:03:31.238
When someone is pleased, they are happy.

00:03:31.297 --> 00:03:35.853
She was pleased with the phone call she received.

00:03:35.913 --> 00:03:38.023
Promise.

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:42.434
To promise is to say you will do something for sure.

00:03:42.494 --> 00:03:47.176
He promised to return my key by tomorrow.

00:03:47.236 --> 00:03:49.416
Reply.

00:03:49.476 --> 00:03:54.317
To reply is to give an answer or say back to someone.

00:03:54.377 --> 00:03:57.438
She asked him what time his meeting was.

00:03:57.498 --> 00:04:00.089
He replied at 3.

00:04:00.149 --> 00:04:02.410
Safe.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:06.352
When a person is safe, they are not in danger.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:10.844
Put on your seatbelt and the car to be safe.

00:04:10.904 --> 00:04:12.904
Trick.

00:04:12.964 --> 00:04:16.936
A trick is something you do to fool another person.

00:04:16.996 --> 00:04:21.008
His car trick really surprised us.

00:04:21.068 --> 00:04:27.770
Well, you use well to say that something was done in a good way.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:32.163
The couple can dance quite well.

00:04:32.223 --> 00:04:36.237
The lion and the rabbit.

00:04:36.296 --> 00:04:39.760
A cruel lion lived in the forest.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:44.032
Every day he killed and ate a lot of animals.

00:04:44.092 --> 00:04:49.076
The other animals were afraid the lion would kill them all.

00:04:49.136 --> 00:04:53.140
The animals told the lion, let's make a deal.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:05:00.405
If you promise to eat only one animal each day, then one of us will come to you every day.

00:05:00.465 --> 00:05:04.138
Then you don't have to hunt and kill us.

00:05:04.198 --> 00:05:09.004
The plan sounded well thought out to the lion, so he agreed.

00:05:09.064 --> 00:05:16.270
But he also said, If you don't come every day, I promise to kill all of you the next day.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:22.396
Each day after that one animal went to the lion so that the lion could eat it.

00:05:22.456 --> 00:05:26.070
Then, all the other animals were safe.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:30.454
Finally, it was the rabbit's turn to go to the lion.

00:05:30.513 --> 00:05:38.170
The rabbit went very slowly that day, so the lion was angry when the rabbit finally arrived.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:43.282
The lion angrily asked the rabbit, why are you late?

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:47.104
I was hiding from another lion in the forest.

00:05:47.164 --> 00:05:51.916
That lion said he was the king, so I was afraid.

00:05:51.976 --> 00:05:56.478
The lion told the rabbit, I am the only king here.

00:05:56.538 --> 00:06:00.790
Take me to that other lion and I will kill him.

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:05.942
The rabbit replied, I will be happy to show you where he lives.

00:06:06.001 --> 00:06:11.044
The rabbit led the lion to an old well in the middle of the forest.

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:14.725
The well was very deep with water at the bottom.

00:06:14.784 --> 00:06:17.942
The rabbit told the lion, look in there.

00:06:18.002 --> 00:06:20.423
The lion lives at the bottom.

00:06:20.483 --> 00:06:25.984
When the lion looked in the well, he could see his own face in the water.

00:06:26.044 --> 00:06:28.904
He thought that was the other lion.

00:06:28.964 --> 00:06:35.376
Without waiting another moment, the lion jumped into the well to attack the other lion.

00:06:35.436 --> 00:06:37.246
He never came out.

00:06:37.306 --> 00:06:45.062
All of the other animals in the forest were very pleased with their rabbit's clever trick.

00:06:45.122 --> 00:06:49.608
Unit 2, word list.

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:51.388
Adventure.

00:06:51.448 --> 00:06:56.142
An adventure is a fun or exciting thing that you do.

00:06:56.202 --> 00:07:00.754
Riding in the rough water was an adventure.

00:07:00.814 --> 00:07:03.026
Approach.

00:07:03.085 --> 00:07:06.778
To approach something means to move close to it.

00:07:06.838 --> 00:07:10.300
The boy approached his school.

00:07:10.359 --> 00:07:12.570
Chemical.

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:16.953
A chemical is something that scientists use in chemistry.

00:07:17.012 --> 00:07:20.964
The scientist mixed the chemicals.

00:07:21.024 --> 00:07:23.236
Carefully.

00:07:23.295 --> 00:07:29.309
Carefully means with great attention, especially to detail or safety.

00:07:29.368 --> 00:07:34.032
The baby carefully climbed down the stairs.

00:07:34.092 --> 00:07:36.242
Create.

00:07:36.302 --> 00:07:39.694
To create means to make something new.

00:07:39.754 --> 00:07:44.836
She created an igloo from blocks of snow.

00:07:44.896 --> 00:07:46.956
Evil.

00:07:47.016 --> 00:07:51.459
Evil describes something or someone bad or cruel.

00:07:51.519 --> 00:07:53.110
Not good.

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:57.404
The evil figure scared us all.

00:07:57.464 --> 00:07:59.776
Experiment.

00:07:59.835 --> 00:08:04.299
An experiment is a test that you do to see what will happen.

00:08:04.358 --> 00:08:09.232
The student did an experiment in science class.

00:08:09.292 --> 00:08:11.304
Kill.

00:08:11.364 --> 00:08:15.550
To kill someone or something is to make them die.

00:08:15.609 --> 00:08:19.684
I killed the fly with the fly swatter.

00:08:19.744 --> 00:08:22.206
Laboratory.

00:08:22.266 --> 00:08:26.278
A laboratory is a room where a scientist works.

00:08:26.338 --> 00:08:30.290
My mother works in a laboratory.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.401
Laugh.

00:08:32.461 --> 00:08:37.463
Laugh is the sound made when someone is happy or a funny thing occurs.

00:08:37.524 --> 00:08:41.846
The sound of their laugh filled the room.

00:08:41.906 --> 00:08:44.126
Loud.

00:08:44.186 --> 00:08:49.228
If a sound is loud, it is strong and very easy to hear.

00:08:49.288 --> 00:08:54.702
The man's voice was so loud that we all could hear him.

00:08:54.762 --> 00:09:01.408
Nervous When a person is nervous, they think something bad will happen.

00:09:01.468 --> 00:09:06.311
The boy became nervous when he heard the news.

00:09:06.371 --> 00:09:11.812
Noise A noise is an unpleasant sound.

00:09:11.872 --> 00:09:16.152
The crying baby made a loud noise.

00:09:16.212 --> 00:09:18.444
Project.

00:09:18.504 --> 00:09:23.878
A project is a type of work that you do for a school or a job.

00:09:23.938 --> 00:09:29.361
His afternoon work project was to paint the room green.

00:09:29.421 --> 00:09:31.572
Scare.

00:09:31.632 --> 00:09:35.796
To scare someone is to make them feel afraid.

00:09:35.856 --> 00:09:41.002
My uncle was scared by what he saw in the room.

00:09:41.062 --> 00:09:43.218
Secret.

00:09:43.278 --> 00:09:47.500
A secret is something that you do not tell other people.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:51.882
The two boys were sharing a secret.

00:09:51.942 --> 00:09:53.964
Shout.

00:09:54.024 --> 00:09:57.186
To shout is to say something loudly.

00:09:57.246 --> 00:10:03.088
My boss shouted at me because I was late for work.

00:10:03.148 --> 00:10:05.270
Smell.

00:10:05.329 --> 00:10:09.732
To smell something means to use your nose to sense it.

00:10:09.792 --> 00:10:13.865
The two friends smell the flower.

00:10:13.925 --> 00:10:16.066
Terrible.

00:10:16.126 --> 00:10:19.910
If something is terrible, it is very bad.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:24.583
The way he treated his classmate was terrible.

00:10:24.643 --> 00:10:26.734
Worse.

00:10:26.794 --> 00:10:32.160
If something is worse, it is of poorer quality than another thing.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:37.692
Business was worse this month than last month.

00:10:37.752 --> 00:10:41.094
The laboratory.

00:10:41.154 --> 00:10:46.608
Mia's father had a laboratory, but she had no idea what was in it.

00:10:46.668 --> 00:10:50.942
Her dad always closed and locked the door when he went in.

00:10:51.002 --> 00:10:54.664
She knew that he used it to do projects for work.

00:10:54.724 --> 00:10:58.268
He never told Mia what these projects were.

00:10:58.328 --> 00:11:02.820
One night, Mia approached the door to the laboratory.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:08.322
She stopped and thought, I wonder what crazy experiment he is doing now.

00:11:08.382 --> 00:11:11.224
Suddenly, she heard a loud noise.

00:11:11.284 --> 00:11:13.894
It sounded like an evil laugh.

00:11:13.954 --> 00:11:18.566
The noise scared her, so she walked quickly back to her room.

00:11:18.626 --> 00:11:22.408
The next night, her friend Liz came to her house.

00:11:22.468 --> 00:11:26.700
When Liz arrived, Mia told her about the night before.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:30.172
Oh, it was terrible, she said.

00:11:30.232 --> 00:11:32.764
Why don't we see what is in there?"

00:11:32.824 --> 00:11:34.074
Liz asked.

00:11:34.134 --> 00:11:36.636
It will be a fun adventure.

00:11:36.696 --> 00:11:42.110
Mia felt nervous about going into her father's laboratory, but she agreed.

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:44.832
As always, the door was locked.

00:11:44.892 --> 00:11:48.922
They waited until Mia's father left the laboratory to eat dinner.

00:11:48.982 --> 00:11:51.062
He didn't lock the door.

00:11:51.122 --> 00:11:53.485
Liz said, let's go.

00:11:53.545 --> 00:11:55.678
The laboratory was dark.

00:11:55.738 --> 00:11:58.780
The girls walked down the stairs carefully.

00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:01.652
Mia smelled strange chemicals.

00:12:01.712 --> 00:12:04.996
What terrible thing was her father creating?

00:12:05.055 --> 00:12:08.320
Suddenly, they heard an evil laugh.

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:12.214
It was even worse than the one Mia heard the night before.

00:12:12.274 --> 00:12:15.296
What if a monster was going to kill them?

00:12:15.356 --> 00:12:17.276
Mia had to do something.

00:12:17.336 --> 00:12:19.016
She shouted for help.

00:12:19.076 --> 00:12:22.387
Mia's father ran into the room and turned on the lights.

00:12:22.447 --> 00:12:24.878
Oh no, he said.

00:12:24.938 --> 00:12:27.408
You must have learned my secret.

00:12:27.468 --> 00:12:31.259
You're monster tried to kill us, Mia said.

00:12:31.319 --> 00:12:33.940
Monster, he asked.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.500
You mean this?

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.043
He had a pretty doll in his hands.

00:12:38.103 --> 00:12:39.686
The doll laughed.

00:12:39.746 --> 00:12:43.058
The laugh didn't sound so evil anymore.

00:12:43.118 --> 00:12:45.660
I made this for your birthday.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:47.821
I wanted to give it to you then.

00:12:47.881 --> 00:12:49.812
But you can have it now.

00:12:49.872 --> 00:12:53.044
I hope you like it.

00:12:53.104 --> 00:12:56.066
Unit 3.

00:12:56.126 --> 00:13:03.212
Word List Alien An alien is a creature from a different world.

00:13:03.272 --> 00:13:06.902
The alien came in peace.

00:13:06.962 --> 00:13:09.172
Among.

00:13:09.232 --> 00:13:13.916
If you are among certain things, they are all around you.

00:13:13.976 --> 00:13:18.888
There was a red apple among the green ones.

00:13:18.948 --> 00:13:24.182
Chart A chart is a list of information.

00:13:24.242 --> 00:13:29.114
We used a chart to see how we had improved.

00:13:29.174 --> 00:13:35.134
Cloud A cloud is a group of water drops in the sky.

00:13:35.195 --> 00:13:39.472
The sky was filled with white clouds.

00:13:39.532 --> 00:13:41.852
Comprehend.

00:13:41.912 --> 00:13:45.364
To comprehend something is to understand it.

00:13:45.424 --> 00:13:49.754
Henry could not comprehend the message.

00:13:49.814 --> 00:13:52.085
Describe.

00:13:52.145 --> 00:13:58.226
To describe is to say or write what someone or something is like.

00:13:58.286 --> 00:14:04.838
They describe their tree as colorful, with gold ribbon and a star.

00:14:04.898 --> 00:14:06.948
Ever.

00:14:07.008 --> 00:14:09.820
Ever means at any time.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:16.013
Going skiing last winter was the most fun I've ever had.

00:14:16.073 --> 00:14:18.164
Fail.

00:14:18.224 --> 00:14:22.808
To fail means you do not succeed in what you try to do.

00:14:22.868 --> 00:14:27.420
Since he failed to get the jump, he was sad.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.562
Friendly.

00:14:29.622 --> 00:14:34.436
Friendly is behaving in a pleasant, kind way toward someone.

00:14:34.496 --> 00:14:38.850
The friendly animals came up to the girl.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.981
Grade.

00:14:41.041 --> 00:14:45.642
A grade is a score or mark given to someone's work.

00:14:45.702 --> 00:14:50.494
I managed to get good grades on my report card.

00:14:50.554 --> 00:14:52.804
Instead.

00:14:52.864 --> 00:14:55.985
Instead means in place of.

00:14:56.045 --> 00:15:00.676
The eighth a carrot instead of the ice cream.

00:15:00.736 --> 00:15:03.022
Library.

00:15:03.082 --> 00:15:07.067
A library is a place where you go to read books.

00:15:07.127 --> 00:15:11.808
The library at school is full of books.

00:15:11.868 --> 00:15:18.000
Planet A planet is a large round thing in space.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:22.772
Saturn is the planet with the ring around it.

00:15:22.832 --> 00:15:28.704
Report A report is something students write for school.

00:15:28.764 --> 00:15:32.838
Karen had trouble writing her report.

00:15:32.898 --> 00:15:34.990
Several.

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:38.772
Several is more than two but not many.

00:15:38.832 --> 00:15:43.043
He had to read several books for class.

00:15:43.103 --> 00:15:45.164
Solve.

00:15:45.224 --> 00:15:49.035
To solve something is to find an answer to it.

00:15:49.095 --> 00:15:54.086
All the students could easily solve the math problem.

00:15:54.146 --> 00:15:56.318
Suddenly.

00:15:56.378 --> 00:16:01.797
If something happens suddenly, it happens quickly and unexpectedly.

00:16:01.857 --> 00:16:07.449
I was suddenly surprised by the cake my friends brought me.

00:16:07.509 --> 00:16:09.740
Suppose.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:12.694
To suppose is to guess.

00:16:12.754 --> 00:16:16.596
I suppose I should go home now.

00:16:16.656 --> 00:16:23.692
Universe The universe is the known or supposed objects in space.

00:16:23.752 --> 00:16:28.706
The universe is so large that it cannot be measured.

00:16:28.766 --> 00:16:33.846
View To view is to look at something.

00:16:33.906 --> 00:16:38.906
Michael likes to view himself in the mirror.

00:16:38.966 --> 00:16:48.127
The report Lee sat among the books at the library and thought about his group project.

00:16:48.188 --> 00:16:53.402
They had to turn it in soon, but he hadn't even started his part.

00:16:53.462 --> 00:16:56.305
Jack and Claire were in his group.

00:16:56.365 --> 00:16:58.016
They had worked hard.

00:16:58.076 --> 00:17:03.412
They were also very smart, and Lee didn't want them to get a bad grade.

00:17:03.472 --> 00:17:05.333
Jack did the report.

00:17:05.393 --> 00:17:11.255
He wrote a lot of very good sentences and described things with great adjectives.

00:17:11.315 --> 00:17:14.346
Claire drew a nice map of the stars.

00:17:14.406 --> 00:17:18.228
Now Lee needed to do his part of the project.

00:17:18.287 --> 00:17:23.020
Well, I suppose I need to start my model, Lee thought.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:26.591
Making a model of a planet was really hard.

00:17:26.651 --> 00:17:32.413
Lee tried to read several books, but he couldn't comprehend any of the charts.

00:17:32.473 --> 00:17:36.854
We're going to fail because of me," Lee said.

00:17:36.914 --> 00:17:45.106
He put his head down on the table and said, I wish I could see a planet instead of having to read about it.

00:17:45.166 --> 00:17:48.316
Suddenly, there was a bright light.

00:17:48.376 --> 00:17:54.648
Lee was pulled from his chair, threw the roof and right into a strange ship.

00:17:54.708 --> 00:17:57.468
Hello, Ken, said an alien.

00:17:57.528 --> 00:17:59.480
Did you ask for help?

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:03.746
Lee told the friendly alien all about his project.

00:18:03.806 --> 00:18:07.600
The alien agreed to help Lee solve his problem.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:11.325
First, we'll fly through space to view the universe.

00:18:11.385 --> 00:18:15.150
Then I can help you make a model of my planet.

00:18:15.211 --> 00:18:18.134
Soon they were going through the clouds.

00:18:18.194 --> 00:18:19.826
They passed the moon.

00:18:19.886 --> 00:18:21.778
Then they viewed Mars.

00:18:21.838 --> 00:18:24.180
Lee was very excited.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:29.324
Instead of a bad grade, his group would have the best project ever.

00:18:29.384 --> 00:18:31.406
It's time to go home.

00:18:31.466 --> 00:18:33.638
The alien finally said.

00:18:33.698 --> 00:18:38.710
On the way back, he helped Lee make a model of the planet Mars.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:41.250
Soon, they were on Earth.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.201
Thanks, Lee said.

00:18:43.261 --> 00:18:45.502
My model will be awesome.

00:18:45.562 --> 00:18:56.320
Then he took his model and said goodbye to his new friend.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:19:07.840
Unit 4. Word List. Appropriate. It is appropriate to wear a suit when you go to the office.

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:10.110
Avoid.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:14.042
To avoid something is to stay away from it.

00:19:14.102 --> 00:19:18.273
Avoid the broken bottle on the floor.

00:19:18.333 --> 00:19:20.524
Behave.

00:19:20.584 --> 00:19:26.186
To behave is to act in a particular way, especially to be good.

00:19:26.246 --> 00:19:31.398
She always behaves well when her father is around.

00:19:31.458 --> 00:19:33.610
Calm.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:38.334
When someone is calm, they do not get excited or upset.

00:19:38.394 --> 00:19:43.259
A nice warm bath makes me feel so calm.

00:19:43.319 --> 00:19:45.610
Concern.

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:48.694
Concern is a feeling of worry.

00:19:48.754 --> 00:19:53.998
I was filled with concern after reading the newspaper.

00:19:54.058 --> 00:19:56.250
Content.

00:19:56.310 --> 00:20:00.454
To be content is to be happy and not want more.

00:20:00.514 --> 00:20:05.668
The baby looked very content sitting on the floor.

00:20:05.728 --> 00:20:07.930
Expect.

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:12.412
If you expect something to happen, you believe it will happen.

00:20:12.472 --> 00:20:17.166
I expect the boss to be here very soon.

00:20:17.226 --> 00:20:19.518
Frequently.

00:20:19.578 --> 00:20:23.480
When something happens frequently, it happens often.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:29.478
We meet frequently, either at the beginning or ending of the week.

00:20:29.538 --> 00:20:34.876
Habit A habit is a thing that you do often.

00:20:34.936 --> 00:20:39.538
Smoking is a bad habit that can kill you.

00:20:39.598 --> 00:20:44.530
Instruct to instruct is to teach.

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:49.473
My teacher instructs us in several subjects.

00:20:49.533 --> 00:20:54.766
Issue An issue is an important topic.

00:20:54.826 --> 00:21:00.099
The men spoke about issues that were important to the people.

00:21:00.159 --> 00:21:02.220
None.

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:06.213
None means not any of someone or something.

00:21:06.273 --> 00:21:08.634
He spent all his money.

00:21:08.694 --> 00:21:11.156
There is none left.

00:21:11.216 --> 00:21:13.347
Patient.

00:21:13.407 --> 00:21:18.790
If a person is patient, they don't become angry or upset easily.

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:24.104
I had to be patient and wait until five o'clock to leave.

00:21:24.164 --> 00:21:26.354
Positive.

00:21:26.414 --> 00:21:29.600
If something is positive, it is good.

00:21:29.661 --> 00:21:37.568
She has a positive future ahead of her after finishing college.

00:21:37.628 --> 00:21:43.531
To punish means to make someone suffer for breaking the rules or laws.

00:21:43.591 --> 00:21:48.534
To punish me, my teacher had me stand in the corner.

00:21:48.594 --> 00:21:50.784
Represent.

00:21:50.844 --> 00:21:56.026
To represent is to speak or act for a person or group.

00:21:56.086 --> 00:22:00.326
My lawyer will represent me in court.

00:22:00.386 --> 00:22:02.343
Shake.

00:22:02.403 --> 00:22:07.304
To shake is to move back and forth or up and down quickly.

00:22:07.364 --> 00:22:12.496
When people shake hands, it usually means they agree.

00:22:12.556 --> 00:22:14.686
Spread.

00:22:14.746 --> 00:22:18.868
To spread is to move quickly to more places.

00:22:18.928 --> 00:22:22.898
I like to spread butter on my toast.

00:22:22.958 --> 00:22:25.049
Stroll.

00:22:25.109 --> 00:22:29.326
To stroll means to walk slowly and calmly.

00:22:29.386 --> 00:22:33.684
My dog and I stroll through the park today.

00:22:33.744 --> 00:22:35.846
Village.

00:22:35.906 --> 00:22:39.178
A village is a very small town.

00:22:39.238 --> 00:22:44.441
There are only a few houses in my village.

00:22:44.501 --> 00:22:47.934
The dog's bell.

00:22:47.994 --> 00:22:51.056
John's dog was a bad dog.

00:22:51.116 --> 00:22:53.272
He bit people frequently.

00:22:53.332 --> 00:22:56.058
John had great concern about this.

00:22:56.118 --> 00:22:59.630
It was not an appropriate way for a dog to behave.

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:04.144
His friends in the village always expected the dog to bite them.

00:23:04.204 --> 00:23:07.866
The news about John's dog spread through the village.

00:23:07.926 --> 00:23:11.018
None of the people wanted to go to John's house.

00:23:11.078 --> 00:23:15.720
John tried to instruct the dog to behave, but it never worked.

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:19.961
He tried to be patient and teach the dog to be calm.

00:23:20.021 --> 00:23:22.182
That also didn't work.

00:23:22.242 --> 00:23:25.053
John didn't want to punish the dog.

00:23:25.113 --> 00:23:28.144
How will I stop my dog's bad habit?

00:23:28.204 --> 00:23:30.024
John asked himself.

00:23:30.084 --> 00:23:33.636
John's friend came to talk to him about the issue.

00:23:33.696 --> 00:23:40.252
During their important meeting, his friend said, the people in the village asked me to represent them.

00:23:40.312 --> 00:23:43.008
We want your dog to stop this habit.

00:23:43.068 --> 00:23:46.039
Why don't you put a bell around the dog's neck?

00:23:46.099 --> 00:23:49.750
This way, we would hear your dog coming down the street.

00:23:49.810 --> 00:23:52.511
John thought this was a great idea.

00:23:52.571 --> 00:23:55.282
Now people could stay away from the dog.

00:23:55.342 --> 00:23:58.693
It would not be able to bite anyone anymore.

00:23:58.753 --> 00:24:01.224
The dog liked the bell too.

00:24:01.284 --> 00:24:04.205
People looked at him when they heard his bell.

00:24:04.265 --> 00:24:06.666
This made the dog very content.

00:24:06.726 --> 00:24:09.903
He liked the song the bell played when he walked.

00:24:09.963 --> 00:24:14.720
One day, John's dog strolled through the village and met some other dogs.

00:24:14.780 --> 00:24:17.690
He expected them to want a bell like his.

00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:19.801
But they laughed at his bell.

00:24:19.861 --> 00:24:22.632
They said the bell made people avoid him.

00:24:22.692 --> 00:24:24.922
John's dog shook his head.

00:24:24.982 --> 00:24:28.723
No, they look at me because they like the bell.

00:24:28.783 --> 00:24:33.834
The other dog said, you have the wrong idea of what makes you popular.

00:24:33.894 --> 00:24:35.984
Of course they like your bell.

00:24:36.044 --> 00:24:39.100
It tells them where you are so they can avoid you.

00:24:39.160 --> 00:24:41.785
You aren't able to bite them anymore.

00:24:41.845 --> 00:24:49.109
You see, being popular isn't something positive when it's for the wrong reason.

00:24:49.169 --> 00:24:52.120
Unit 5.

00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:53.671
Word List.

00:24:53.731 --> 00:24:55.412
Aware.

00:24:55.472 --> 00:24:59.254
If you are aware of something, you know about it.

00:24:59.314 --> 00:25:03.446
I was not aware of the ringing phone.

00:25:03.506 --> 00:25:05.808
Badly.

00:25:05.868 --> 00:25:09.953
Badly means in a severe or harmful way.

00:25:10.013 --> 00:25:14.358
He hurt his arm badly playing with friends.

00:25:14.418 --> 00:25:16.618
Belong.

00:25:16.678 --> 00:25:20.079
If something belongs to you, you own it.

00:25:20.139 --> 00:25:23.709
The blue suit belongs to Paul.

00:25:23.769 --> 00:25:26.000
Continue.

00:25:26.060 --> 00:25:29.370
To continue something is to keep doing it.

00:25:29.430 --> 00:25:34.921
She stood under her umbrella as the rain continued to fall.

00:25:34.981 --> 00:25:36.992
Error.

00:25:37.052 --> 00:25:40.086
An error is something you do wrong.

00:25:40.146 --> 00:25:45.875
I made an error on my report, so my boss was angry.

00:25:45.934 --> 00:25:48.216
Experience.

00:25:48.276 --> 00:25:52.308
An experience is something you have seen or done.

00:25:52.368 --> 00:25:56.572
Raw climbing was a fun experience.

00:25:56.632 --> 00:25:58.722
Field.

00:25:58.782 --> 00:26:02.255
A field is a big area of land.

00:26:02.315 --> 00:26:06.340
The field of flowers looks so pretty.

00:26:06.400 --> 00:26:12.514
Hurt To hurt is to do something that makes you feel pain.

00:26:12.574 --> 00:26:16.754
She hurt her leg falling down the stairs.

00:26:16.814 --> 00:26:23.557
Judgment Judgment is the ability to form opinions or decisions.

00:26:23.617 --> 00:26:28.538
It's good judgment to recycle your aluminum cans.

00:26:28.598 --> 00:26:34.991
Likely If something likely happens, it will probably happen.

00:26:35.051 --> 00:26:40.045
I will likely stay at home and watch TV tonight.

00:26:40.105 --> 00:26:42.276
Normal.

00:26:42.336 --> 00:26:47.190
If something is normal, it is not strange nor surprising to you.

00:26:47.250 --> 00:26:51.544
It is normal for me to bathe every night.

00:26:51.604 --> 00:26:53.675
Rare.

00:26:53.735 --> 00:26:57.718
If something is rare, you do not see it very often.

00:26:57.778 --> 00:27:01.769
It is rare for him to miss his fight.

00:27:01.829 --> 00:27:04.008
Relax.

00:27:04.068 --> 00:27:06.660
To relax is to rest.

00:27:06.720 --> 00:27:10.792
The frog relaxed in the warm sun.

00:27:10.852 --> 00:27:13.082
Request.

00:27:13.142 --> 00:27:16.634
To request something is to ask for it.

00:27:16.694 --> 00:27:22.356
The little girl requested a special gift from Santa Claus.

00:27:22.416 --> 00:27:24.598
Reside.

00:27:24.658 --> 00:27:29.850
To reside means to live somewhere permanently or for a long time.

00:27:29.910 --> 00:27:36.073
My brother and his family reside in a lovely house on the beach.

00:27:36.133 --> 00:27:38.274
Result.

00:27:38.334 --> 00:27:42.388
A result is something that happens because of something else.

00:27:42.448 --> 00:27:48.322
As a result of all the rain, the man had to climb on the roof.

00:27:48.382 --> 00:27:50.424
Roll.

00:27:50.484 --> 00:27:54.688
To roll is to move by turning over and over.

00:27:54.748 --> 00:27:59.572
You must roll the ball into the pins when you bowl.

00:27:59.632 --> 00:28:01.696
Since.

00:28:01.756 --> 00:28:06.870
Since is used to talk about a past event, still happening now.

00:28:06.930 --> 00:28:11.964
Since 1992, he has been driving that car.

00:28:12.024 --> 00:28:14.126
Visible.

00:28:14.186 --> 00:28:17.570
If something is visible, it can be seen.

00:28:17.630 --> 00:28:22.012
The moon and stars were visible in the night sky.

00:28:22.072 --> 00:28:23.674
Wild.

00:28:23.734 --> 00:28:27.354
If something is wild, it is found in nature.

00:28:27.414 --> 00:28:34.144
You should be careful around a fox because it is a wild animal.

00:28:34.204 --> 00:28:43.160
The Jackal and the Sun Child A jackal is a wild dog with a big black back.

00:28:43.220 --> 00:28:45.432
It resides in the desert.

00:28:45.492 --> 00:28:49.234
But how did the jackal get his black back?

00:28:49.294 --> 00:28:51.706
This was how it happened.

00:28:51.766 --> 00:28:54.918
One day the jackal saw a girl.

00:28:54.978 --> 00:28:57.119
She was sitting upon a rock.

00:28:57.179 --> 00:28:59.651
She was not a normal child.

00:28:59.711 --> 00:29:03.054
She was a rare and beautiful sunchild.

00:29:03.114 --> 00:29:06.106
She was bright and warm like the sun.

00:29:06.166 --> 00:29:09.298
The child saw that Jackal and smiled.

00:29:09.358 --> 00:29:15.512
She said, Jackal, I have been relaxing on this rock for too long.

00:29:15.572 --> 00:29:20.936
I must get home soon, but I am slow and you are fast.

00:29:20.996 --> 00:29:24.367
You will likely get me home more quickly.

00:29:24.427 --> 00:29:28.257
Then she requested, will you carry me home?

00:29:28.317 --> 00:29:31.168
If you do, I'll give you a gift.

00:29:31.228 --> 00:29:36.060
This necklace belongs to me, but I will give it to you."

00:29:36.120 --> 00:29:41.853
The wild Jackal agreed, so the Sun Child sat on the dog's back.

00:29:41.913 --> 00:29:45.985
They started to walk, but soon the Jackal felt ill.

00:29:46.045 --> 00:29:49.266
The Sun Child was very hot on his back.

00:29:49.326 --> 00:29:52.788
The heat was hurting his back very badly.

00:29:52.848 --> 00:29:57.479
I made a terrible error in judgment," he thought.

00:29:57.539 --> 00:30:02.360
He shouldn't have agreed to carry her, so he asked her to get off.

00:30:02.420 --> 00:30:03.930
But she did not.

00:30:03.990 --> 00:30:07.571
The Jackal's back continued to get harder and harder.

00:30:07.631 --> 00:30:12.162
He had to get away from the Sun Child, so he made a plan.

00:30:12.222 --> 00:30:15.032
First, he ran as fast as he could.

00:30:15.092 --> 00:30:17.643
He hoped the Sun Child would fall off.

00:30:17.703 --> 00:30:19.194
But she did not.

00:30:19.254 --> 00:30:27.920
So when the Sun Child was looking at the sky, not aware of the jackal's next plan, he jumped into a field of flowers.

00:30:27.980 --> 00:30:31.282
As a result, the child rolled off his back.

00:30:31.342 --> 00:30:33.404
The jackal ran away.

00:30:33.464 --> 00:30:39.547
But the Sun Child left a mark on the jackal's back, a visible black mark.

00:30:39.607 --> 00:30:47.486
Ever since his experience with the Sun Child, the jackal has had a black back.

00:30:47.546 --> 00:30:52.040
Unit 6, word list.

00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:53.931
Advantage.

00:30:53.991 --> 00:30:57.072
An advantage is something that helps you.

00:30:57.132 --> 00:31:02.133
Being tall is an advantage to a basketball player.

00:31:02.193 --> 00:31:04.264
Cause.

00:31:04.324 --> 00:31:07.424
To cause is to make something happen.

00:31:07.484 --> 00:31:11.276
The cold weather caused her to get sick.

00:31:11.336 --> 00:31:13.396
Choice.

00:31:13.456 --> 00:31:18.282
A choice is the act or possibility of picking something.

00:31:18.342 --> 00:31:22.718
I had my choice of five doors to open.

00:31:22.778 --> 00:31:25.059
Community.

00:31:25.119 --> 00:31:29.051
A community is a group of people who live together.

00:31:29.111 --> 00:31:34.154
The kids from my community usually play together.

00:31:34.214 --> 00:31:36.264
Dead.

00:31:36.324 --> 00:31:39.586
To be dead is to not be alive.

00:31:39.646 --> 00:31:44.269
A dead person is usually buried in the ground.

00:31:44.329 --> 00:31:46.490
Distance.

00:31:46.550 --> 00:31:51.304
The distance between two things is how far it is between them.

00:31:51.365 --> 00:31:59.310
The distance between the Earth and the Moon is 384,400 km.

00:31:59.370 --> 00:32:01.410
Escape.

00:32:01.471 --> 00:32:05.374
To escape is to run away from something bad.

00:32:05.434 --> 00:32:09.986
The butterfly could not escape from the cage.

00:32:10.046 --> 00:32:12.058
Face.

00:32:12.118 --> 00:32:15.479
If you face a problem, you deal with it.

00:32:15.539 --> 00:32:21.842
My sister and I have to find a better way to face our differences.

00:32:21.902 --> 00:32:23.943
Follow.

00:32:24.003 --> 00:32:28.656
To follow means to go behind someone and go where they go.

00:32:28.716 --> 00:32:32.728
The little boy followed his mother home.

00:32:32.788 --> 00:32:34.730
Fright.

00:32:34.790 --> 00:32:37.912
Fright is the feeling of being scared.

00:32:37.971 --> 00:32:41.158
She was filled with fright.

00:32:41.218 --> 00:32:47.374
Ghost A ghost is the spirit of a dead person.

00:32:47.434 --> 00:32:51.526
Many people are afraid of ghosts.

00:32:51.586 --> 00:32:57.288
Individual An individual is one person.

00:32:57.348 --> 00:33:02.310
Only one individual could win the bicycle race.

00:33:02.370 --> 00:33:08.375
Pet A pet is an animal that lives with people.

00:33:08.435 --> 00:33:13.451
Out of all my pets, the dog is my favorite.

00:33:13.511 --> 00:33:15.482
Reach.

00:33:15.542 --> 00:33:19.004
To reach means to arrive at a place.

00:33:19.064 --> 00:33:23.558
I was happy to finally reach my destination.

00:33:23.618 --> 00:33:25.819
Return.

00:33:25.879 --> 00:33:29.382
To return is to go back to a place.

00:33:29.442 --> 00:33:34.656
I was happy to return home to my mom after school.

00:33:34.716 --> 00:33:36.890
Survive.

00:33:36.950 --> 00:33:39.900
To survive is to stay alive.

00:33:39.960 --> 00:33:44.152
My dog survived her fall into the water.

00:33:44.212 --> 00:33:46.252
Upset.

00:33:46.312 --> 00:33:50.044
To be upset is to be unhappy about something.

00:33:50.104 --> 00:33:54.414
She was upset because she broke her toy.

00:33:54.474 --> 00:33:56.565
Voice.

00:33:56.625 --> 00:34:01.297
A voice is the sound a person makes when they talk or sing.

00:34:01.357 --> 00:34:06.495
He used a microphone so everyone could hear his voice.

00:34:06.555 --> 00:34:08.622
Weather.

00:34:08.682 --> 00:34:11.603
The weather is the condition of the air.

00:34:11.664 --> 00:34:20.136
Hot, rainy, windy, etc. The weather can be sunny, rainy or cold.

00:34:20.196 --> 00:34:22.257
Wise.

00:34:22.318 --> 00:34:27.840
To be wise is to use experience and intelligence to make good choices.

00:34:27.900 --> 00:34:33.932
Many people believe that owls are very wise animals.

00:34:33.992 --> 00:34:37.471
The Friendly Ghost.

00:34:37.531 --> 00:34:41.081
A nice woman lived by a large river.

00:34:41.142 --> 00:34:43.344
She loved children.

00:34:43.404 --> 00:34:46.356
She wanted to help them in any way.

00:34:46.417 --> 00:34:48.548
She loved her community.

00:34:48.608 --> 00:34:51.492
And everyone in the community loved her.

00:34:51.552 --> 00:34:56.126
She lived a very long time, and became very wise.

00:34:56.186 --> 00:34:59.428
When she died, she became a ghost.

00:34:59.488 --> 00:35:03.962
She was dead, but every night she returned to her community.

00:35:04.022 --> 00:35:10.356
She wanted to help children and not to cause them fright, but she had a scary voice.

00:35:10.416 --> 00:35:14.688
Children were afraid of her, but the ghost was a good one.

00:35:14.748 --> 00:35:17.350
She only scared them to help them.

00:35:17.410 --> 00:35:22.172
One night, some children and a dog were playing by the river.

00:35:22.232 --> 00:35:26.970
They were having fun with their pet, but they were far from home.

00:35:27.031 --> 00:35:29.537
Then the weather became bad.

00:35:29.597 --> 00:35:31.988
It rained and rained.

00:35:32.048 --> 00:35:34.099
The river was rising.

00:35:34.159 --> 00:35:36.020
It was very dark.

00:35:36.080 --> 00:35:38.291
The children knew they were lost.

00:35:38.351 --> 00:35:43.113
They needed to go north, but they didn't know which direction it was.

00:35:43.173 --> 00:35:47.395
When the moon came out, they saw a ghost by the river.

00:35:47.455 --> 00:35:51.060
The ghost said, go away!

00:35:51.120 --> 00:35:53.893
The children felt great fright.

00:35:53.953 --> 00:35:56.024
They knew it was a ghost.

00:35:56.084 --> 00:35:58.355
Then the ghost moved closer.

00:35:58.415 --> 00:36:01.277
She yelled again, go away!

00:36:01.297 --> 00:36:04.648
The children became very upset.

00:36:04.708 --> 00:36:06.960
Some of them began to cry.

00:36:07.020 --> 00:36:09.300
The children knew they had a choice.

00:36:09.360 --> 00:36:14.693
They could escape, or they could stay and face this scary individual in the dark.

00:36:14.753 --> 00:36:17.914
The children ran a long distance away.

00:36:17.975 --> 00:36:20.629
The ghost followed them all the way.

00:36:20.689 --> 00:36:23.214
Finally the children reached home.

00:36:23.274 --> 00:36:25.524
The ghost was very happy.

00:36:25.585 --> 00:36:28.526
Soon the river rose higher and higher.

00:36:28.586 --> 00:36:30.628
It was very dangerous.

00:36:30.688 --> 00:36:33.640
The ghost had helped the children survive.

00:36:33.700 --> 00:36:36.401
She had saved them from the rising water.

00:36:36.461 --> 00:36:39.372
She also used her power to lead them home.

00:36:39.432 --> 00:36:42.915
Sometimes meeting a ghost has advantages.

00:36:42.975 --> 00:36:46.896
A ghost can save your life.

00:36:46.956 --> 00:36:50.018
Unit 7.

00:36:50.078 --> 00:36:51.658
Word list.

00:36:51.718 --> 00:36:53.339
Allow.

00:36:53.400 --> 00:36:57.302
To allow something to happen means to let it happen.

00:36:57.362 --> 00:37:01.975
Having a ticket will allow you to enter the show.

00:37:02.035 --> 00:37:04.106
Announce.

00:37:04.167 --> 00:37:07.088
To announce something is to make it known.

00:37:07.149 --> 00:37:12.342
He announced to everyone his new idea for the company.

00:37:12.402 --> 00:37:14.522
Beside.

00:37:14.582 --> 00:37:18.842
When someone or something is beside you, they are next to you.

00:37:18.902 --> 00:37:22.661
The two brothers stood beside each other.

00:37:22.721 --> 00:37:24.842
Challenge.

00:37:24.902 --> 00:37:28.343
A challenge is something difficult to complete.

00:37:28.403 --> 00:37:33.044
It was a challenge to climb to the top of the mountain.

00:37:33.104 --> 00:37:35.126
Claim.

00:37:35.186 --> 00:37:38.906
To claim means to say that something is true.

00:37:38.966 --> 00:37:43.958
He claimed to know why the country's laws were weak.

00:37:44.018 --> 00:37:51.079
Condition The condition of someone or something is the state that they are in.

00:37:51.139 --> 00:37:55.310
The patient's condition was very good.

00:37:55.370 --> 00:38:02.423
Contribute To contribute to something means to do something to make it successful.

00:38:02.483 --> 00:38:07.515
We decided to contribute money to the new hospital.

00:38:07.575 --> 00:38:14.006
Difference A difference is a way that something is not like other things.

00:38:14.066 --> 00:38:19.706
The biggest difference between the birds is the color of their feathers.

00:38:19.766 --> 00:38:21.886
Divide.

00:38:21.946 --> 00:38:25.667
To divide something is to make it into smaller parts.

00:38:25.727 --> 00:38:28.868
We divided the pizza.

00:38:28.928 --> 00:38:31.018
Expert.

00:38:31.078 --> 00:38:35.270
An expert is someone who is very good at doing something.

00:38:35.330 --> 00:38:39.215
The wizard was an expert at magic.

00:38:39.275 --> 00:38:41.390
Famous.

00:38:41.450 --> 00:38:46.023
If someone or something is famous, they are known to many people.

00:38:46.083 --> 00:38:50.716
The Eiffel Tower in Baris is very famous.

00:38:50.776 --> 00:38:52.827
Force.

00:38:52.887 --> 00:38:56.399
Force is a person's strength or power.

00:38:56.458 --> 00:39:01.382
He used all his force to try and open the door.

00:39:01.442 --> 00:39:03.472
Harm.

00:39:03.533 --> 00:39:08.230
Harm is hurt or problems caused to someone or something.

00:39:08.290 --> 00:39:13.806
A hot iron can cause great harm if you are not careful.

00:39:13.866 --> 00:39:15.867
Lay.

00:39:15.927 --> 00:39:21.118
To lay means to put or place in a horizontal or flat position.

00:39:21.178 --> 00:39:24.879
Don't lay your socks on the floor.

00:39:24.939 --> 00:39:26.919
Peace.

00:39:26.979 --> 00:39:29.740
Peace is a time without war.

00:39:29.800 --> 00:39:33.881
A white dove is a symbol for peace.

00:39:33.941 --> 00:39:35.982
Prince.

00:39:36.042 --> 00:39:38.952
A prince is the son of a king.

00:39:39.012 --> 00:39:42.891
The prince and the princess were married.

00:39:42.952 --> 00:39:45.092
Protect.

00:39:45.152 --> 00:39:49.123
To protect someone is to stop them from getting hurt.

00:39:49.183 --> 00:39:53.104
Firemen protect us from fires.

00:39:53.164 --> 00:39:55.194
Sense.

00:39:55.254 --> 00:39:59.535
To sense something is to know about it without being told.

00:39:59.595 --> 00:40:03.316
I could sense that he was watching me.

00:40:03.376 --> 00:40:05.416
Sudden.

00:40:05.476 --> 00:40:09.277
When something is sudden, it happens very quickly.

00:40:09.338 --> 00:40:13.284
He felt a sudden pain in his chest.

00:40:13.344 --> 00:40:18.944
Therefore, therefore means, for this reason.

00:40:19.004 --> 00:40:24.821
He is fat, therefore he will go on a diet.

00:40:24.881 --> 00:40:31.053
The best prince King Minos was very sick.

00:40:31.113 --> 00:40:33.434
His condition was getting worse.

00:40:33.494 --> 00:40:35.235
He had three sons.

00:40:35.295 --> 00:40:36.816
He loved them all.

00:40:36.876 --> 00:40:39.908
He had to announce who would become king.

00:40:39.968 --> 00:40:43.970
Two of the princes stood waiting outside the king's room.

00:40:44.030 --> 00:40:47.192
Theseus was the oldest and strongest.

00:40:47.252 --> 00:40:50.034
He thought his father would make him king.

00:40:50.094 --> 00:40:53.728
Pilius, the second son, thought differently.

00:40:53.788 --> 00:40:56.090
He was an expert with weapons.

00:40:56.150 --> 00:40:58.602
He thought the king would choose him.

00:40:58.662 --> 00:41:05.328
When I'm king, Theseus told Pilius, I'll let you contribute to the defense of our country.

00:41:05.388 --> 00:41:07.300
You can lead the army.

00:41:07.360 --> 00:41:09.601
Paleus became angry.

00:41:09.661 --> 00:41:13.303
Father knows I'm famous for my sword skills.

00:41:13.363 --> 00:41:15.054
He'll make me king.

00:41:15.114 --> 00:41:17.314
You, Theseus yelled.

00:41:17.374 --> 00:41:19.045
He won't choose you.

00:41:19.106 --> 00:41:20.906
The kingdom is mine.

00:41:20.966 --> 00:41:22.437
Paleus claimed.

00:41:22.497 --> 00:41:27.404
Father will give it to me, or I'll use force to take it.

00:41:27.464 --> 00:41:33.091
Theseus made a sudden move to take out his sword, then Paleus did the same.

00:41:33.151 --> 00:41:40.500
Beating me will be a challenge, Theseus and fight me now, the winner gets the kingdom.

00:41:40.560 --> 00:41:42.202
Palius agreed.

00:41:42.262 --> 00:41:45.092
King Minos could hear his sons fighting.

00:41:45.152 --> 00:41:48.424
The youngest son, Jason, stood beside him.

00:41:48.484 --> 00:41:50.954
He sensed his father's sadness.

00:41:51.014 --> 00:41:54.505
The king laid his hand flat on Jason's arm.

00:41:54.565 --> 00:41:58.166
Your brothers fight too much, the king told him.

00:41:58.226 --> 00:42:01.478
I must protect my kingdom from all harm.

00:42:01.538 --> 00:42:03.648
They'll divide it between them.

00:42:03.708 --> 00:42:06.039
The people won't know what to do.

00:42:06.099 --> 00:42:07.630
There'll be war.

00:42:07.690 --> 00:42:10.802
I can't allow either of them to be king.

00:42:10.862 --> 00:42:14.105
Therefore, I'm making you king.

00:42:14.165 --> 00:42:17.328
Your kindness has always made you special.

00:42:17.388 --> 00:42:20.690
It's the difference between you and your brothers.

00:42:20.750 --> 00:42:22.501
You can bring peace.

00:42:22.561 --> 00:42:23.862
They can't.

00:42:23.922 --> 00:42:25.673
Then the king died.

00:42:25.733 --> 00:42:29.655
Theseus and Paleus heard that their youngest brother was king.

00:42:29.715 --> 00:42:31.246
They were surprised.

00:42:31.306 --> 00:42:33.938
They realized that their fighting was wrong.

00:42:33.998 --> 00:42:37.269
It had kept them from saying goodbye to their father.

00:42:37.329 --> 00:42:40.041
They agreed to have Jason as their king.

00:42:40.101 --> 00:42:44.163
He was the best choice.

00:42:44.223 --> 00:42:47.034
Unit 8.

00:42:47.094 --> 00:42:48.516
Word List.

00:42:48.576 --> 00:42:50.146
Accept.

00:42:50.206 --> 00:42:53.877
To accept something that is offered is to take it.

00:42:53.937 --> 00:42:57.897
I accepted the girl's very nice gift.

00:42:57.957 --> 00:43:00.098
Arrange.

00:43:00.158 --> 00:43:03.918
To arrange things is to put them in the right place.

00:43:03.978 --> 00:43:08.990
Please arrange the bowling pins in order so we can play.

00:43:09.050 --> 00:43:11.130
Attend.

00:43:11.190 --> 00:43:14.301
To attend something is to go to it.

00:43:14.361 --> 00:43:18.692
My sister and I attend the same school.

00:43:18.752 --> 00:43:20.842
Balance.

00:43:20.902 --> 00:43:24.534
To balance something is to keep it from falling.

00:43:24.594 --> 00:43:29.166
We saw an elephant balance itself on a ball.

00:43:29.226 --> 00:43:35.677
Contrast A contrast is the sharp difference between two things.

00:43:35.737 --> 00:43:40.658
The contrast between my parents is very noticeable.

00:43:40.718 --> 00:43:42.858
Encourage.

00:43:42.918 --> 00:43:47.039
To encourage someone is to make them want to do something.

00:43:47.099 --> 00:43:51.777
My football coach will encourage us when we are losing.

00:43:51.838 --> 00:43:54.016
Familiar.

00:43:54.076 --> 00:43:59.469
If someone or something is familiar to you, you know them well.

00:43:59.530 --> 00:44:03.952
The two friends were very familiar with each other.

00:44:04.013 --> 00:44:06.074
Grab.

00:44:06.134 --> 00:44:11.247
To grab is to take hold of someone or something suddenly.

00:44:11.307 --> 00:44:14.679
I grabbed a pear from the tree.

00:44:14.740 --> 00:44:16.790
Hang.

00:44:16.850 --> 00:44:20.899
To hang something is to keep it above the ground.

00:44:20.959 --> 00:44:26.488
I drew a picture of my family and my mother hung it on the wall.

00:44:26.548 --> 00:44:28.628
Huge.

00:44:28.688 --> 00:44:32.190
If something is huge, it is very big.

00:44:32.250 --> 00:44:36.532
At work, my father drives a huge truck.

00:44:36.592 --> 00:44:38.914
Necessary.

00:44:38.974 --> 00:44:42.776
If something is necessary, you must do it.

00:44:42.836 --> 00:44:48.658
It is necessary to have a passport when you travel to a foreign country.

00:44:48.718 --> 00:44:50.744
Pattern.

00:44:50.804 --> 00:44:55.470
A pattern is a way in which something is done or organized.

00:44:55.530 --> 00:45:03.365
My pattern of brushing my teeth is the same as most people's.

00:45:03.425 --> 00:45:07.228
To propose something is to say that it should be done.

00:45:07.288 --> 00:45:13.152
Santa Claus proposed that I try to be a good boy all year.

00:45:13.212 --> 00:45:18.918
Purpose A purpose is the reason that you do something.

00:45:18.978 --> 00:45:23.623
The purpose of exercising is to get into shape.

00:45:23.684 --> 00:45:29.296
Release To release something is to stop holding it.

00:45:29.356 --> 00:45:33.007
She released the bird from her hands.

00:45:33.068 --> 00:45:40.041
Require To require something is to say that it is necessary.

00:45:40.101 --> 00:45:44.916
We require teachers to have a university degree.

00:45:44.976 --> 00:45:47.078
Single.

00:45:47.138 --> 00:45:50.920
If something is single, then there is only one.

00:45:50.980 --> 00:45:54.732
I have a single key in my hand.

00:45:54.792 --> 00:45:57.004
Success.

00:45:57.064 --> 00:46:01.366
Success is doing something well that you choose to do.

00:46:01.426 --> 00:46:05.638
My daughter was a big success at school.

00:46:05.698 --> 00:46:07.609
Tear.

00:46:07.669 --> 00:46:10.880
To tear something means to pull it apart.

00:46:10.940 --> 00:46:14.243
It is easy to tear paper.

00:46:14.303 --> 00:46:16.354
theory.

00:46:16.414 --> 00:46:20.235
A theory is an idea about how something works.

00:46:20.295 --> 00:46:26.226
We talked about Einstein's theory of relativity in class.

00:46:26.286 --> 00:46:30.768
How the sun and the moon were made.

00:46:30.828 --> 00:46:35.389
Do you ever wonder where the moon and the sun came from?

00:46:35.449 --> 00:46:38.810
The Inuit people of Alaska have a theory.

00:46:38.870 --> 00:46:42.146
They tell a story about a beautiful girl.

00:46:42.206 --> 00:46:44.209
She was very nice.

00:46:44.269 --> 00:46:48.476
In contrast, her brother was a mean little boy.

00:46:48.536 --> 00:46:51.142
One day he proposed something.

00:46:51.203 --> 00:46:54.598
We should go to a party," he said.

00:46:54.658 --> 00:46:56.270
The girl accepted.

00:46:56.330 --> 00:46:59.312
First it was necessary for her to prepare.

00:46:59.372 --> 00:47:02.555
She arranged her hair and put on nice clothes.

00:47:02.615 --> 00:47:05.118
This required a lot of time.

00:47:05.178 --> 00:47:09.261
But the girl worked hard and soon she had success.

00:47:09.321 --> 00:47:11.352
She looked perfect.

00:47:11.412 --> 00:47:13.882
They attended the party together.

00:47:13.942 --> 00:47:16.171
The girl was having fun.

00:47:16.231 --> 00:47:18.823
Later she walked into the bathroom.

00:47:18.883 --> 00:47:21.624
Suddenly, the lights were turned off.

00:47:21.684 --> 00:47:25.277
Someone grabbed her hair and tore her clothes.

00:47:25.337 --> 00:47:27.478
She ran out of the bathroom.

00:47:27.538 --> 00:47:30.090
She wanted to know who did this to her.

00:47:30.150 --> 00:47:32.152
Then she had an idea.

00:47:32.212 --> 00:47:34.253
She fixed her hair again.

00:47:34.313 --> 00:47:36.954
This time it was even more beautiful.

00:47:37.014 --> 00:47:40.076
She even balanced beautiful jewels in it.

00:47:40.136 --> 00:47:43.690
She wanted to encourage the person to grab it again.

00:47:43.750 --> 00:47:46.424
She put black dirt in her hair.

00:47:46.484 --> 00:47:49.536
The purpose of this was to catch the person.

00:47:49.596 --> 00:47:53.368
She went to the bathroom again, and it was the same pattern.

00:47:53.428 --> 00:47:56.732
The lights went off, and someone grabbed her hair.

00:47:56.792 --> 00:47:59.833
When he released it, his hand was black.

00:47:59.894 --> 00:48:02.236
The girl returned to the party.

00:48:02.296 --> 00:48:05.928
She knew there was only a single person with a black hand.

00:48:05.988 --> 00:48:09.540
When she saw that person, he was very familiar.

00:48:09.600 --> 00:48:11.358
It was her brother.

00:48:11.418 --> 00:48:13.344
He ran into the woods.

00:48:13.404 --> 00:48:15.116
The girl ran after him.

00:48:15.176 --> 00:48:18.210
They both carried fire so they could see in the dark.

00:48:18.270 --> 00:48:20.382
The smoke went into the air.

00:48:20.442 --> 00:48:22.504
As they ran, they grew.

00:48:22.564 --> 00:48:24.426
They became huge.

00:48:24.486 --> 00:48:26.508
Then they went into space.

00:48:26.568 --> 00:48:30.152
When the girl's fire went out, she hung in the sky.

00:48:30.212 --> 00:48:33.986
She became the moon, and her brother became the sun.

00:48:34.046 --> 00:48:37.876
They chase each other forever.

00:48:37.936 --> 00:48:40.956
Unit 9.

00:48:41.016 --> 00:48:42.526
Word List.

00:48:42.586 --> 00:48:44.197
Against.

00:48:44.258 --> 00:48:49.130
To be against something is to be touching it or opposed to it.

00:48:49.190 --> 00:48:52.852
They both leaned against the wall.

00:48:52.912 --> 00:48:54.994
Beach.

00:48:55.054 --> 00:48:59.166
The beach is a sandy or rocky place by the ocean.

00:48:59.226 --> 00:49:03.900
The little girl built a sand castle on the beach.

00:49:03.960 --> 00:49:06.070
Damage.

00:49:06.130 --> 00:49:08.938
To damage something is to break it.

00:49:08.998 --> 00:49:12.866
The car was damaged in the accident.

00:49:12.926 --> 00:49:15.098
Discover.

00:49:15.158 --> 00:49:18.870
To discover something is to find it for the first time.

00:49:18.930 --> 00:49:23.453
I discovered some new information in this book.

00:49:23.513 --> 00:49:25.714
Emotion.

00:49:25.774 --> 00:49:28.416
An emotion is how you feel.

00:49:28.476 --> 00:49:33.179
Anger is a common emotion that we all feel.

00:49:33.239 --> 00:49:35.280
Fix.

00:49:35.341 --> 00:49:38.370
To fix something is to make it work.

00:49:38.430 --> 00:49:43.729
My dad has many tools to help him fix broken things.

00:49:43.789 --> 00:49:45.790
Frank.

00:49:45.850 --> 00:49:49.301
If you are Frank, you are being very honest.

00:49:49.361 --> 00:49:53.994
The teacher had a frank discussion with their students.

00:49:54.054 --> 00:49:56.384
Identify.

00:49:56.444 --> 00:50:00.036
To identify something is to be able to name it.

00:50:00.096 --> 00:50:04.475
I use the file to identify his name.

00:50:04.535 --> 00:50:06.614
Island.

00:50:06.674 --> 00:50:10.006
An island is land in the middle of water.

00:50:10.067 --> 00:50:13.850
Japan is a group of islands.

00:50:13.910 --> 00:50:15.942
Ocean.

00:50:16.002 --> 00:50:20.295
The ocean is all of the salt water that surrounds land.

00:50:20.356 --> 00:50:24.208
The ocean can make powerful waves.

00:50:24.268 --> 00:50:26.420
Perhaps.

00:50:26.480 --> 00:50:30.374
Perhaps is used when you say that something could happen.

00:50:30.434 --> 00:50:34.556
Perhaps I will eat an apple for lunch.

00:50:34.616 --> 00:50:36.756
Pleasant.

00:50:36.816 --> 00:50:39.968
If something is pleasant, you enjoy it.

00:50:40.029 --> 00:50:44.531
The character had a pleasant look on its face.

00:50:44.592 --> 00:50:46.704
Prevent.

00:50:46.764 --> 00:50:50.226
To prevent something is to stop it from happening.

00:50:50.286 --> 00:50:54.989
The handcuffs prevented me from moving my hands.

00:50:55.049 --> 00:50:57.070
Rock.

00:50:57.130 --> 00:51:00.002
A rock is a hard thing in the dirt.

00:51:00.062 --> 00:51:04.007
I stacked rocks on top of one another.

00:51:04.068 --> 00:51:06.110
Save.

00:51:06.170 --> 00:51:09.744
To save something is to keep it from being hurt.

00:51:09.804 --> 00:51:13.337
I want to help save the world.

00:51:13.397 --> 00:51:15.398
Step.

00:51:15.458 --> 00:51:18.080
To step is to walk.

00:51:18.140 --> 00:51:21.534
Be careful where you step.

00:51:21.594 --> 00:51:23.686
Still.

00:51:23.746 --> 00:51:28.170
Still is used when you say that a situation keeps going on.

00:51:28.230 --> 00:51:32.420
They are still waiting in line to get tickets.

00:51:32.480 --> 00:51:38.282
A taste is the flavor something makes in your mouth.

00:51:38.342 --> 00:51:41.894
The taste of the fruit was sweet.

00:51:41.955 --> 00:51:43.996
Throw.

00:51:44.056 --> 00:51:48.850
To throw something is to use your hand to make it go through the air.

00:51:48.910 --> 00:51:53.513
The pitcher can throw the baseball very fast.

00:51:53.573 --> 00:51:55.604
Wave.

00:51:55.665 --> 00:52:00.246
A wave is a line of water that moves higher than the rest of the water.

00:52:00.306 --> 00:52:05.666
The water was filled with large blue waves.

00:52:05.726 --> 00:52:12.738
The Starfish Last summer, I took a trip to an island.

00:52:12.799 --> 00:52:14.729
I had a lot of fun.

00:52:14.789 --> 00:52:18.610
I sat and watched the waves and listened to the ocean.

00:52:18.670 --> 00:52:21.141
I learned to identify birds.

00:52:21.201 --> 00:52:25.642
I discovered pretty things and enjoyed the taste of new foods.

00:52:25.702 --> 00:52:27.943
It was a very nice time.

00:52:28.003 --> 00:52:31.674
One evening I took a pleasant walk by the ocean.

00:52:31.734 --> 00:52:36.146
When the waves came in, many starfish fell on the beach.

00:52:36.206 --> 00:52:40.547
Some starfish went back into the water, and they were safe.

00:52:40.608 --> 00:52:47.270
But other starfish were still on the sand, and they would die if they did not get into the water.

00:52:47.330 --> 00:52:50.552
There were many starfish on the beach that night.

00:52:50.612 --> 00:52:54.845
It made me sad, but I knew I could not fix the problem.

00:52:54.905 --> 00:52:58.728
I stepped very carefully, so I did not damage them.

00:52:58.788 --> 00:53:01.280
Then I saw little girl.

00:53:01.340 --> 00:53:04.282
She was also sad about the starfish.

00:53:04.342 --> 00:53:07.674
She wanted to prevent all of them from dying.

00:53:07.734 --> 00:53:10.824
She asked me if I could perhaps help her.

00:53:10.884 --> 00:53:14.916
To be frank, I don't think we can do anything, I said.

00:53:14.976 --> 00:53:17.428
The little girl started to cry.

00:53:17.488 --> 00:53:21.089
She sat back against a rock and thought for a while.

00:53:21.149 --> 00:53:24.010
Finally, the emotion was gone.

00:53:24.070 --> 00:53:26.584
She stopped crying and stood up.

00:53:26.644 --> 00:53:30.692
Then she picked up a starfish and threw it into the water.

00:53:30.752 --> 00:53:32.144
What are you doing?

00:53:32.204 --> 00:53:33.096
I asked her.

00:53:33.156 --> 00:53:34.968
But she did not answer me.

00:53:35.028 --> 00:53:38.282
She just threw as many starfish as she could.

00:53:38.342 --> 00:53:41.506
You cannot save all of them, I said.

00:53:41.566 --> 00:53:43.458
She stopped to look at me.

00:53:43.518 --> 00:53:46.892
No, I cannot save them all," she replied.

00:53:46.952 --> 00:53:52.156
Then she picked up a very big starfish and said, but I can save this one.

00:53:52.216 --> 00:53:59.662
And then she smiled and threw the starfish as far as she could into the ocean.

00:53:59.722 --> 00:54:02.584
Unit 10.

00:54:02.644 --> 00:54:04.165
Word List.

00:54:04.226 --> 00:54:05.926
Benefit.

00:54:05.986 --> 00:54:08.699
A benefit is a good thing.

00:54:08.759 --> 00:54:13.466
Being able to fly is a good benefit to burns.

00:54:13.526 --> 00:54:15.610
Certain.

00:54:15.670 --> 00:54:19.613
If you are certain about something, you know it is true.

00:54:19.673 --> 00:54:23.746
I am certain that zebras have stripes.

00:54:23.806 --> 00:54:25.916
Chance.

00:54:25.976 --> 00:54:29.468
A chance is an opportunity to do something.

00:54:29.529 --> 00:54:34.652
I had a chance to see the Roman Colosseum last summer.

00:54:34.712 --> 00:54:36.773
Effect.

00:54:36.833 --> 00:54:40.425
An effect is a change made by something else.

00:54:40.485 --> 00:54:45.498
The medicine had a good effect on the boy.

00:54:45.558 --> 00:54:51.120
If something is essential, it is very important and necessary.

00:54:51.180 --> 00:54:55.902
It is essential to have oxygen when you scuba dive.

00:54:55.962 --> 00:54:57.922
Far.

00:54:57.982 --> 00:55:01.324
If something is far, it is not close.

00:55:01.384 --> 00:55:06.685
It's far going from the east coast to the west coast of America.

00:55:06.746 --> 00:55:08.816
Focus.

00:55:08.876 --> 00:55:13.476
To focus on something is to think about it and pay attention to it.

00:55:13.536 --> 00:55:18.586
My mom always helps me to focus on my schoolwork.

00:55:18.647 --> 00:55:20.728
Function.

00:55:20.788 --> 00:55:23.970
The function of something is what it does.

00:55:24.030 --> 00:55:29.373
The function of a flashlight is to help you see in the dark.

00:55:29.434 --> 00:55:31.494
Grass.

00:55:31.554 --> 00:55:34.986
Grass is the green leaves that cover the ground.

00:55:35.046 --> 00:55:38.799
The grass looks so soft and green.

00:55:38.859 --> 00:55:40.940
Guard.

00:55:41.000 --> 00:55:43.988
To guard something is to take care of it.

00:55:44.048 --> 00:55:48.606
The police officer will guard us from any harm.

00:55:48.666 --> 00:55:53.968
Image The image of something is a picture of it.

00:55:54.028 --> 00:55:58.259
The image of her eye was very clear.

00:55:58.320 --> 00:56:03.862
Immediate If something is immediate, it happens quickly.

00:56:03.922 --> 00:56:08.624
An immediate response came from the pizza place.

00:56:08.685 --> 00:56:14.865
Primary If something is primary, it is the most important thing.

00:56:14.925 --> 00:56:18.924
His primary thoughts are about money.

00:56:18.984 --> 00:56:21.055
Proud.

00:56:21.115 --> 00:56:25.407
If someone feels proud, they are happy about what they have done.

00:56:25.467 --> 00:56:30.108
She is proud of the picture she drew of her house.

00:56:30.168 --> 00:56:32.280
Remain.

00:56:32.340 --> 00:56:35.500
To remain somewhere is to stay there.

00:56:35.560 --> 00:56:40.201
My sister had to remain home since she was sick.

00:56:40.262 --> 00:56:42.242
Rest.

00:56:42.302 --> 00:56:47.395
To rest is to stop being active while the body gets back at strength.

00:56:47.455 --> 00:56:51.257
I rested on the couch after work.

00:56:51.318 --> 00:56:53.439
Separate.

00:56:53.499 --> 00:56:57.042
If two things are separate, they are not together.

00:56:57.102 --> 00:57:02.705
New York and Los Angeles are in two separate parts of America.

00:57:02.765 --> 00:57:04.786
Site.

00:57:04.846 --> 00:57:07.198
A site is a place.

00:57:07.258 --> 00:57:11.349
We found the perfect site for our picnic.

00:57:11.409 --> 00:57:19.064
A tail is a part of an animal's body, sticking out from its rear or back.

00:57:19.124 --> 00:57:23.458
Our dog wags its tail when it's happy.

00:57:23.518 --> 00:57:25.540
Trouble.

00:57:25.600 --> 00:57:28.212
Trouble is a problem or a difficulty.

00:57:28.232 --> 00:57:33.326
I have trouble working with my boss.

00:57:33.386 --> 00:57:36.847
The first peacock.

00:57:36.907 --> 00:57:39.716
Argos lived in ancient Greece.

00:57:39.776 --> 00:57:42.596
He was a husband and a proud father.

00:57:42.656 --> 00:57:45.547
He worked hard and did well at his job.

00:57:45.607 --> 00:57:48.448
But one thing about him wasn't normal.

00:57:48.508 --> 00:57:51.108
He was born with 100 eyes.

00:57:51.168 --> 00:57:54.989
Having many eyes was usually a benefit to him.

00:57:55.049 --> 00:57:57.920
He had a chance to see many things.

00:57:57.980 --> 00:58:03.211
Also, since he had so many eyes, he was very good at guarding things.

00:58:03.271 --> 00:58:07.132
While sleeping, he only rested a few eyes at a time.

00:58:07.192 --> 00:58:08.963
The other stayed awake.

00:58:09.023 --> 00:58:12.014
He worked for Hera, a great goddess.

00:58:12.074 --> 00:58:15.414
His primary function was to guard a special cow.

00:58:15.474 --> 00:58:17.955
The cow was very important to Hera.

00:58:18.015 --> 00:58:19.796
It was her favorite pet.

00:58:19.856 --> 00:58:23.576
The most essential part of his job was to keep the cow alone.

00:58:23.636 --> 00:58:28.778
It had to be kept separate from all the other cows and far away from people.

00:58:28.838 --> 00:58:31.598
This was an easy job for Argos.

00:58:31.658 --> 00:58:34.350
The cow just ate grass all day.

00:58:34.410 --> 00:58:37.070
But the god Zeus wanted the cow.

00:58:37.130 --> 00:58:39.831
He wanted to take it away from Hera.

00:58:39.891 --> 00:58:41.701
He had a plan.

00:58:41.762 --> 00:58:44.612
He found a great music player.

00:58:44.672 --> 00:58:48.484
He asked the man to play a beautiful song for Argos.

00:58:48.544 --> 00:58:51.928
Zeus was certain Argos would go to sleep.

00:58:51.988 --> 00:58:54.750
The song had an immediate effect.

00:58:54.810 --> 00:58:57.432
Argos couldn't focus on his job.

00:58:57.493 --> 00:58:59.314
He fell asleep.

00:58:59.375 --> 00:59:02.466
Zeus saw this, and he took the cow.

00:59:02.526 --> 00:59:05.510
Hera was very angry with Argos.

00:59:05.570 --> 00:59:07.922
She turned him into a peacock.

00:59:07.982 --> 00:59:10.934
She put his many eyes on his tail.

00:59:10.994 --> 00:59:13.400
Argos was very sad.

00:59:13.460 --> 00:59:17.055
Zeus saw how much trouble he had caused Argos.

00:59:17.115 --> 00:59:19.115
He made another plan.

00:59:19.175 --> 00:59:22.106
He turned Argos into a group of stars.

00:59:22.166 --> 00:59:25.617
He wanted Argos to remain in the sky forever.

00:59:25.677 --> 00:59:32.058
Even today, Argos' image remains there, above the site where all his problems began.

00:59:32.118 --> 00:59:36.356
We can still see him in the night sky.

00:59:36.417 --> 00:59:40.926
Unit 11, word list.

00:59:40.986 --> 00:59:42.656
Anymore.

00:59:42.716 --> 00:59:45.388
Anymore means any longer.

00:59:45.448 --> 00:59:48.290
Her old pants don't fit her anymore.

00:59:48.310 --> 00:59:51.502
Asleep.

00:59:51.562 --> 00:59:54.944
When a person is asleep, they are not awake.

00:59:55.004 --> 00:59:58.976
The baby has been asleep for hours.

00:59:59.036 --> 01:00:01.178
Berry.

01:00:01.238 --> 01:00:06.252
A berry is a small round fruit that grows on certain plants and trees.

01:00:06.312 --> 01:00:09.665
The berry looked delicious.

01:00:09.725 --> 01:00:11.806
Collect.

01:00:11.866 --> 01:00:16.300
To collect things is to group them together all in one place.

01:00:16.360 --> 01:00:20.334
I collected shells when I was younger.

01:00:20.394 --> 01:00:22.556
Compete.

01:00:22.616 --> 01:00:26.338
To compete is to try to be better than someone.

01:00:26.398 --> 01:00:30.632
He will compete with very good athletes.

01:00:30.692 --> 01:00:33.064
Conversation.

01:00:33.124 --> 01:00:36.396
A conversation is a talk between people.

01:00:36.456 --> 01:00:41.197
There were two conversations going on at once.

01:00:41.258 --> 01:00:46.310
Creature A creature is any living thing.

01:00:46.370 --> 01:00:52.024
The creature we saw today was either a dolphin or a porpoise.

01:00:52.084 --> 01:00:56.936
Decision A decision is a choice.

01:00:56.996 --> 01:01:00.174
He made the wrong decision.

01:01:00.234 --> 01:01:02.322
Either.

01:01:02.382 --> 01:01:08.004
Either is used with ore to say there are two or more possibilities.

01:01:08.065 --> 01:01:13.668
You can choose to be either white or black when you play chess.

01:01:13.728 --> 01:01:15.828
Forest.

01:01:15.888 --> 01:01:19.840
A forest is a place with lots of trees and animals.

01:01:19.900 --> 01:01:23.732
I love to go walking in the forest.

01:01:23.792 --> 01:01:25.893
Ground.

01:01:25.954 --> 01:01:29.756
The ground is the top part of the earth that we walk on.

01:01:29.816 --> 01:01:34.690
The ground under our feet was dry and brown.

01:01:34.750 --> 01:01:36.922
Introduce.

01:01:36.982 --> 01:01:41.234
To introduce someone or something is to say who they are.

01:01:41.294 --> 01:01:46.348
I introduce myself to our newest coworker today.

01:01:46.408 --> 01:01:48.469
Mary.

01:01:48.530 --> 01:01:52.442
To marry is to legally become husband and wife.

01:01:52.502 --> 01:01:57.068
Rose and Henry were married and they lived happily.

01:01:57.128 --> 01:01:59.230
Prepare.

01:01:59.290 --> 01:02:02.442
To prepare is to get ready for something.

01:02:02.502 --> 01:02:06.306
I prepared my speech to the class.

01:02:06.366 --> 01:02:08.426
Sale.

01:02:08.486 --> 01:02:12.009
To sail is to move a boat on the water.

01:02:12.070 --> 01:02:16.102
I love to sail my boat on the lake.

01:02:16.162 --> 01:02:18.284
Serious.

01:02:18.344 --> 01:02:22.626
When something is serious, it is bad or unsafe.

01:02:22.686 --> 01:02:26.459
The accident was very serious.

01:02:26.519 --> 01:02:28.680
Spend.

01:02:28.741 --> 01:02:33.694
To spend is to use time doing something or being somewhere.

01:02:33.754 --> 01:02:37.786
I like to spend my free time fishing.

01:02:37.846 --> 01:02:40.027
Strange.

01:02:40.087 --> 01:02:43.448
When something is strange, it is not normal.

01:02:43.509 --> 01:02:49.352
Joe had a strange look on his face after he saw what happened.

01:02:49.412 --> 01:02:51.384
Truth.

01:02:51.444 --> 01:02:55.084
The truth is a fact or something that is right.

01:02:55.144 --> 01:03:00.167
He was telling the truth about seeing a large green snake.

01:03:00.227 --> 01:03:02.178
Wake.

01:03:02.239 --> 01:03:05.542
To wake is to not be sleeping anymore.

01:03:05.602 --> 01:03:11.146
He is always full of energy when he wakes in the morning.

01:03:11.206 --> 01:03:15.426
Princess Rose and the creature.

01:03:15.486 --> 01:03:19.254
There was once a beautiful princess named Rose.

01:03:19.314 --> 01:03:24.208
Her mother, the queen, however, was not as beautiful as the princess.

01:03:24.268 --> 01:03:29.804
The queen felt bad that she was not the most beautiful woman in the kingdom anymore.

01:03:29.864 --> 01:03:32.996
She was tired of competing with her daughter.

01:03:33.056 --> 01:03:35.158
She made a decision.

01:03:35.218 --> 01:03:37.900
She prepared a drink for the princess.

01:03:37.960 --> 01:03:41.322
After the princess drank it, she fell asleep.

01:03:41.382 --> 01:03:44.435
Then the queen took the princess to the forest.

01:03:44.495 --> 01:03:46.357
She left the princess there.

01:03:46.417 --> 01:03:48.999
It was a very serious thing to do.

01:03:49.059 --> 01:03:53.943
Either she will be killed by animals or she will get lost in the forest.

01:03:54.003 --> 01:03:56.915
The queen thought the princess had a dream.

01:03:56.975 --> 01:04:00.758
She dreamed about a man with brown hair and brown eyes.

01:04:00.818 --> 01:04:02.840
It was the man she would marry.

01:04:02.900 --> 01:04:04.492
The princess woke up.

01:04:04.552 --> 01:04:07.575
She saw a strange creature on the ground.

01:04:07.635 --> 01:04:11.360
It looked like a man, but he was hairy and green.

01:04:11.420 --> 01:04:15.074
He had horns on his head and a pig's nose.

01:04:15.134 --> 01:04:18.727
The creature said, did I scare you?

01:04:18.787 --> 01:04:19.917
I hope not.

01:04:19.977 --> 01:04:22.118
Let me introduce myself.

01:04:22.178 --> 01:04:23.398
I am Henry.

01:04:23.458 --> 01:04:25.079
I am not scared.

01:04:25.139 --> 01:04:28.300
To tell you the truth, I think you are cute."

01:04:28.360 --> 01:04:29.410
said Rose.

01:04:29.470 --> 01:04:32.181
Rose and Henry spent the day together.

01:04:32.241 --> 01:04:36.112
They collected berries, caught fish, and had lunch.

01:04:36.172 --> 01:04:40.654
They had a very good day filled with nice conversations.

01:04:40.714 --> 01:04:44.728
Rose, I have to go home," said Henry.

01:04:44.788 --> 01:04:47.090
My ship will sail home soon.

01:04:47.150 --> 01:04:50.074
I can't leave you here in the forest alone.

01:04:50.134 --> 01:04:51.936
Will you come with me?"

01:04:51.996 --> 01:04:54.038
Rose was very happy.

01:04:54.098 --> 01:04:57.482
She gave Henry a kiss right on his pig nose.

01:04:57.542 --> 01:05:01.333
As soon as she kissed Henry, he began to change.

01:05:01.394 --> 01:05:04.345
His pig nose turned into a man's nose.

01:05:04.405 --> 01:05:07.416
His horns and green hair went away.

01:05:07.476 --> 01:05:11.718
Standing in front of her was the man Rose had dreamt about.

01:05:11.778 --> 01:05:15.460
Rose and Henry were married, and they lived happily.

01:05:15.480 --> 01:05:20.492
Unit 12.

01:05:20.552 --> 01:05:22.012
Word List.

01:05:22.072 --> 01:05:23.752
Alone.

01:05:23.812 --> 01:05:28.042
If someone is alone, they are not with another person.

01:05:28.102 --> 01:05:31.954
The boy wanted to be alone to think.

01:05:32.014 --> 01:05:34.176
Apartment.

01:05:34.236 --> 01:05:38.548
An apartment is a set of rooms in a building where people live.

01:05:38.608 --> 01:05:42.360
She has a nice apartment in the city.

01:05:42.420 --> 01:05:44.542
Article.

01:05:44.602 --> 01:05:48.884
An article is a story in a newspaper or magazine.

01:05:48.944 --> 01:05:54.198
Did you read the article in the newspaper about the soccer game?

01:05:54.258 --> 01:05:56.312
artist.

01:05:56.372 --> 01:06:01.426
An artist is a person who paints, draws, or makes sculptures.

01:06:01.486 --> 01:06:05.389
He went to Paris to become an artist.

01:06:05.449 --> 01:06:07.661
Attitude.

01:06:07.722 --> 01:06:11.674
Someone's attitude is the way they feel and think.

01:06:11.734 --> 01:06:14.076
John has a bad attitude.

01:06:14.136 --> 01:06:16.548
He's always angry.

01:06:16.609 --> 01:06:18.720
Compare.

01:06:18.780 --> 01:06:23.856
To compare means to say how two things are the same and different.

01:06:23.916 --> 01:06:29.730
If you compare cats and dogs, you'll see that they're both good pets.

01:06:29.790 --> 01:06:35.674
Judge To judge something is to say if it is good or bad.

01:06:35.734 --> 01:06:40.866
The boy was going to judge how his mother's turkey tasted.

01:06:40.926 --> 01:06:48.531
Magazine A magazine is a regular publication with news, stories and articles.

01:06:48.592 --> 01:06:52.257
She likes to read fashion magazines.

01:06:52.317 --> 01:06:57.793
Material A material is what is used to make something.

01:06:57.853 --> 01:07:02.496
Brick is a good material for building houses.

01:07:02.556 --> 01:07:10.048
Meal A meal is a time when food is eaten, like breakfast, lunch or dinner.

01:07:10.109 --> 01:07:15.802
Breakfast is my favorite meal because I enjoy breakfast foods.

01:07:15.862 --> 01:07:20.832
Method A method is the way to do something.

01:07:20.892 --> 01:07:27.281
One method to remember things is to tie a string around your finger.

01:07:27.341 --> 01:07:29.451
Neighbor.

01:07:29.512 --> 01:07:32.532
A neighbor is a person who lives near you.

01:07:32.592 --> 01:07:36.963
I like my neighbor because he's very friendly.

01:07:37.023 --> 01:07:39.273
Professional.

01:07:39.333 --> 01:07:44.464
If something is professional, it deals with work that uses special skills.

01:07:44.524 --> 01:07:50.515
If you want to be a pilot, you must have professional training.

01:07:50.575 --> 01:07:55.786
A profit is the extra money you make when you sell something.

01:07:55.846 --> 01:08:00.668
I made a small profit from selling my old clothes.

01:08:00.728 --> 01:08:02.790
Quality.

01:08:02.850 --> 01:08:05.901
The quality of something is how good it is.

01:08:05.961 --> 01:08:10.302
The quality of his car is very good.

01:08:10.362 --> 01:08:12.274
Shape.

01:08:12.334 --> 01:08:16.336
A shape is a simple form like a square or circle.

01:08:16.395 --> 01:08:20.132
The triangle is my favorite shape.

01:08:20.192 --> 01:08:22.228
Space.

01:08:22.288 --> 01:08:25.120
A space is an empty area.

01:08:25.180 --> 01:08:29.722
I don't have much space for things in my small house.

01:08:29.782 --> 01:08:31.873
Stairs.

01:08:31.934 --> 01:08:35.955
Stairs are the things that are used to go up in a building.

01:08:36.015 --> 01:08:40.138
You can take the stairs to the second floor.

01:08:40.198 --> 01:08:42.298
Symbol.

01:08:42.359 --> 01:08:45.970
A symbol is a thing that stands for something else.

01:08:46.030 --> 01:08:50.962
This symbol tells us that we cannot smoke in this area.

01:08:51.022 --> 01:08:57.185
Then, if someone or something is thin, they are not fat.

01:08:57.245 --> 01:09:02.346
The man was thin because he didn't eat much.

01:09:02.406 --> 01:09:09.975
The Crazy Artist Friedhofer was the best artist in the world.

01:09:10.034 --> 01:09:11.765
Everyone loved him.

01:09:11.825 --> 01:09:15.066
The quality of his paintings was very high.

01:09:15.127 --> 01:09:18.098
He always used the best materials.

01:09:18.158 --> 01:09:20.959
He made a big profit from his paintings.

01:09:21.019 --> 01:09:24.120
He had delicious meals with his rich neighbors.

01:09:24.181 --> 01:09:26.021
He taught art classes.

01:09:26.081 --> 01:09:27.752
Life was good.

01:09:27.812 --> 01:09:30.143
Then his attitude changed.

01:09:30.203 --> 01:09:32.934
He stopped selling paintings and teaching.

01:09:32.994 --> 01:09:35.398
He tried a new method of painting.

01:09:35.457 --> 01:09:38.442
He stayed alone in his apartment all day.

01:09:38.501 --> 01:09:42.195
He worked all day and all night, rarely eating.

01:09:42.254 --> 01:09:48.799
Soon, Friedhofer became very thin, but he kept working on the same paintings for many years.

01:09:48.859 --> 01:09:51.110
He worked as hard as he could.

01:09:51.170 --> 01:09:53.972
Finally, he finished the painting.

01:09:54.033 --> 01:09:57.674
He was very happy and invited other artists to see it.

01:09:57.735 --> 01:10:00.616
I want your professional opinion, he said.

01:10:00.676 --> 01:10:04.489
He wanted them to judge it and compare it to other paintings.

01:10:04.549 --> 01:10:09.052
Everyone was very excited as they went up the stairs to his apartment.

01:10:09.112 --> 01:10:14.326
Friedhofer was excited to show his painting, and the artists were excited to see it.

01:10:14.386 --> 01:10:17.108
They'll love it, he thought.

01:10:17.168 --> 01:10:19.561
But, they did not.

01:10:19.621 --> 01:10:22.244
They were surprised by his painting.

01:10:22.304 --> 01:10:24.616
There was no white anywhere.

01:10:24.676 --> 01:10:28.557
Friedhofer filled the whole painting with lines and colors.

01:10:28.617 --> 01:10:31.446
There was no space for a normal picture.

01:10:31.506 --> 01:10:33.817
It was full of strange shapes.

01:10:33.877 --> 01:10:36.558
It looked bad to the other artists.

01:10:36.618 --> 01:10:40.110
He used symbols and they didn't understand them.

01:10:40.170 --> 01:10:42.261
They thought it was terrible.

01:10:42.321 --> 01:10:44.782
Why did you paint this strange picture?

01:10:44.842 --> 01:10:46.023
Someone asked.

01:10:46.083 --> 01:10:48.311
They didn't understand its beauty.

01:10:48.371 --> 01:10:52.420
But after some time, many people began to like his painting.

01:10:52.480 --> 01:10:55.310
People wrote articles about it in magazines.

01:10:55.370 --> 01:10:57.392
They said it was his best work.

01:10:57.452 --> 01:10:59.612
They loved his strange symbols.

01:10:59.672 --> 01:11:01.713
They loved his strange colors.

01:11:01.773 --> 01:11:07.956
Friedhofer's painting reminded everyone that just because something was new, didn't mean that it was bad.

01:11:08.016 --> 01:11:15.795
He also helped them to realize that sometimes it takes people a little time to understand great things.

01:11:15.855 --> 01:11:18.953
Unit 13.

01:11:19.013 --> 01:11:20.494
Word list.

01:11:20.554 --> 01:11:22.165
Blood.

01:11:22.225 --> 01:11:25.227
Blood is the red liquid in your body.

01:11:25.287 --> 01:11:29.810
I cut my finger and got blood on my shirt.

01:11:29.870 --> 01:11:31.921
Burn.

01:11:31.982 --> 01:11:35.264
To burn something is to set it on fire.

01:11:35.323 --> 01:11:39.056
I burn some wood in the campfire.

01:11:39.116 --> 01:11:41.158
Cell.

01:11:41.218 --> 01:11:45.305
A cell is a small room where a person is locked in.

01:11:45.365 --> 01:11:51.264
The jail cell was very small.

01:11:51.324 --> 01:11:54.636
To contain something is to have it inside.

01:11:54.696 --> 01:11:58.148
The mailbox contained a letter.

01:11:58.208 --> 01:12:00.280
Correct.

01:12:00.340 --> 01:12:02.992
To be correct is to be right.

01:12:03.052 --> 01:12:07.264
All of my answers on the test were correct.

01:12:07.324 --> 01:12:09.356
Crop.

01:12:09.416 --> 01:12:12.702
A crop is food that a farmer grows.

01:12:12.762 --> 01:12:16.946
Wheat is a crop that is made into bread.

01:12:17.006 --> 01:12:23.148
Demand To demand something is to say strongly that you want it.

01:12:23.207 --> 01:12:27.318
The workers demanded to be paid more money.

01:12:27.378 --> 01:12:32.290
Equal To be equal is to be the same.

01:12:32.350 --> 01:12:36.211
Both students are equal in age.

01:12:36.271 --> 01:12:40.910
Feed To feed is to give food.

01:12:40.970 --> 01:12:45.352
Mother feeds my baby brother every day.

01:12:45.412 --> 01:12:46.783
Hole.

01:12:46.803 --> 01:12:50.376
A hole is an opening in something.

01:12:50.436 --> 01:12:55.188
The man was going to jump into the hole in the ice.

01:12:55.248 --> 01:12:57.440
Increase.

01:12:57.500 --> 01:13:01.302
To increase something is to make it larger or more.

01:13:01.362 --> 01:13:06.166
They've increased the price of gas by 15 cents.

01:13:06.226 --> 01:13:08.338
Lord.

01:13:08.398 --> 01:13:12.699
Long ago, a Lord was a man in charge of a town.

01:13:12.759 --> 01:13:16.750
The Lord of the town was not kind.

01:13:16.811 --> 01:13:18.651
Oh.

01:13:18.711 --> 01:13:24.153
To owe is to have to pay or give back something received from another.

01:13:24.213 --> 01:13:28.764
I owed him twenty dollars, so I paid him back.

01:13:28.824 --> 01:13:30.995
Position.

01:13:31.055 --> 01:13:34.256
A position is the way something is placed.

01:13:34.316 --> 01:13:37.892
How can you sit in that position?

01:13:37.952 --> 01:13:39.968
Raise.

01:13:40.028 --> 01:13:42.879
To raise something is to lift it up.

01:13:42.939 --> 01:13:47.500
We had to work together to raise the last piece.

01:13:47.560 --> 01:13:49.920
Responsible.

01:13:49.980 --> 01:13:53.971
If a person is responsible, they do the right things.

01:13:54.031 --> 01:13:58.202
I tried to be responsible and save money.

01:13:58.262 --> 01:14:00.212
Site.

01:14:00.272 --> 01:14:03.533
A site is something interesting to see.

01:14:03.593 --> 01:14:06.124
I saw the pyramids of Egypt.

01:14:06.184 --> 01:14:08.222
What a sight.

01:14:08.282 --> 01:14:10.370
Spot.

01:14:10.430 --> 01:14:13.702
A spot is a place where something happens.

01:14:13.762 --> 01:14:17.864
The kitchen is a good spot to eat meals.

01:14:17.924 --> 01:14:20.075
Structure.

01:14:20.135 --> 01:14:22.456
A structure is a building.

01:14:22.516 --> 01:14:27.218
They just built a beautiful new structure downtown.

01:14:27.278 --> 01:14:29.279
Whole.

01:14:29.339 --> 01:14:32.010
Whole means all of something.

01:14:32.070 --> 01:14:34.061
I ate the whole pie.

01:14:34.121 --> 01:14:37.272
We don't have any more.

01:14:37.332 --> 01:14:41.236
The Farmer and the Cats.

01:14:41.296 --> 01:14:46.722
Arthur was a responsible farmer, and Maria was a nice lady.

01:14:46.782 --> 01:14:48.514
But they were poor.

01:14:48.574 --> 01:14:51.635
They owed the town lord money for their land.

01:14:51.695 --> 01:14:54.176
One summer, their farm burned.

01:14:54.236 --> 01:14:58.656
One structure caught fire, and most of the animals ran away.

01:14:58.716 --> 01:15:00.717
Only the cat stayed.

01:15:00.777 --> 01:15:05.758
So Arthur and Maria had to bring in their crops without an animal's help.

01:15:05.818 --> 01:15:09.129
On a fall day, the Lord demanded his money.

01:15:09.189 --> 01:15:13.616
Arthur asked if the Lord could wait until he brought in his crops.

01:15:13.676 --> 01:15:15.493
The Lord was angry.

01:15:15.553 --> 01:15:20.284
He raised his hands high and yelled, Pay me by the end of the week.

01:15:20.344 --> 01:15:24.105
If you don't, I will increase the money you have to pay.

01:15:24.165 --> 01:15:27.026
I might put you in a jail cell.

01:15:27.086 --> 01:15:31.476
So Arthur and Maria worked until there was blood on their hands.

01:15:31.536 --> 01:15:35.017
They finished four lines of corn and went to bed.

01:15:35.077 --> 01:15:38.328
But the next morning, eight lines were finished.

01:15:38.388 --> 01:15:41.869
Maria, didn't we stop in this spot here?"

01:15:41.929 --> 01:15:43.160
Arthur asked.

01:15:43.220 --> 01:15:49.552
Yes, that is correct, and the tools were in a different position till Maria said.

01:15:49.612 --> 01:15:51.973
They were surprised and happy.

01:15:52.033 --> 01:15:55.694
That day they worked hard and finished five lines.

01:15:55.754 --> 01:15:58.815
But in the morning, ten lines were done.

01:15:58.875 --> 01:16:01.526
Each day, they did a lot of work.

01:16:01.586 --> 01:16:05.498
Each night, someone else did an equal amount of work.

01:16:05.558 --> 01:16:08.490
In a week, the whole field was finished.

01:16:08.550 --> 01:16:13.102
Tomorrow, I will sell the crops and pay the Lord," Arthur said.

01:16:13.162 --> 01:16:15.913
But that morning, the crops were gone.

01:16:15.973 --> 01:16:18.584
A bank was in the middle of the field.

01:16:18.644 --> 01:16:20.135
It contained money.

01:16:20.195 --> 01:16:23.477
Maria, let's see who has helped this work.

01:16:23.537 --> 01:16:27.220
Through a hole in the wall, they saw a funny sight.

01:16:27.280 --> 01:16:30.882
The cats were dancing in the field and eating corn.

01:16:30.942 --> 01:16:33.555
Now Arthur knew what had happened.

01:16:33.615 --> 01:16:35.726
The cats had worked at night.

01:16:35.786 --> 01:16:43.012
After that, Arthur was very nice to his cats and fed them lots of corn.

01:16:43.072 --> 01:16:46.225
Unit 14.

01:16:46.285 --> 01:16:52.766
Word List Coach A coach is a person who teaches sports.

01:16:52.826 --> 01:16:57.104
My coach gets very excited during games.

01:16:57.164 --> 01:16:59.324
Control.

01:16:59.384 --> 01:17:03.036
To control something is to make it do what you want.

01:17:03.096 --> 01:17:07.528
To control the TV, just push the buttons.

01:17:07.588 --> 01:17:09.869
Description.

01:17:09.928 --> 01:17:14.240
A description of someone or something says what they are like.

01:17:14.300 --> 01:17:19.713
I gave a description of the man with the gun and hat to the police.

01:17:19.773 --> 01:17:21.884
Direct.

01:17:21.945 --> 01:17:26.146
If something is direct, it goes straight between two places.

01:17:26.206 --> 01:17:30.738
The green path is a direct route to my house.

01:17:30.798 --> 01:17:32.968
Exam.

01:17:33.028 --> 01:17:35.440
An exam is a test.

01:17:35.500 --> 01:17:40.322
I did some practice questions for the math exam on the board.

01:17:40.382 --> 01:17:42.572
Example.

01:17:42.632 --> 01:17:46.824
An example of something is a thing that is typical of it.

01:17:46.884 --> 01:17:51.012
Cola is an example of a soft drink.

01:17:51.072 --> 01:17:58.053
Limit A limit is the largest or smallest amount of something that you allow.

01:17:58.113 --> 01:18:03.026
My mother put a limit on how much I could use the phone.

01:18:03.086 --> 01:18:08.438
Local If something is local, it is nearby.

01:18:08.498 --> 01:18:14.032
The local market in my neighborhood sells all the food we need.

01:18:14.092 --> 01:18:21.438
Magical Magical describes a quality that makes someone or something special.

01:18:21.498 --> 01:18:26.592
The fireworks made the night sky look so magical.

01:18:26.652 --> 01:18:32.404
Mail. Mail is letters and other things sent to people.

01:18:32.464 --> 01:18:37.956
I get a lot of mail because I have friends all over the world.

01:18:38.016 --> 01:18:43.307
Novel A novel is a book that tells a story.

01:18:43.367 --> 01:18:47.649
He wrote a great novel about ancient China.

01:18:47.709 --> 01:18:49.910
Outline.

01:18:49.970 --> 01:18:54.194
An outline is the plan for a story or essay.

01:18:54.254 --> 01:18:58.838
Before I wrote my essay, I made an outline.

01:18:58.898 --> 01:19:00.940
Poet.

01:19:01.000 --> 01:19:04.412
A poet is a person who writes poems.

01:19:04.472 --> 01:19:08.775
William Shakespeare was one of the greatest poets.

01:19:08.835 --> 01:19:10.776
Print.

01:19:10.836 --> 01:19:14.120
To print something is to put it onto paper.

01:19:14.180 --> 01:19:18.528
Make sure that you print your name clearly.

01:19:18.588 --> 01:19:24.476
Scene A scene is one part of a book or movie.

01:19:24.536 --> 01:19:29.658
A movie is made up of many short pieces or scenes.

01:19:29.718 --> 01:19:35.420
Sheet A sheet is a thin, flat piece of paper.

01:19:35.480 --> 01:19:40.754
I only needed a single sheet of paper to do my homework.

01:19:40.814 --> 01:19:47.472
Silly If someone or something is silly, they show a lack of thought.

01:19:47.532 --> 01:19:52.310
I made a silly mistake of dropping mom's vase.

01:19:52.370 --> 01:19:54.460
Store.

01:19:54.520 --> 01:19:57.862
A store is a place where you can buy things.

01:19:57.922 --> 01:20:02.234
I picked up a few things at the grocery store.

01:20:02.294 --> 01:20:04.315
Suffer.

01:20:04.375 --> 01:20:07.186
To suffer is to feel pain.

01:20:07.246 --> 01:20:11.068
Her headache made her suffer all day.

01:20:11.128 --> 01:20:13.418
Technology.

01:20:13.478 --> 01:20:17.372
Technology is new things made by using science.

01:20:17.432 --> 01:20:22.776
He loves technology, such as laptop computers.

01:20:22.836 --> 01:20:28.717
A Magical Book Sarah loved to read.

01:20:28.777 --> 01:20:31.287
She read novels and poems.

01:20:31.347 --> 01:20:34.638
She loved the beautiful descriptions and phrases.

01:20:34.698 --> 01:20:38.278
She loved reading work from poets and novelists.

01:20:38.338 --> 01:20:41.589
She didn't like video games or technology.

01:20:41.649 --> 01:20:45.890
She was on the basketball team, but she didn't like sports.

01:20:45.950 --> 01:20:48.490
Her parents made her play basketball.

01:20:48.550 --> 01:20:51.901
In fact, Sarah's parents made her do many things.

01:20:51.961 --> 01:20:54.492
But she didn't want to do those things.

01:20:54.552 --> 01:20:57.552
She just wanted to sit and read all day.

01:20:57.612 --> 01:21:00.843
One day, a small book came in the mail.

01:21:00.903 --> 01:21:02.523
It was for Sarah.

01:21:02.583 --> 01:21:04.823
The book looked very special.

01:21:04.883 --> 01:21:07.304
It was printed on sheets of gold.

01:21:07.364 --> 01:21:09.224
Sarah began to read.

01:21:09.284 --> 01:21:11.854
The outline of the story was simple.

01:21:11.914 --> 01:21:14.430
It was about a magical place.

01:21:14.490 --> 01:21:17.116
Strange things happened there.

01:21:17.177 --> 01:21:21.180
One example from the book was about a boy who could control people.

01:21:21.240 --> 01:21:25.074
In one scene, he made his friends tell funny jokes.

01:21:25.134 --> 01:21:27.006
Sarah loved the book.

01:21:27.066 --> 01:21:28.898
She read it all the time.

01:21:28.958 --> 01:21:31.220
Then something strange happened.

01:21:31.280 --> 01:21:34.312
The book gave Sarah a special power.

01:21:34.372 --> 01:21:36.946
She could control other people.

01:21:37.006 --> 01:21:39.442
She was like the boy in the book.

01:21:39.501 --> 01:21:43.647
During one exam, she made her friend tell silly jokes.

01:21:43.707 --> 01:21:45.690
Her friend got in trouble.

01:21:45.750 --> 01:21:49.594
After school, Sarah did not make a direct trip home.

01:21:49.654 --> 01:21:52.678
On the way, she went to the local store.

01:21:52.738 --> 01:21:55.142
She wanted to play more tricks on people.

01:21:55.202 --> 01:21:57.072
She caused problems.

01:21:57.132 --> 01:21:59.183
She made people fall down.

01:21:59.243 --> 01:22:01.363
She laughed and had fun.

01:22:01.423 --> 01:22:04.744
Finally, she laughed and started to walk home.

01:22:04.804 --> 01:22:06.714
Then she saw something.

01:22:06.774 --> 01:22:10.295
Her basketball coach was about to walk in front of a bus.

01:22:10.355 --> 01:22:12.355
He was looking the other way.

01:22:12.415 --> 01:22:14.236
She had to stop him.

01:22:14.296 --> 01:22:16.186
She used her power.

01:22:16.246 --> 01:22:17.906
She controlled him.

01:22:17.966 --> 01:22:20.224
She made him stop walking.

01:22:20.284 --> 01:22:22.601
Sarah learned something that day.

01:22:22.661 --> 01:22:25.913
It was better to help people than make them suffer.

01:22:25.973 --> 01:22:29.265
So she put a limit on how she used her power.

01:22:29.325 --> 01:22:32.658
She did not want to do bad things with it anymore.

01:22:32.718 --> 01:22:36.920
She only wanted to do good.

01:22:36.980 --> 01:22:40.082
Unit 15.

01:22:40.142 --> 01:22:47.126
Word List Across To go across something is to go to the other side of it.

01:22:47.186 --> 01:22:51.509
He walked across the board to the other side.

01:22:51.569 --> 01:22:53.640
Breathe.

01:22:53.700 --> 01:22:58.334
To breathe means to let air go in and out of your body.

01:22:58.394 --> 01:23:03.246
We need strong healthy lungs to help us breathe well.

01:23:03.306 --> 01:23:05.648
Characteristic.

01:23:05.708 --> 01:23:10.651
A characteristic is something that shows what a person or a thing is like.

01:23:10.710 --> 01:23:15.553
One characteristic of tigers is their black stripes.

01:23:15.613 --> 01:23:17.794
Consume.

01:23:17.854 --> 01:23:21.592
To consume something means to eat or drink it.

01:23:21.652 --> 01:23:25.710
Jack consumed a whole plate of spaghetti.

01:23:25.770 --> 01:23:27.791
Excite.

01:23:27.851 --> 01:23:31.863
To excite someone means to make them happy and interested.

01:23:31.923 --> 01:23:34.885
I heard about the school dance on Friday.

01:23:34.945 --> 01:23:37.246
This excited me.

01:23:37.306 --> 01:23:39.537
Extreme.

01:23:39.597 --> 01:23:44.740
If something is extreme, it is in a large amount or degree.

01:23:44.800 --> 01:23:49.768
His workout was so extreme that he was sweating heavily.

01:23:49.828 --> 01:23:51.693
Fear.

01:23:51.753 --> 01:23:54.834
Fear is the feeling of being afraid.

01:23:54.894 --> 01:23:58.684
I have a great fear of skateboarding.

01:23:58.744 --> 01:24:00.815
Fortunate.

01:24:00.875 --> 01:24:03.836
If you are fortunate, you are lucky.

01:24:03.896 --> 01:24:07.246
I was fortunate to get a seat.

01:24:07.306 --> 01:24:09.306
Happen.

01:24:09.366 --> 01:24:13.577
If someone happens to do something, they do it by chance.

01:24:13.637 --> 01:24:18.826
I happen to meet some new friends at school today.

01:24:18.886 --> 01:24:24.956
The length of something is how long it is from one end to the other.

01:24:25.016 --> 01:24:29.010
The length of the floor is 3 meters.

01:24:29.070 --> 01:24:31.162
Mistake.

01:24:31.222 --> 01:24:34.174
A mistake is something you do wrong.

01:24:34.234 --> 01:24:39.048
My boss always yells at me when I make a mistake.

01:24:39.108 --> 01:24:41.220
Observe.

01:24:41.280 --> 01:24:44.422
To observe something is to watch it.

01:24:44.482 --> 01:24:49.184
Ryan observed the sun rising over the mountains.

01:24:49.244 --> 01:24:51.544
Opportunity.

01:24:51.604 --> 01:24:55.236
An opportunity is a chance to do something.

01:24:55.296 --> 01:25:00.028
I had an opportunity to take pictures in the jungle.

01:25:00.088 --> 01:25:02.209
Prize.

01:25:02.269 --> 01:25:06.642
A prize is something of value that is given to the winner.

01:25:06.702 --> 01:25:12.004
I won a prize for getting the best grade on my science test.

01:25:12.064 --> 01:25:14.065
Race.

01:25:14.125 --> 01:25:18.223
A race is a contest to see who is the fastest.

01:25:18.283 --> 01:25:23.260
Paul is a fast runner, so he easily won the race.

01:25:23.320 --> 01:25:25.491
Realize.

01:25:25.551 --> 01:25:28.952
To realize is to suddenly understand.

01:25:29.012 --> 01:25:34.323
After I left my house, I realized that I left the light on.

01:25:34.383 --> 01:25:36.574
Respond.

01:25:36.634 --> 01:25:41.075
To respond is to give an answer to what someone else said.

01:25:41.135 --> 01:25:45.980
When the teacher asked the question, we all responded.

01:25:46.040 --> 01:25:48.064
Risk.

01:25:48.124 --> 01:25:51.726
A risk is a chance of something bad happening.

01:25:51.786 --> 01:25:55.997
I took a risk and climbed the snowy mountain.

01:25:56.057 --> 01:25:58.098
Wonder.

01:25:58.158 --> 01:26:02.770
To wonder is to ask yourself questions or have a need to know.

01:26:02.830 --> 01:26:07.731
The young mother wondered if she'd have a boy or a girl.

01:26:07.791 --> 01:26:09.772
Yet.

01:26:09.832 --> 01:26:14.080
Yet is used to say something has not happened up to now.

01:26:14.140 --> 01:26:16.042
We can't go out yet.

01:26:16.102 --> 01:26:19.062
We're still eating.

01:26:19.122 --> 01:26:26.336
The Big Race A dog saw a group of animals across the road.

01:26:26.396 --> 01:26:28.457
He walked over to meet them.

01:26:28.517 --> 01:26:29.948
What are you doing?"

01:26:30.008 --> 01:26:31.240
he asked them.

01:26:31.300 --> 01:26:37.284
I just sold them tickets to a race between the rabbit and the turtle, the duck responded.

01:26:37.344 --> 01:26:39.986
This news excited the dog.

01:26:40.046 --> 01:26:43.278
He felt fortunate that he happened to be there.

01:26:43.338 --> 01:26:46.661
I don't have anything to do today, the dog said.

01:26:46.721 --> 01:26:48.902
I want to buy a ticket too.

01:26:48.962 --> 01:26:51.913
The dogs sat down to observe the race.

01:26:51.973 --> 01:26:53.894
The race would be extreme.

01:26:53.954 --> 01:26:56.685
It would be many kilometers in length.

01:26:56.745 --> 01:27:00.116
The rabbit and the turtle stood next to each other.

01:27:00.176 --> 01:27:02.607
They waited for the race to start.

01:27:02.667 --> 01:27:07.188
The dog wondered why the turtle agreed to run against the rabbit.

01:27:07.248 --> 01:27:11.010
Being fast was not a characteristic of turtles.

01:27:11.070 --> 01:27:13.701
The rabbit was going to win easily.

01:27:13.761 --> 01:27:16.112
Suddenly, the race began.

01:27:16.172 --> 01:27:18.924
The rabbit ran extremely quickly.

01:27:18.984 --> 01:27:21.124
The turtle walked slowly.

01:27:21.184 --> 01:27:23.936
After a minute, the rabbit looked back.

01:27:23.996 --> 01:27:30.068
He saw that the turtle was far behind him and was breathing quickly because he was so tired.

01:27:30.128 --> 01:27:33.130
The rabbit smiled and slowed to a walk.

01:27:33.190 --> 01:27:37.783
A minute later, the rabbit said, I'm winning, so I'll take a rest.

01:27:37.843 --> 01:27:40.616
He sat and began to consume some grass.

01:27:40.676 --> 01:27:42.717
Then he let his eyes close.

01:27:42.777 --> 01:27:47.951
He wasn't the winner yet, but there was no risk of him losing the race.

01:27:48.011 --> 01:27:49.502
He went to sleep.

01:27:49.562 --> 01:27:52.734
Hours later, a loud sound woke him.

01:27:52.794 --> 01:27:56.576
All of the animals were yelling and looking at the field.

01:27:56.636 --> 01:27:59.258
He felt fear for the first time.

01:27:59.318 --> 01:28:02.199
The turtle was almost at the finish line.

01:28:02.259 --> 01:28:06.882
Now the rabbit realized his mistake, but the race was over.

01:28:06.942 --> 01:28:11.584
He gave the turtle an opportunity to win, and the turtle took it.

01:28:11.644 --> 01:28:14.236
The duck handed the turtle his prize.

01:28:14.296 --> 01:28:17.559
It was the happiest day of the turtle's life.

01:28:17.619 --> 01:28:20.022
The dog was happy for the turtle.

01:28:20.082 --> 01:28:27.629
He isn't fast, the dog thought, but he tried his best and did something great.

01:28:27.689 --> 01:28:30.932
Unit 16.

01:28:30.992 --> 01:28:32.564
Word list.

01:28:32.624 --> 01:28:34.296
Academy.

01:28:34.356 --> 01:28:37.749
An academy is a special type of school.

01:28:37.809 --> 01:28:42.857
There are many courses taught at the academy that I go to.

01:28:42.917 --> 01:28:44.982
Ancient.

01:28:45.041 --> 01:28:48.614
If something is ancient, it is very old.

01:28:48.674 --> 01:28:52.866
I want to see the ancient buildings in Rome.

01:28:52.925 --> 01:28:55.076
Board.

01:28:55.136 --> 01:28:58.098
A board is a flat piece of wood.

01:28:58.158 --> 01:29:02.350
The sign was made of a few wooden boards.

01:29:02.410 --> 01:29:04.622
Century.

01:29:04.682 --> 01:29:07.792
A century is 100 years.

01:29:07.852 --> 01:29:13.238
Our company is celebrating a century of business in London.

01:29:13.298 --> 01:29:20.943
Clue A clue is a fact or object that helps solve a mystery or crime.

01:29:21.003 --> 01:29:25.374
The detective found some clues on the sidewalk.

01:29:25.434 --> 01:29:31.978
Concert A concert is an event where you listen to people play music.

01:29:32.038 --> 01:29:34.959
I enjoyed the concert last night.

01:29:35.019 --> 01:29:37.750
The band was very good.

01:29:37.811 --> 01:29:44.724
County A county is the largest political division of a state in the US.

01:29:44.784 --> 01:29:49.396
He wanted to represent the citizens of his county.

01:29:49.456 --> 01:29:55.988
Dictionary A dictionary is a book that tells you what words mean.

01:29:56.048 --> 01:30:00.350
I use the dictionary to learn new words.

01:30:00.410 --> 01:30:05.391
Exist To exist is to be real.

01:30:05.451 --> 01:30:09.963
Do you really think that unicorns ever existed?

01:30:10.022 --> 01:30:17.598
Flat Flat describes something that is level and smooth with no curved parts.

01:30:17.658 --> 01:30:23.373
My parents bought a new flat-screen TV over the weekend.

01:30:23.433 --> 01:30:28.518
Gentlemen A gentleman is a nice man.

01:30:28.578 --> 01:30:33.132
My grandfather is a kind and helpful gentleman.

01:30:33.192 --> 01:30:39.956
Hidden Hidden means to be not easily noticed or too hard to find.

01:30:40.016 --> 01:30:44.948
The hidden camera recorded everything in the parking lot.

01:30:45.008 --> 01:30:47.070
Maybe.

01:30:47.130 --> 01:30:52.114
Maybe is used to show that something is possible or may be true.

01:30:52.174 --> 01:30:57.839
If I focus hard enough, maybe I can come up with the right answer.

01:30:57.899 --> 01:31:00.012
Officer.

01:31:00.072 --> 01:31:03.124
An officer is a leader in the army.

01:31:03.184 --> 01:31:07.527
The soldiers followed the orders of the officer.

01:31:07.587 --> 01:31:09.737
Original.

01:31:09.797 --> 01:31:14.038
If something is original, it is the first one of that thing.

01:31:14.098 --> 01:31:18.689
This is the original painting of the Mona Lisa.

01:31:18.750 --> 01:31:20.770
Pound.

01:31:20.830 --> 01:31:25.791
To pound something is to hit it many times with a lot of force.

01:31:25.852 --> 01:31:29.432
He pounded the nail with the hammer.

01:31:29.492 --> 01:31:31.683
Process.

01:31:31.743 --> 01:31:35.698
A process is the steps to take to do something.

01:31:35.758 --> 01:31:39.714
Making a cake is a long process.

01:31:39.774 --> 01:31:46.436
Publish To publish a book is to get it printed and ready to sell.

01:31:46.496 --> 01:31:50.908
That company publishes daily newspapers.

01:31:50.968 --> 01:31:58.182
Theatre A theatre is a building where you watch plays, shows and movies.

01:31:58.242 --> 01:32:02.144
We went to the theatre to see a play.

01:32:02.204 --> 01:32:07.376
Wealth Wealth is a large amount of money.

01:32:07.436 --> 01:32:13.289
One of the most important things to some people is wealth.

01:32:13.348 --> 01:32:20.270
Adams County's Gold Adams Academy was a good school.

01:32:20.330 --> 01:32:23.191
Boys lived there and took classes.

01:32:23.251 --> 01:32:25.690
Tom worked hard all week.

01:32:25.750 --> 01:32:29.519
On a spring Saturday, he wanted to do something fun.

01:32:29.579 --> 01:32:32.849
He asked his friend Jeff to go to the movie theater.

01:32:32.909 --> 01:32:35.170
Sorry, Jeff answered.

01:32:35.230 --> 01:32:36.960
I'm going to a concert.

01:32:37.020 --> 01:32:39.801
So Tom asked Joe to go to the movies.

01:32:39.861 --> 01:32:42.401
But Joe's soccer team had a game.

01:32:42.461 --> 01:32:46.252
Next, Tom went down the hall to Brad's room.

01:32:46.312 --> 01:32:49.723
Brad was reading a very large old book.

01:32:49.783 --> 01:32:52.353
Hi Brad, Tom said.

01:32:52.413 --> 01:32:54.254
Are you reading a dictionary?

01:32:54.314 --> 01:32:55.812
It looks ancient.

01:32:55.872 --> 01:33:00.194
No, this is called the Wealth of Adams County.

01:33:00.254 --> 01:33:03.286
It's about hidden gold in Adams County.

01:33:03.346 --> 01:33:05.720
It's more than a century old.

01:33:05.780 --> 01:33:08.302
It was published in 1870.

01:33:08.362 --> 01:33:11.778
Look, it even has the original cover on it.

01:33:11.838 --> 01:33:14.882
Tom asked, where did you get it?

01:33:14.942 --> 01:33:17.023
It's from my dad's friend.

01:33:17.083 --> 01:33:20.205
He is a nice gentleman, an officer in the army.

01:33:20.265 --> 01:33:25.267
Answered Brad, the gold doesn't really exist, does it?

01:33:25.327 --> 01:33:26.608
Tom asked.

01:33:26.668 --> 01:33:31.160
I don't know, but maybe there are clues to it in this book.

01:33:31.220 --> 01:33:32.630
Let's find it.

01:33:32.690 --> 01:33:35.263
Looking for gold sounded like fun.

01:33:35.323 --> 01:33:39.236
The first clue was to find a flat tree underground.

01:33:39.296 --> 01:33:42.468
It must be in the forest, Tom said.

01:33:42.528 --> 01:33:47.220
Brad said, the flat tree could be a board under the dirt.

01:33:47.280 --> 01:33:49.191
It could cover the gold.

01:33:49.251 --> 01:33:52.272
Tom and Brad dug in the dirt all morning.

01:33:52.332 --> 01:33:55.464
The process of looking for gold made them hungry.

01:33:55.524 --> 01:33:57.776
They were ready to stop for lunch.

01:33:57.836 --> 01:34:00.266
But then Brad hit something hard.

01:34:00.326 --> 01:34:01.998
It was a board.

01:34:02.058 --> 01:34:04.962
Brad pounded on the board until it broke.

01:34:05.022 --> 01:34:07.425
There was a small hole under it.

01:34:07.485 --> 01:34:08.826
Look!

01:34:08.886 --> 01:34:11.056
He held up a gold coin.

01:34:11.116 --> 01:34:13.838
Tom saw a piece of paper in the hole.

01:34:13.898 --> 01:34:15.869
Brad, there's more.

01:34:15.929 --> 01:34:18.310
It's a map to the rest of the gold.

01:34:18.370 --> 01:34:19.931
Brad smiled.

01:34:19.991 --> 01:34:21.382
Let's go.

01:34:21.442 --> 01:34:26.402
And they hurried to find the wealth of Adams County.

01:34:26.462 --> 01:34:29.650
Unit 17.

01:34:29.710 --> 01:34:31.282
Word list.

01:34:31.342 --> 01:34:33.052
Appreciate.

01:34:33.112 --> 01:34:37.334
To appreciate something is to understand its good qualities.

01:34:37.394 --> 01:34:41.366
I can appreciate the lovely scenery.

01:34:41.426 --> 01:34:43.588
Available.

01:34:43.648 --> 01:34:47.120
If something is available, it means you can get it.

01:34:47.180 --> 01:34:51.262
There are many seats available in the room.

01:34:51.322 --> 01:34:53.362
Beat.

01:34:53.422 --> 01:34:57.210
To beat someone means to do better than they do.

01:34:57.271 --> 01:35:01.338
I manage to beat everyone in the race.

01:35:01.398 --> 01:35:03.420
Bright.

01:35:03.480 --> 01:35:07.021
If something is bright, it shows a lot of light.

01:35:07.081 --> 01:35:11.642
The bright light from the explosion hurt my eyes.

01:35:11.702 --> 01:35:13.914
Celebrate.

01:35:13.974 --> 01:35:18.546
To celebrate is to do something to show that an event is special.

01:35:18.606 --> 01:35:23.011
We all celebrate it when we heard the great news.

01:35:23.071 --> 01:35:25.236
Determine.

01:35:25.296 --> 01:35:28.948
To determine means to choose or make a decision.

01:35:29.008 --> 01:35:33.592
He tried to determine which one to eat first.

01:35:33.652 --> 01:35:35.862
Disappear.

01:35:35.922 --> 01:35:40.366
To disappear means to go away or not be seen.

01:35:40.426 --> 01:35:45.219
The top of the building is disappearing in the clouds.

01:35:45.279 --> 01:35:47.250
Else.

01:35:47.310 --> 01:35:51.758
If you talk about something else, you talk about something different.

01:35:51.818 --> 01:35:57.216
I wanted a bike for my birthday, but I got something else.

01:35:57.276 --> 01:35:59.336
Fair.

01:35:59.396 --> 01:36:04.500
Fair describes treating someone in a way that is reasonable or right.

01:36:04.560 --> 01:36:08.752
He sold me his car for a fair price.

01:36:08.812 --> 01:36:10.872
Flow.

01:36:10.932 --> 01:36:15.685
Two flow is to move easily and continuously in one direction.

01:36:15.745 --> 01:36:20.365
The water flowed over the rocks and into the lane.

01:36:20.425 --> 01:36:22.604
Forward.

01:36:22.664 --> 01:36:26.787
If you move forward, you move in the direction in front of you.

01:36:26.848 --> 01:36:31.851
When he saw his mother, the baby crawled forward to her.

01:36:31.911 --> 01:36:33.942
Hill.

01:36:34.002 --> 01:36:36.974
A hill is a round area of land.

01:36:37.034 --> 01:36:39.626
It is higher than a land around it.

01:36:39.686 --> 01:36:43.910
The sun was rising above the green hills.

01:36:43.970 --> 01:36:46.032
Level.

01:36:46.092 --> 01:36:49.732
A level is a point on a scale that measures something.

01:36:49.792 --> 01:36:53.492
Please check the level of the temperature.

01:36:53.552 --> 01:36:55.613
Loan.

01:36:55.673 --> 01:37:01.086
If someone or something is loan, they are the only one of that kind.

01:37:01.146 --> 01:37:04.918
A lone man walked along the street.

01:37:04.978 --> 01:37:06.980
Puddle.

01:37:07.040 --> 01:37:10.412
A puddle is a pool of liquid on the ground.

01:37:10.472 --> 01:37:14.634
When the ice melted, it formed a puddle.

01:37:14.694 --> 01:37:16.946
Response.

01:37:17.006 --> 01:37:20.218
A response is the answer to a question.

01:37:20.278 --> 01:37:22.560
He asked if I was sad.

01:37:22.620 --> 01:37:25.532
My response was no.

01:37:25.592 --> 01:37:27.674
Season.

01:37:27.734 --> 01:37:30.176
A season is a time of the year.

01:37:30.236 --> 01:37:33.648
Spring, summer, fall, or winter.

01:37:33.708 --> 01:37:38.962
Fall is a warm season, while winter is very cold.

01:37:39.022 --> 01:37:41.204
Solution.

01:37:41.264 --> 01:37:44.606
A solution is a way to solve a problem.

01:37:44.666 --> 01:37:46.637
There are many problems.

01:37:46.697 --> 01:37:49.184
We need solutions.

01:37:49.244 --> 01:37:51.260
Waste.

01:37:51.320 --> 01:37:55.304
To waste means to carelessly use something all up.

01:37:55.364 --> 01:37:59.487
Turn off the water so you don't waste it.

01:37:59.547 --> 01:38:01.528
Weather.

01:38:01.588 --> 01:38:05.772
You use weather when you must choose between two things.

01:38:05.832 --> 01:38:11.048
I could not decide whether to go left or right.

01:38:11.108 --> 01:38:14.773
The race for water.

01:38:14.833 --> 01:38:18.060
There was a town next to a river.

01:38:18.120 --> 01:38:22.868
The people there had a lot of water, but they wasted it.

01:38:22.928 --> 01:38:25.472
That made the sky angry.

01:38:25.532 --> 01:38:30.286
It said, If you waste water, I will take it away from you.

01:38:30.346 --> 01:38:32.508
But the people didn't listen.

01:38:32.568 --> 01:38:37.812
When the season changed from spring to summer, the clouds disappeared.

01:38:37.872 --> 01:38:41.655
The bright sun was hot and made the river dry.

01:38:41.715 --> 01:38:44.277
There was no water available.

01:38:44.337 --> 01:38:47.800
People asked, When will the rain fall?

01:38:47.860 --> 01:38:52.165
The sky's response was, you don't appreciate water.

01:38:52.225 --> 01:38:55.869
You waste it, and now I will never make rain again."

01:38:55.890 --> 01:38:59.414
A boy determined that this wasn't fair.

01:38:59.474 --> 01:39:01.116
He thought of a solution.

01:39:01.176 --> 01:39:03.408
He asked the sky to raise him.

01:39:03.468 --> 01:39:11.162
He said, If I get to the top of that hill before your rain can form puddles, you must fill our river.

01:39:11.222 --> 01:39:12.743
The sky laughed.

01:39:12.803 --> 01:39:15.254
Little boy, I am the sky.

01:39:15.314 --> 01:39:17.385
I am above everything else.

01:39:17.445 --> 01:39:19.366
You cannot beat me.

01:39:19.426 --> 01:39:21.976
But the boy knew he would win.

01:39:22.036 --> 01:39:25.307
When the race began, the boy ran forward.

01:39:25.367 --> 01:39:30.098
The sky started raining on the hill, but puddles did not form there.

01:39:30.158 --> 01:39:33.769
When it rained on the hill, the water went down.

01:39:33.829 --> 01:39:35.850
The sky kept raining.

01:39:35.910 --> 01:39:38.620
The water flowed down into the river.

01:39:38.680 --> 01:39:43.032
When the boy reached the top of the hill, the river was full.

01:39:43.092 --> 01:39:45.452
The people began to celebrate.

01:39:45.512 --> 01:39:49.633
It was the highest level the river had ever been at before.

01:39:49.693 --> 01:39:51.774
The sky was angry.

01:39:51.834 --> 01:39:53.664
A boy can't beat me.

01:39:53.724 --> 01:39:56.605
I won't fill your river," it said.

01:39:56.665 --> 01:39:58.465
Now the boy laughed.

01:39:58.525 --> 01:40:02.716
It doesn't matter whether you want to fill it or not, he said.

01:40:02.776 --> 01:40:04.287
You already did.

01:40:04.347 --> 01:40:06.797
The sky looked at the full river.

01:40:06.857 --> 01:40:09.118
You tricked me, it said.

01:40:09.178 --> 01:40:13.039
It asked the people, do you appreciate water now?

01:40:13.099 --> 01:40:16.630
Yes, they said, we won't waste it.

01:40:16.690 --> 01:40:23.654
That is how a lone boy saved his town and won the race for water.

01:40:23.714 --> 01:40:29.787
Unit 18, word list, argue.

01:40:29.847 --> 01:40:34.920
To argue is to angrily speak to someone because you do not agree.

01:40:34.979 --> 01:40:38.686
We argued about where to go for dinner.

01:40:38.746 --> 01:40:51.048
Communicate To communicate is to give information by talking, writing, etc. I communicated with Paul about his new ideas.

01:40:51.108 --> 01:40:56.180
Crowd A crowd is a large group of people.

01:40:56.240 --> 01:41:01.384
A large crowd had gathered on the street to see the accident.

01:41:01.443 --> 01:41:07.271
Depend To depend on someone or something is to need them.

01:41:07.330 --> 01:41:11.868
Children depend on their parents for many things.

01:41:11.928 --> 01:41:14.000
Dish.

01:41:14.059 --> 01:41:16.401
A dish is a plate.

01:41:16.460 --> 01:41:20.674
She put a clean white dish on the table.

01:41:20.734 --> 01:41:22.774
Empty.

01:41:22.834 --> 01:41:26.588
If something is empty, it does not have anything in it.

01:41:26.648 --> 01:41:33.025
My gas tank was almost empty, so I couldn't drive my car very long.

01:41:33.085 --> 01:41:35.240
Exact.

01:41:35.300 --> 01:41:39.122
If something is exact, it is just the right amount.

01:41:39.182 --> 01:41:43.966
Please use the exact amount of sugar for the cake.

01:41:44.026 --> 01:41:46.026
Fresh.

01:41:46.086 --> 01:41:48.438
If something is fresh, it is new.

01:41:48.458 --> 01:41:51.530
I just bought these oranges.

01:41:51.590 --> 01:41:54.052
They are very fresh.

01:41:54.112 --> 01:41:56.153
Gather.

01:41:56.214 --> 01:42:00.976
Together is to collect several things, usually from different places.

01:42:01.036 --> 01:42:05.008
Sam gathered some flowers for his mother.

01:42:05.068 --> 01:42:07.160
Indicate.

01:42:07.220 --> 01:42:12.394
To indicate means to show, point, or make something clear.

01:42:12.454 --> 01:42:17.758
He pointed to his eyes to indicate where he had heard himself.

01:42:17.818 --> 01:42:19.800
Item.

01:42:19.860 --> 01:42:23.312
An item is a thing that you buy or sell.

01:42:23.372 --> 01:42:27.886
I have many items for school in my bank.

01:42:27.946 --> 01:42:46.939
Offer To offer is to present someone with something He offered me the keys to his car Price The price of something is how much it costs What is the price of this item?

01:42:46.999 --> 01:43:01.956
Product A product is something that is made My sister has many beauty products in her room Property Property is something that someone owns.

01:43:02.016 --> 01:43:05.398
The house is now my property.

01:43:05.457 --> 01:43:10.440
Purchase To purchase something is to buy it.

01:43:10.500 --> 01:43:14.272
I recently purchased a new car.

01:43:14.332 --> 01:43:20.685
Recommend To recommend something is to say that someone should do it.

01:43:20.745 --> 01:43:25.590
My doctor recommended that I get some exercise.

01:43:25.650 --> 01:43:27.682
Select.

01:43:27.742 --> 01:43:30.716
To select something is to choose it.

01:43:30.776 --> 01:43:35.650
I hope that I selected the right answers on the test.

01:43:35.710 --> 01:43:37.682
Tool.

01:43:37.742 --> 01:43:41.164
A tool is something that helps you do a task.

01:43:41.224 --> 01:43:45.158
We used a tool to fix the window.

01:43:45.218 --> 01:43:47.140
Treat.

01:43:47.200 --> 01:43:51.113
To treat is to act in a certain way toward someone.

01:43:51.174 --> 01:43:56.082
The cats treated the mouse very nicely.

01:43:56.142 --> 01:44:04.016
The Little Red Chicken A little red chicken had a store in a small town.

01:44:04.076 --> 01:44:07.939
She sold many different items to people in the town.

01:44:07.999 --> 01:44:10.360
The people loved her products.

01:44:10.420 --> 01:44:13.613
One day, a cat came to her property.

01:44:13.673 --> 01:44:17.805
He saw the sign that indicated where the chicken store was located.

01:44:17.866 --> 01:44:19.877
He wanted to purchase bread.

01:44:19.937 --> 01:44:22.588
But the chicken store was almost empty.

01:44:22.648 --> 01:44:25.010
She had only a bag of wheat.

01:44:25.070 --> 01:44:29.264
You can use the wheat to make bread, the chicken said.

01:44:29.323 --> 01:44:33.268
No, I don't want to work," the cat said.

01:44:33.328 --> 01:44:35.410
I just want to buy bread.

01:44:35.470 --> 01:44:38.882
The cat became angry and left the store.

01:44:38.942 --> 01:44:43.308
Later, the little red chicken saw the cat in a crowd.

01:44:43.368 --> 01:44:49.184
I will help you make the bread, she said, but the cat treated her badly.

01:44:49.244 --> 01:44:51.724
He did not even communicate with her.

01:44:51.784 --> 01:44:56.914
He did not want to do any work, so the chicken decided to make the bread.

01:44:56.974 --> 01:45:01.077
She selected the exact amount of wheat to make fresh bread.

01:45:01.137 --> 01:45:04.980
She used a stone to pound the wheat to get it ready.

01:45:05.040 --> 01:45:07.650
Soon, her bread was ready.

01:45:07.710 --> 01:45:10.902
The cat came and saw the bread on a dish.

01:45:10.962 --> 01:45:14.485
Give me some of your bread," he said.

01:45:14.544 --> 01:45:17.566
No, said the little red chicken.

01:45:17.626 --> 01:45:22.188
You did not help me make the bread, so you shall not have any to eat.

01:45:22.249 --> 01:45:24.350
The cat argued with the chicken.

01:45:24.410 --> 01:45:29.943
He tried to offer a price for it, but the little red chicken did not want to sell her bread.

01:45:30.003 --> 01:45:35.326
Don't depend on others to do work for you, said the little red chicken.

01:45:35.386 --> 01:45:37.876
Then how will I get bread?

01:45:37.936 --> 01:45:41.516
The cat asked, I recommend doing some work.

01:45:41.576 --> 01:45:45.779
Said the little red chicken, use a tool to plant your own wheat.

01:45:45.839 --> 01:45:49.751
When it grows big, you can gather it and make your own bread.

01:45:49.811 --> 01:45:55.404
You need to learn to do work for what you want.

01:45:55.464 --> 01:46:01.777
Unit 19, word list, alive.

01:46:01.837 --> 01:46:06.166
If someone or something is alive, they are not dead.

01:46:06.226 --> 01:46:12.217
My grandparents are still alive, even though they are over 90.

01:46:12.277 --> 01:46:17.542
Bone A bone is a hard part of the body.

01:46:17.602 --> 01:46:21.916
I brought home a nice bone for my dog.

01:46:21.976 --> 01:46:27.652
Bother To bother is to make the effort to do something.

01:46:27.711 --> 01:46:31.892
No one bothered to wash the dishes today.

01:46:31.952 --> 01:46:34.010
Captain.

01:46:34.070 --> 01:46:38.214
A captain is the person who leads a ship or airplane.

01:46:38.273 --> 01:46:42.606
The captain sailed his ship to Australia.

01:46:42.666 --> 01:46:44.878
Conclusion.

01:46:44.938 --> 01:46:48.470
The conclusion of something is the final part of it.

01:46:48.530 --> 01:46:54.356
At the conclusion of the race, the spectators cheered for the winner.

01:46:54.416 --> 01:46:56.448
Doubt.

01:46:56.508 --> 01:46:59.740
Doubt is a feeling of not being sure.

01:46:59.800 --> 01:47:03.804
I have doubt that the story is true.

01:47:03.864 --> 01:47:06.068
Explore.

01:47:06.128 --> 01:47:09.298
To explore is to look for new places.

01:47:09.358 --> 01:47:14.280
He wants to explore the world and see new things.

01:47:14.340 --> 01:47:16.441
Foreign.

01:47:16.501 --> 01:47:20.352
If something is foreign, it is from a different country.

01:47:20.412 --> 01:47:25.014
Mexican food is a popular foreign food.

01:47:25.074 --> 01:47:27.154
Glad.

01:47:27.214 --> 01:47:30.125
If you are glad, you're happy.

01:47:30.185 --> 01:47:33.867
I am glad you came to my party.

01:47:33.927 --> 01:47:40.670
However, however means despite or not being influenced by something.

01:47:40.731 --> 01:47:42.741
She is a great cook.

01:47:42.801 --> 01:47:47.012
However, she never had professional lessons.

01:47:47.072 --> 01:47:49.384
Injustice.

01:47:49.444 --> 01:47:53.065
Injustice is a lack of fairness or justice.

01:47:53.125 --> 01:47:58.731
Putting an innocent person in jail is an act of injustice.

01:47:58.791 --> 01:48:01.146
International.

01:48:01.206 --> 01:48:05.748
If something is international, it involves more than one country.

01:48:05.808 --> 01:48:11.410
The United Nations is a powerful international organization.

01:48:11.470 --> 01:48:13.550
Lawyer.

01:48:13.610 --> 01:48:17.782
A lawyer works with the law and represents people in court.

01:48:17.842 --> 01:48:23.524
The lawyer left the courthouse after the judge made her decision.

01:48:23.584 --> 01:48:25.666
Mention.

01:48:25.726 --> 01:48:28.972
To mention something is to talk about it.

01:48:29.032 --> 01:48:34.020
The doctors mentioned the problems that the patient was having.

01:48:34.080 --> 01:48:38.814
Policy A policy is a rule.

01:48:38.874 --> 01:48:44.137
He told us that his policy was to put customers first.

01:48:44.197 --> 01:48:51.012
Social If something is social, it is about many people in a community.

01:48:51.072 --> 01:48:56.635
People should come together and fix the world's social problems.

01:48:56.695 --> 01:49:02.258
Speech A speech is something said to a group of people.

01:49:02.318 --> 01:49:05.888
She gave a speech to the class.

01:49:05.948 --> 01:49:12.230
Staff A staff is a group of people working together in a company.

01:49:12.290 --> 01:49:17.832
My dad has a staff of four people to help him at the office.

01:49:17.892 --> 01:49:23.774
Toward If you go toward something, you go closer to it.

01:49:23.834 --> 01:49:28.562
Santa walked toward my house with a special tree.

01:49:28.622 --> 01:49:30.663
Wood.

01:49:30.723 --> 01:49:33.863
Wood is the thing that trees are made of.

01:49:33.923 --> 01:49:38.765
I put the pieces of wood in a pile.

01:49:38.825 --> 01:49:41.838
Shipwrecked.

01:49:41.898 --> 01:49:44.470
Simon Yates was a lawyer.

01:49:44.530 --> 01:49:46.411
He helped many people.

01:49:46.471 --> 01:49:49.523
However, he was not a nice man.

01:49:49.583 --> 01:49:53.074
His policy was to help only rich people.

01:49:53.134 --> 01:49:56.436
He didn't bother about social injustice.

01:49:56.496 --> 01:50:01.179
He made a lot of money, but many people didn't like him.

01:50:01.239 --> 01:50:04.600
Even people on his staff didn't like him.

01:50:04.660 --> 01:50:07.641
They wanted bad things to happen to him.

01:50:07.701 --> 01:50:11.692
In fact, they were glad when he got into trouble.

01:50:11.752 --> 01:50:14.524
Simon had a very bad day.

01:50:14.584 --> 01:50:17.835
He did many things wrong and lost his job.

01:50:17.895 --> 01:50:20.656
Soon, he didn't have any money.

01:50:20.716 --> 01:50:25.007
His wife, Mrs. Yates, began to have doubts about him.

01:50:25.067 --> 01:50:27.738
Simon wanted to start a new life.

01:50:27.798 --> 01:50:29.969
He planned to leave the country.

01:50:30.029 --> 01:50:33.492
He mentioned his plan to the captain of a ship.

01:50:33.552 --> 01:50:36.446
The captain was exploring the world.

01:50:36.506 --> 01:50:42.412
The captain felt bad for Simon and said, I will take you to foreign countries.

01:50:42.472 --> 01:50:44.779
They left the next day.

01:50:44.839 --> 01:50:50.250
Near the conclusion of their international trip, the weather turned bad.

01:50:50.310 --> 01:50:54.965
A wave pushed Simon off the boat, but he was alive.

01:50:55.025 --> 01:50:57.228
He swam toward an island.

01:50:57.287 --> 01:51:00.140
After a long time, he got there.

01:51:00.200 --> 01:51:02.602
At first he was upset.

01:51:02.662 --> 01:51:05.044
He was lost and alone.

01:51:05.104 --> 01:51:08.307
I'll never go home again, he thought.

01:51:08.367 --> 01:51:12.310
He had a lot of problems, but he survived.

01:51:12.370 --> 01:51:14.842
He built a house in a tree.

01:51:14.902 --> 01:51:17.414
He lived on a diet of fish.

01:51:17.474 --> 01:51:20.276
He made tools from wood and bones.

01:51:20.336 --> 01:51:23.238
He made a cup to drink rainwater.

01:51:23.298 --> 01:51:26.802
Slowly, he learned to be happy on the island.

01:51:26.862 --> 01:51:28.414
He swam every day.

01:51:28.434 --> 01:51:33.950
He had trouble sometimes, but he always found a way to fix the problem.

01:51:34.010 --> 01:51:35.500
Life was simple.

01:51:35.561 --> 01:51:36.672
He liked it.

01:51:36.732 --> 01:51:40.834
Finally, people on a ship saw Simon on the island.

01:51:40.894 --> 01:51:43.006
They wanted to take him home.

01:51:43.066 --> 01:51:44.906
But Simon was happy.

01:51:44.966 --> 01:51:47.838
He gave them a long speech about life.

01:51:47.898 --> 01:51:49.919
He said he wanted to stay.

01:51:49.979 --> 01:51:55.772
He liked his new simple life more than his old life.

01:51:55.832 --> 01:52:00.335
Unit 20, word list.

01:52:00.395 --> 01:52:01.966
Achieve.

01:52:02.026 --> 01:52:06.412
To achieve something is to successfully do it after trying hard.

01:52:06.472 --> 01:52:10.717
I was happy that I could achieve my goal.

01:52:10.777 --> 01:52:16.378
Advice To advise someone is to tell them what to do.

01:52:16.438 --> 01:52:21.339
My mother often advises people about their money.

01:52:21.399 --> 01:52:23.559
Already?

01:52:23.619 --> 01:52:28.150
If something happens already, it happens before a certain time.

01:52:28.210 --> 01:52:31.551
It is already time for the movie to start.

01:52:31.611 --> 01:52:33.680
Let's go in.

01:52:33.740 --> 01:52:40.255
Basic If something is basic, it is very simple or easy.

01:52:40.315 --> 01:52:44.969
I learned some basic English skills in school today.

01:52:45.029 --> 01:52:50.204
Bit A bit is a small amount of something.

01:52:50.264 --> 01:52:54.888
I ate a bit of chocolate before I went to bed.

01:52:54.948 --> 01:53:00.544
Consider To consider something means to think about it.

01:53:00.604 --> 01:53:05.819
Pete didn't like his job, he considered getting a new one.

01:53:05.879 --> 01:53:08.092
Destroy.

01:53:08.152 --> 01:53:13.736
To destroy means to damage something so badly that it cannot be used.

01:53:13.796 --> 01:53:16.979
The glass was destroyed.

01:53:17.039 --> 01:53:19.220
Entertain.

01:53:19.280 --> 01:53:23.474
To entertain someone is to do something that they enjoy.

01:53:23.534 --> 01:53:27.710
The clown entertained the kids at the party.

01:53:27.770 --> 01:53:29.812
Extra.

01:53:29.872 --> 01:53:33.654
If something is extra, it is more than what is needed.

01:53:33.714 --> 01:53:37.926
The squirrel had extra knots for the winter.

01:53:37.986 --> 01:53:40.026
Goal.

01:53:40.086 --> 01:53:42.908
A goal is something you work toward.

01:53:42.968 --> 01:53:46.768
Her goal was to become a doctor.

01:53:46.828 --> 01:53:48.830
Lie.

01:53:48.890 --> 01:53:53.622
To lie is to say or write something untrue to deceive someone.

01:53:53.682 --> 01:53:58.904
Whenever Pinocchio lied to his father, his nose grew.

01:53:58.964 --> 01:54:03.797
Meat Meat is food made of animals.

01:54:03.857 --> 01:54:08.350
This piece of meat I'm eating tastes very good.

01:54:08.410 --> 01:54:10.500
Opinion.

01:54:10.560 --> 01:54:14.362
An opinion is a thought about a person or a thing.

01:54:14.422 --> 01:54:17.554
Meg told me her opinion of my story.

01:54:17.614 --> 01:54:20.726
She said it was not funny.

01:54:20.786 --> 01:54:22.838
Real.

01:54:22.898 --> 01:54:26.670
If something is real, it actually exists.

01:54:26.730 --> 01:54:31.474
The handbag has a stamp on it, so it's real.

01:54:31.534 --> 01:54:33.605
Reflect.

01:54:33.665 --> 01:54:39.619
To reflect is when a surface sends back light, heat, sound, or an image.

01:54:39.678 --> 01:54:46.062
Her face was reflected on the smooth glass.

01:54:46.122 --> 01:54:51.136
To regard someone or something is to think of them in a certain way.

01:54:51.196 --> 01:54:55.522
The boy regarded the girl as a good friend.

01:54:55.582 --> 01:54:57.628
Serve.

01:54:57.688 --> 01:55:01.679
To serve someone is to give them food or drinks.

01:55:01.739 --> 01:55:05.360
He served us our drinks quickly.

01:55:05.420 --> 01:55:11.032
Vegetable A vegetable is a plant used as food.

01:55:11.092 --> 01:55:14.844
Carrots are my favorite vegetable.

01:55:14.904 --> 01:55:21.016
War A war is a big fight between two groups of people.

01:55:21.076 --> 01:55:25.930
Many young men died in the war.

01:55:25.990 --> 01:55:32.026
If something is worth an amount of money, it costs that amount.

01:55:32.086 --> 01:55:36.628
Our house is worth a lot of money.

01:55:36.688 --> 01:55:47.091
The Seven Cities of Gold Many years ago, a Spanish officer named Coronado heard the story of seven great cities.

01:55:47.151 --> 01:55:50.992
The walls of these cities are made of gold, his friends told him.

01:55:51.052 --> 01:55:56.163
The people eat meat from golden plates and dress in nice clothes, they said.

01:55:56.223 --> 01:55:59.434
They called these cities the seven cities of gold.

01:55:59.494 --> 01:56:01.064
Were the cities real?

01:56:01.124 --> 01:56:04.005
Coronado never considered asking his friends.

01:56:04.065 --> 01:56:09.318
Coronado thought to himself, the things in these cities must be worth a lot of money.

01:56:09.378 --> 01:56:12.281
So he went to find the seven cities of gold.

01:56:12.341 --> 01:56:16.473
He took along three hundred men, many horses and extra food.

01:56:16.533 --> 01:56:17.874
They headed west.

01:56:17.934 --> 01:56:21.286
Coronado wanted to achieve his gold very badly.

01:56:21.345 --> 01:56:24.377
Coronado and his men rode for many days.

01:56:24.437 --> 01:56:26.308
Then they saw some cities.

01:56:26.368 --> 01:56:30.330
We found the seven cities of gold, his men yelled.

01:56:30.390 --> 01:56:32.330
But Coronado wasn't happy.

01:56:32.390 --> 01:56:34.192
He had a different opinion.

01:56:34.251 --> 01:56:37.763
These can't be the seven cities of gold, he said.

01:56:37.823 --> 01:56:40.065
Look, they're made of dirt.

01:56:40.125 --> 01:56:41.606
Cornado is right.

01:56:41.666 --> 01:56:44.019
The cities weren't bright and golden.

01:56:44.079 --> 01:56:45.811
They were dirty and brown.

01:56:45.871 --> 01:56:48.714
The people didn't eat meat from golden plates.

01:56:48.774 --> 01:56:51.608
They ate vegetables from regular bowls.

01:56:51.668 --> 01:56:53.960
They wore the most basic clothes.

01:56:54.020 --> 01:56:57.410
Coronado regarded the cities as ugly places.

01:56:57.470 --> 01:57:00.562
What happened to the cities of gold, he thought?

01:57:00.622 --> 01:57:02.252
Did someone destroy them?

01:57:02.312 --> 01:57:03.742
Was there a war?

01:57:03.802 --> 01:57:06.613
Did someone already come and take the gold?

01:57:06.674 --> 01:57:12.265
That night, the people of the cities entertained Coronado and his men and served them food.

01:57:12.325 --> 01:57:14.727
They advised Coronado to go home.

01:57:14.787 --> 01:57:17.650
There is no gold here," they told him.

01:57:17.710 --> 01:57:19.432
Coronado was angry.

01:57:19.492 --> 01:57:21.754
Did his friends lie to him?

01:57:21.814 --> 01:57:23.756
He left the next morning.

01:57:23.816 --> 01:57:26.648
He looked back at the city's one more time.

01:57:26.708 --> 01:57:29.622
The sun reflected light on the dirt houses.

01:57:29.682 --> 01:57:32.445
Coronado thought he saw a bit of gold.

01:57:32.504 --> 01:57:34.936
Were his friends right after all?

01:57:34.996 --> 01:57:38.930
No, he told himself, it's just the sun.

01:57:38.990 --> 01:57:42.910
Then he turned away and went home.

01:57:42.970 --> 01:57:47.699
Unit 21, word list.

01:57:47.759 --> 01:57:49.309
Appear.

01:57:49.370 --> 01:57:52.060
To appear is to seem.

01:57:52.120 --> 01:57:54.441
She appeared to be sad.

01:57:54.501 --> 01:57:56.672
She was crying.

01:57:56.732 --> 01:57:58.742
Base.

01:57:58.802 --> 01:58:01.824
The base is the bottom of something.

01:58:01.884 --> 01:58:06.125
The base of the table has three legs.

01:58:06.185 --> 01:58:08.246
Brain.

01:58:08.306 --> 01:58:12.235
The brain is the organ in your head that lets you think.

01:58:12.294 --> 01:58:16.564
You must use your brain to solve the problem.

01:58:16.624 --> 01:58:23.126
Career A career is a job that you do for a large part of your life.

01:58:23.186 --> 01:58:28.338
He was in the hospitality business for most of his career.

01:58:28.398 --> 01:58:32.771
Clerk A clerk is a type of worker.

01:58:32.830 --> 01:58:35.612
Clerks in a store help customers.

01:58:35.672 --> 01:58:40.024
The clerk added up her bill for the groceries.

01:58:40.084 --> 01:58:42.155
Effort.

01:58:42.215 --> 01:58:46.026
Effort is hard work or an attempt to do something.

01:58:46.086 --> 01:58:50.896
He always puts a lot of effort into his studies.

01:58:50.956 --> 01:58:52.947
Enter.

01:58:53.007 --> 01:58:56.008
To enter a place is to go into it.

01:58:56.068 --> 01:59:00.918
Two guards greeted me as I entered the front door.

01:59:00.978 --> 01:59:03.079
Excellent.

01:59:03.139 --> 01:59:06.699
When something is excellent, it is very good.

01:59:06.759 --> 01:59:11.314
I got an excellent scar on my school test.

01:59:11.374 --> 01:59:13.369
Hero.

01:59:13.428 --> 01:59:17.491
A hero is a brave person who does things to help others.

01:59:17.551 --> 01:59:23.805
To children, the man in the blue and red costume was a real hero.

01:59:23.865 --> 01:59:25.806
Hurry.

01:59:25.866 --> 01:59:28.918
To hurry is to do something quickly.

01:59:28.978 --> 01:59:32.530
I hurried home on my bike.

01:59:32.590 --> 01:59:34.772
Inform.

01:59:34.831 --> 01:59:38.613
To inform someone is to tell them about something.

01:59:38.674 --> 01:59:43.134
I called and informed her about my idea.

01:59:43.194 --> 01:59:45.312
Later.

01:59:45.372 --> 01:59:50.383
Later means after the present, expected or usual time.

01:59:50.443 --> 01:59:56.384
She missed the train, so she'll arrive a little later than expected.

01:59:56.444 --> 01:59:58.485
Leave.

01:59:58.544 --> 02:00:02.785
To leave means to go away from someone or something.

02:00:02.845 --> 02:00:07.516
Epact is back and was ready to leave for home.

02:00:07.576 --> 02:00:09.686
Locate.

02:00:09.746 --> 02:00:12.690
To locate something is to find it.

02:00:12.750 --> 02:00:16.905
I could not locate my keys in the house.

02:00:16.964 --> 02:00:23.077
Nurse A nurse is a person who helps sick people in the hospital.

02:00:23.137 --> 02:00:26.558
A nurse helped me get better.

02:00:26.618 --> 02:00:34.122
Operation An operation is when a doctor replaces or removes something in the body.

02:00:34.182 --> 02:00:38.494
The operation on my arm was a success.

02:00:38.554 --> 02:00:40.606
Pain.

02:00:40.666 --> 02:00:44.037
Pain is the feeling that you have when you are hurt.

02:00:44.097 --> 02:00:47.838
His hand was full of pain.

02:00:47.898 --> 02:00:50.110
Refuse.

02:00:50.170 --> 02:00:53.231
To refuse something is to say no to it.

02:00:53.291 --> 02:00:57.202
The dog refused to play with the cat.

02:00:57.262 --> 02:00:59.334
Though.

02:00:59.394 --> 02:01:04.316
Though is used when the second idea makes the first seem surprising.

02:01:04.376 --> 02:01:08.874
Though he was overweight, he liked to be active.

02:01:08.934 --> 02:01:11.092
Various.

02:01:11.152 --> 02:01:14.766
If something is various, there are many types of it.

02:01:14.826 --> 02:01:20.318
She owns shoes of various styles.

02:01:20.378 --> 02:01:26.820
I first met 8-year-old Katy on a rainy afternoon.

02:01:26.880 --> 02:01:29.472
I was a nurse at a hospital.

02:01:29.532 --> 02:01:32.973
The clerk at the desk told me about Katy.

02:01:33.033 --> 02:01:36.514
She was there because she felt a lot of pain.

02:01:36.574 --> 02:01:40.726
The doctors located a problem at the base of her brain.

02:01:40.786 --> 02:01:44.808
I knew she was special, even before she got better.

02:01:44.868 --> 02:01:47.981
I'll always remember Katy as a hero.

02:01:48.041 --> 02:01:51.944
When I entered Katy's room, she was not in her bed.

02:01:52.004 --> 02:01:55.796
She was in a chair next to Tommy, a little boy.

02:01:55.856 --> 02:02:01.000
Though Katy did not feel well, she was playing with Tommy and his toys.

02:02:01.060 --> 02:02:05.192
It took a lot of effort for her just to sit in the chair.

02:02:05.252 --> 02:02:08.894
But she played with Tommy because it made him happy.

02:02:08.954 --> 02:02:13.800
Katy was always smiling and never appeared to be in pain.

02:02:13.860 --> 02:02:17.034
She refused to just lie in bed.

02:02:17.094 --> 02:02:20.548
One day, I found her painting a picture.

02:02:20.608 --> 02:02:24.637
Later, she gave it to one of the older patients.

02:02:24.697 --> 02:02:30.246
Another day, she went outside to get flowers for another sick little girl.

02:02:30.306 --> 02:02:32.848
Katy made everyone smile.

02:02:32.908 --> 02:02:37.022
The doctors hurried to fix the problem in Katy's brain.

02:02:37.082 --> 02:02:39.684
The operation was successful.

02:02:39.744 --> 02:02:43.747
The doctors informed the hospital staff of the good news.

02:02:43.807 --> 02:02:45.528
Katy was fine.

02:02:45.588 --> 02:02:47.750
She soon felt excellent.

02:02:47.810 --> 02:02:52.654
She got better and was able to leave the hospital a month later.

02:02:52.714 --> 02:02:56.096
I have had a long career as a nurse.

02:02:56.156 --> 02:02:58.347
I have met many patients.

02:02:58.407 --> 02:03:02.348
However, I have never met another girl like Katy.

02:03:02.408 --> 02:03:06.650
Even after she got well, she still came to the hospital.

02:03:06.710 --> 02:03:10.251
She played various games with the young patients.

02:03:10.311 --> 02:03:13.402
She read many books to the older patients.

02:03:13.462 --> 02:03:17.114
Katy's kind heart helped her get better so quickly.

02:03:17.174 --> 02:03:22.954
She is a hero to me and everyone else at the hospital.

02:03:23.014 --> 02:03:27.794
Unit 22, word list.

02:03:27.854 --> 02:03:29.575
Actual.

02:03:29.634 --> 02:03:33.316
Actual means that something is real or true.

02:03:33.376 --> 02:03:39.059
This is the actual sword that the king owned, not a fake one.

02:03:39.120 --> 02:03:41.261
Amaze.

02:03:41.321 --> 02:03:45.194
To amaze someone is to surprise them very much.

02:03:45.254 --> 02:03:49.136
The news in the paper, Amaze Jack.

02:03:49.196 --> 02:03:51.246
Charge.

02:03:51.306 --> 02:03:54.451
A charge is the price to pay for something.

02:03:54.511 --> 02:03:58.916
The charge for the shirts was $15.

02:03:58.976 --> 02:04:04.518
Comfort To comfort someone means to make them feel better.

02:04:04.579 --> 02:04:09.990
I wanted to comfort my friend after I heard the bad news.

02:04:10.050 --> 02:04:15.894
Contact To contact someone is to speak or write to them.

02:04:15.954 --> 02:04:19.826
I contacted Sue about my party.

02:04:19.886 --> 02:04:25.796
Customer A customer is a person who buys something at a store.

02:04:25.856 --> 02:04:30.220
The customer put a few items in a bag.

02:04:30.280 --> 02:04:36.516
Deliver To deliver something is to take it from one place to another.

02:04:36.576 --> 02:04:40.999
The man delivered Chinese food to my house.

02:04:41.059 --> 02:04:46.784
Earn To earn means to get money for the work you do.

02:04:46.844 --> 02:04:51.826
He earns his living as a chef in a great restaurant.

02:04:51.886 --> 02:04:56.417
Gate A gate is a type of door.

02:04:56.477 --> 02:04:59.489
Gates are usually made of metal or wood.

02:04:59.549 --> 02:05:04.362
We want to put up a wooden gate around our house.

02:05:04.422 --> 02:05:10.656
Include To include something means to have it as part of a group.

02:05:10.716 --> 02:05:14.548
Does this meal include a soft drink?

02:05:14.608 --> 02:05:20.945
Manage To manage something means to control or be in charge of it.

02:05:21.005 --> 02:05:24.888
I had to manage the meeting myself.

02:05:24.948 --> 02:05:31.660
Mystery A mystery is something that is difficult to understand or explain.

02:05:31.720 --> 02:05:36.451
The path on the map was a complete mystery to me.

02:05:36.511 --> 02:05:41.342
Occur To occur means to happen.

02:05:41.402 --> 02:05:44.882
When did the thunderstorm occur?

02:05:44.942 --> 02:05:52.592
Opposite If A is the opposite of B, A is completely different from B.

02:05:52.652 --> 02:05:56.214
The opposite of black is white.

02:05:56.274 --> 02:05:58.234
Plate.

02:05:58.294 --> 02:06:02.426
A plate is a flat round thing that you put food on.

02:06:02.486 --> 02:06:07.358
I put my plate down so I could put some food on it.

02:06:07.418 --> 02:06:09.478
Receive.

02:06:09.538 --> 02:06:12.429
To receive something is to get it.

02:06:12.489 --> 02:06:16.314
I received a present on my birthday.

02:06:16.374 --> 02:06:18.538
Reward.

02:06:18.598 --> 02:06:23.790
A reward is something given in exchange for good behavior or work.

02:06:23.850 --> 02:06:28.621
He was given a reward for his excellent performance.

02:06:28.681 --> 02:06:30.652
Set.

02:06:30.711 --> 02:06:33.982
To set something is to put it somewhere.

02:06:34.043 --> 02:06:37.914
Please set the dice down on the table.

02:06:37.974 --> 02:06:39.994
Steel.

02:06:40.054 --> 02:06:43.965
To steal is to take something that is not yours.

02:06:44.025 --> 02:06:48.985
The men try to steal money from the bank.

02:06:49.045 --> 02:06:55.078
A thief is someone who quietly takes things that do not belong to them.

02:06:55.138 --> 02:07:01.185
A thief broke into our home and took my mother's jewelry.

02:07:01.245 --> 02:07:04.628
A better reward.

02:07:04.688 --> 02:07:07.638
Jenny delivered food for a restaurant.

02:07:07.698 --> 02:07:13.260
She read the newspaper and said, uh-oh, there was a story about a thief.

02:07:13.320 --> 02:07:16.741
He stole food, and no one had seen him.

02:07:16.801 --> 02:07:19.102
Even the police couldn't catch him.

02:07:19.162 --> 02:07:21.352
Jenny was a little scared.

02:07:21.412 --> 02:07:23.633
She worked close to that area.

02:07:23.693 --> 02:07:26.764
The newspaper included a message from the police.

02:07:26.824 --> 02:07:29.702
If anything strange occurs, call us.

02:07:29.762 --> 02:07:33.774
If you help us to catch the thief, you'll earn a reward."

02:07:33.834 --> 02:07:35.616
Jenny talked to Jen.

02:07:35.676 --> 02:07:37.728
He managed the restaurant.

02:07:37.787 --> 02:07:39.930
Do you know about the thief?

02:07:39.990 --> 02:07:41.862
Yes, he said.

02:07:41.922 --> 02:07:44.584
But he steals more than one person can eat.

02:07:44.644 --> 02:07:47.055
And why haven't the police stopped him yet?

02:07:47.115 --> 02:07:48.726
It's a mystery.

02:07:48.786 --> 02:07:51.488
If you see him, contact the police.

02:07:51.548 --> 02:07:53.140
Don't run after him.

02:07:53.200 --> 02:07:55.544
Jenny drove to a customer's house.

02:07:55.604 --> 02:07:58.527
She left her car and opened the gate to the house.

02:07:58.587 --> 02:08:01.030
But then she heard a noise by her car.

02:08:01.090 --> 02:08:03.282
She yelled, thief!

02:08:03.342 --> 02:08:04.994
She wasn't scared.

02:08:05.054 --> 02:08:06.832
She wanted the reward.

02:08:06.892 --> 02:08:09.690
She did the opposite of what Jim told her to do.

02:08:09.750 --> 02:08:11.752
Hey, she yelled.

02:08:11.812 --> 02:08:13.202
Get back here.

02:08:13.262 --> 02:08:16.416
She set the food on the ground and ran to her car.

02:08:16.476 --> 02:08:19.118
But the thief had already left with the food.

02:08:19.178 --> 02:08:21.850
Ginny followed a noise around the corner.

02:08:21.910 --> 02:08:23.602
She was amazed.

02:08:23.662 --> 02:08:26.265
She saw a dog and some puppies.

02:08:26.325 --> 02:08:28.618
They were eating her food.

02:08:28.678 --> 02:08:30.978
They looked thin and scared.

02:08:31.038 --> 02:08:33.818
The actual thief is just a dog.

02:08:33.878 --> 02:08:36.699
She's feeding her puppies, she said.

02:08:36.759 --> 02:08:39.230
That's why she steals so much food.

02:08:39.290 --> 02:08:41.010
Jenny felt bad.

02:08:41.070 --> 02:08:44.491
She tried to comfort the dogs with another plate of food.

02:08:44.551 --> 02:08:46.872
Then she took them back to the store.

02:08:46.932 --> 02:08:49.462
Everyone there took a puppy home.

02:08:49.522 --> 02:08:51.472
Jenny called the police.

02:08:51.532 --> 02:08:54.428
She told them there was no real thief.

02:08:54.488 --> 02:08:57.924
Ginny didn't do it to receive the reward anymore.

02:08:57.984 --> 02:09:00.775
She said, it was just a dog.

02:09:00.835 --> 02:09:04.367
But there's no charge for catching this thief, she said.

02:09:04.427 --> 02:09:08.729
My new dog is a better reward.

02:09:08.789 --> 02:09:12.010
Unit 23.

02:09:12.070 --> 02:09:18.104
Word List Advance To advance is to go forward.

02:09:18.164 --> 02:09:21.669
He advanced up the ladder slowly.

02:09:21.729 --> 02:09:23.814
Athlete.

02:09:23.874 --> 02:09:27.196
An athlete is a person who plays sports.

02:09:27.255 --> 02:09:32.079
Some athletes can play many sports very well.

02:09:32.139 --> 02:09:34.240
Average.

02:09:34.300 --> 02:09:37.923
If something is average, it is at a normal level.

02:09:37.982 --> 02:09:40.044
I'm not rich or poor.

02:09:40.104 --> 02:09:42.115
I'm average.

02:09:42.175 --> 02:09:44.346
Behavior.

02:09:44.406 --> 02:09:47.258
Your behavior is the way you act.

02:09:47.318 --> 02:09:50.380
Their behavior was good this semester.

02:09:50.440 --> 02:09:52.888
They didn't cause trouble.

02:09:52.948 --> 02:09:55.095
Behind.

02:09:55.155 --> 02:09:58.426
Behind means to be at the back of something.

02:09:58.486 --> 02:10:02.736
The little girl was hiding behind a tree.

02:10:02.796 --> 02:10:04.847
Course.

02:10:04.907 --> 02:10:07.898
A course is a class in school.

02:10:07.957 --> 02:10:12.048
I took a PE course in school this year.

02:10:12.108 --> 02:10:14.119
Lower.

02:10:14.179 --> 02:10:17.439
To lower something is to make it go down.

02:10:17.499 --> 02:10:22.814
The chart shows how his production has lowered over the year.

02:10:22.874 --> 02:10:24.938
Match.

02:10:24.998 --> 02:10:28.501
To match is to be the same or similar.

02:10:28.562 --> 02:10:30.693
The two shoes matched.

02:10:30.753 --> 02:10:33.034
They look the same.

02:10:33.094 --> 02:10:35.186
Member.

02:10:35.246 --> 02:10:38.488
A member is a person who is part of a group.

02:10:38.548 --> 02:10:42.972
Julie is the newest member of our team.

02:10:43.032 --> 02:10:45.144
Mental.

02:10:45.204 --> 02:10:48.796
If something is mental, it has to do with your mind.

02:10:48.856 --> 02:10:52.576
I made a mental picture of the room.

02:10:52.636 --> 02:11:00.188
Passenger A passenger is a person who rides in a car, train, or airplane.

02:11:00.247 --> 02:11:04.840
One passenger was standing in the subway train.

02:11:04.900 --> 02:11:11.605
Personality Your personality is what you are like and how you behave.

02:11:11.665 --> 02:11:15.268
John has a bad personality.

02:11:15.327 --> 02:11:20.350
Poem A poem is a short kind of writing.

02:11:20.410 --> 02:11:24.717
William Shakespeare wrote many poems.

02:11:24.777 --> 02:11:32.306
A pole is a long, thin stick made of wood or metal that supports things.

02:11:32.366 --> 02:11:36.438
The flag was hanging from the flagpole.

02:11:36.498 --> 02:11:38.620
Remove.

02:11:38.680 --> 02:11:41.872
To remove something is to take it away.

02:11:41.932 --> 02:11:45.485
I remove the nail from the board.

02:11:45.545 --> 02:11:47.696
Safety.

02:11:47.756 --> 02:11:52.700
Safety means to be the condition of being safe and free from danger.

02:11:52.760 --> 02:11:57.602
For his own safety, he was placed in a car seat.

02:11:57.662 --> 02:11:59.574
Shoot.

02:11:59.634 --> 02:12:04.778
To shoot is to fire something like a bullet at someone or something.

02:12:04.838 --> 02:12:09.522
The hunter raised his gun to shoot at the target.

02:12:09.582 --> 02:12:11.654
Sound.

02:12:11.714 --> 02:12:14.596
To sound means to make a noise.

02:12:14.656 --> 02:12:19.197
The alarm clock sounded and woke us all up.

02:12:19.257 --> 02:12:21.306
Swim.

02:12:21.366 --> 02:12:24.398
To swim is to move through water.

02:12:24.458 --> 02:12:28.130
I love to swim in the ocean.

02:12:28.190 --> 02:12:30.272
Web.

02:12:30.332 --> 02:12:33.644
A web is a home made by a spider.

02:12:33.704 --> 02:12:38.927
Mom cleaned the spider webs out of the garage.

02:12:38.986 --> 02:12:41.919
The camp.

02:12:41.979 --> 02:12:50.492
Stacey wanted to stay at a nice hotel for vacation, but her parents sent her to a terrible camp instead.

02:12:50.552 --> 02:12:57.233
For breakfast, Stacey liked fresh juice and chocolate milk, but she got water at the camp.

02:12:57.293 --> 02:13:02.474
In the afternoon, she wanted to write poems, but she had to swim.

02:13:02.534 --> 02:13:06.055
The camp was near an airport with loud planes.

02:13:06.115 --> 02:13:08.676
Spiderwebs hung over her bed.

02:13:08.736 --> 02:13:13.080
To her, the kid's average behavior was very bad.

02:13:13.140 --> 02:13:15.872
No girl matched her personality.

02:13:15.932 --> 02:13:17.193
She hated it.

02:13:17.253 --> 02:13:19.474
One day, they had a class.

02:13:19.534 --> 02:13:25.530
Mental exercise sounded good to Stacy, but it was a course on water safety.

02:13:25.590 --> 02:13:28.832
They learned how to be safe passengers on a boat.

02:13:28.892 --> 02:13:32.075
Stacy didn't ever plan to go on a boat.

02:13:32.135 --> 02:13:34.961
The next day, they played a game.

02:13:35.021 --> 02:13:38.216
There were a red team and a blue team.

02:13:38.276 --> 02:13:40.677
Stacy was on the blue team.

02:13:40.737 --> 02:13:45.720
Each team had to try to remove the other team's flag from a pole.

02:13:45.780 --> 02:13:48.560
They also had to use water guns.

02:13:48.620 --> 02:13:53.923
I'm not much of an athlete, she said, but she still had to play.

02:13:53.983 --> 02:13:57.905
Stacy took a water gun and looked for somewhere to hide.

02:13:57.965 --> 02:14:01.616
A boy said, Stacy, you advance to the middle.

02:14:01.676 --> 02:14:03.067
I will go right.

02:14:03.127 --> 02:14:05.238
Those two will go left.

02:14:05.298 --> 02:14:07.749
Stacy still didn't want to play.

02:14:07.809 --> 02:14:11.981
She walked into the forest and saw a red team player coming.

02:14:12.041 --> 02:14:16.944
Stacy hid behind a tree and then jumped out and shot the other player.

02:14:17.004 --> 02:14:19.865
This is fun, Stacy thought.

02:14:19.925 --> 02:14:24.908
Several minutes after advancing further, Stacy saw the red flag.

02:14:24.968 --> 02:14:27.639
A red team member was watching over it.

02:14:27.699 --> 02:14:29.770
She shot him with her water gun.

02:14:29.830 --> 02:14:33.333
Then she lowered the flag and ran back to her team.

02:14:33.393 --> 02:14:35.464
I got it, she yelled.

02:14:35.524 --> 02:14:37.216
The blue team won.

02:14:37.276 --> 02:14:39.118
Stacey was the hero.

02:14:39.178 --> 02:14:42.300
For the rest of the week, Stacey had fun.

02:14:42.360 --> 02:14:50.970
She even made new friends.

02:14:51.030 --> 02:15:01.090
Unit 24. Word List. Block. I saw a block of ice on the floor.

02:15:01.150 --> 02:15:03.162
Cheer.

02:15:03.222 --> 02:15:07.804
To cheer is to give a loud shout of approval or encouragement.

02:15:07.865 --> 02:15:12.338
The crowd all cheered when the home team won.

02:15:12.398 --> 02:15:14.710
Complex.

02:15:14.770 --> 02:15:18.362
If something is complex, it has many small parts.

02:15:18.422 --> 02:15:19.904
It is hard to understand.

02:15:19.924 --> 02:15:27.180
A jigsaw puzzle can be complex because it has so many pieces.

02:15:27.240 --> 02:15:40.004
A critic is someone who gives their opinions about movies, books, plays, etc. The wine critic tasted the wine, so he could give his opinion.

02:15:40.064 --> 02:15:46.706
Event An event is something that happens, especially something important.

02:15:46.766 --> 02:15:51.514
Finishing high school was a major event in his life.

02:15:51.574 --> 02:15:53.789
Exercise.

02:15:53.849 --> 02:15:58.660
Two exercises to run or play sports so that you can be healthy.

02:15:58.720 --> 02:16:02.342
You should exercise every day.

02:16:02.402 --> 02:16:04.302
Fit.

02:16:04.362 --> 02:16:09.194
If something fits, it is small enough or the right size to go there.

02:16:09.254 --> 02:16:13.464
The colorful eggs fit into the box.

02:16:13.524 --> 02:16:15.595
Friendship.

02:16:15.655 --> 02:16:19.696
Friendship is the relationship between people who are friends.

02:16:19.755 --> 02:16:24.998
Michael and Lisa have a very strong friendship with each other.

02:16:25.058 --> 02:16:30.370
Guide A guide is someone who shows you where to go.

02:16:30.430 --> 02:16:34.062
We followed a guide at the park.

02:16:34.121 --> 02:16:39.884
Lack If there is a lack of something, there is not enough of it.

02:16:39.944 --> 02:16:43.996
His only problem is a lack of money.

02:16:44.057 --> 02:16:51.443
Passage A passage is a long area with walls that goes from one place to another.

02:16:51.503 --> 02:16:56.474
The long passage led us to the other side of the field.

02:16:56.534 --> 02:16:58.644
Perform.

02:16:58.704 --> 02:17:02.735
To perform is to do something in front of people who watch.

02:17:02.795 --> 02:17:06.796
He will perform a song for the class.

02:17:06.856 --> 02:17:08.866
Pressure.

02:17:08.926 --> 02:17:12.557
Pressure is what you apply to make someone do something.

02:17:12.617 --> 02:17:17.756
They put pressure on him to change his mind.

02:17:17.817 --> 02:17:22.657
If something is probable, it is likely to happen.

02:17:22.718 --> 02:17:28.451
It is probable that you will get a good grade if you study for the test.

02:17:28.511 --> 02:17:30.512
Public.

02:17:30.572 --> 02:17:34.686
If something is public, it is meant for everyone to use.

02:17:34.746 --> 02:17:39.188
I went to the public park to play with my friends.

02:17:39.248 --> 02:17:41.240
Strike.

02:17:41.299 --> 02:17:44.712
To strike someone or something is to hit them.

02:17:44.772 --> 02:17:48.665
She struck the other girl in the face.

02:17:48.725 --> 02:17:55.409
Support To support something is to like it and help it be successful.

02:17:55.469 --> 02:17:59.740
Everyone at work supports the new plan.

02:17:59.801 --> 02:18:05.264
Task A task is work that someone has to do.

02:18:05.324 --> 02:18:09.515
Who has the task of building the brick wall?

02:18:09.576 --> 02:18:14.408
Term A term is a word for something.

02:18:14.468 --> 02:18:19.428
I often use the term oops when I make a mistake.

02:18:19.487 --> 02:18:21.506
Unite.

02:18:21.567 --> 02:18:25.071
To unite is to get together to do something.

02:18:25.131 --> 02:18:30.729
If we unite we can finish our project faster.

02:18:30.789 --> 02:18:34.203
A strong friendship.

02:18:34.263 --> 02:18:37.274
Tim was the strongest man in the town.

02:18:37.334 --> 02:18:40.386
When he played sports, he always won.

02:18:40.446 --> 02:18:43.977
He performed and exercised in the public park.

02:18:44.038 --> 02:18:47.139
He did this to show everyone how strong he was.

02:18:47.199 --> 02:18:50.611
Most people liked him, but one man didn't.

02:18:50.671 --> 02:18:52.262
His name was Jack.

02:18:52.322 --> 02:18:53.942
Jack hated Tim.

02:18:54.003 --> 02:18:57.464
Jack was a movie critic and the smartest man in town.

02:18:57.525 --> 02:19:01.816
He could solve complex math problems, but no one cared.

02:19:01.876 --> 02:19:04.508
Jack wanted to be famous like Tim.

02:19:04.568 --> 02:19:07.700
One day, there was an unusual event.

02:19:07.760 --> 02:19:10.021
A big storm came suddenly.

02:19:10.082 --> 02:19:12.042
Snow covered the town.

02:19:12.103 --> 02:19:13.944
No one could get out.

02:19:14.004 --> 02:19:15.595
They needed food.

02:19:15.655 --> 02:19:19.868
The people said, this is a task for a strong man.

02:19:19.928 --> 02:19:22.479
Tim was under pressure to save them.

02:19:22.540 --> 02:19:26.122
But Jack wanted to be the hero, so they both went.

02:19:26.182 --> 02:19:30.267
Tim said, you can't help because of your lack of strength.

02:19:30.327 --> 02:19:33.670
but Jack found some small passages under the snow.

02:19:33.730 --> 02:19:36.321
One of them led toward another town.

02:19:36.381 --> 02:19:38.282
That town had food.

02:19:38.342 --> 02:19:42.853
Because Tim was so big and strong, he almost couldn't fit inside.

02:19:42.914 --> 02:19:45.965
They walked until there was a block of ice in their way.

02:19:46.025 --> 02:19:48.906
Jack said, we can't get past it.

02:19:48.966 --> 02:19:51.197
But if you strike it, it might break.

02:19:51.257 --> 02:19:53.338
Tim knew that was probable.

02:19:53.398 --> 02:19:54.787
He broke it.

02:19:54.847 --> 02:19:58.218
When there were more ice blocks, Tim broke them.

02:19:58.278 --> 02:19:59.910
That made him tired.

02:19:59.970 --> 02:20:01.881
He couldn't walk anymore.

02:20:01.941 --> 02:20:05.593
Jack said, let's unite and support each other.

02:20:05.654 --> 02:20:07.395
I'll get the food alone.

02:20:07.455 --> 02:20:08.956
You rest here.

02:20:09.016 --> 02:20:11.078
Jack came back with food.

02:20:11.138 --> 02:20:13.990
Tim couldn't remember which passage led home.

02:20:14.050 --> 02:20:16.400
He needed Jack to be his guide.

02:20:16.460 --> 02:20:19.532
The men became friends by working together.

02:20:19.592 --> 02:20:23.304
In town, people saw Jack with the food and cheered.

02:20:23.364 --> 02:20:25.296
They called Jack a hero.

02:20:25.356 --> 02:20:27.076
But Jack didn't care.

02:20:27.136 --> 02:20:29.258
He was thinking of something else.

02:20:29.318 --> 02:20:34.752
He said to Tim, I thought I was smart, but I learned a new term today.

02:20:34.812 --> 02:20:37.734
Friendship.

02:20:37.794 --> 02:20:40.926
Unit 25.

02:20:40.986 --> 02:20:42.446
Word list.

02:20:42.506 --> 02:20:44.272
Associate.

02:20:44.332 --> 02:20:48.747
To associate means to connect something with a person or thing.

02:20:48.807 --> 02:20:54.070
Most people associate birthday parties with having fun.

02:20:54.130 --> 02:21:00.353
Environment The environment is the place where people work or live.

02:21:00.413 --> 02:21:05.516
Keeping our environment clean is important to our health.

02:21:05.576 --> 02:21:12.097
Factory A factory is a building where things are made or put together.

02:21:12.157 --> 02:21:16.636
We have only one factory in our town.

02:21:16.696 --> 02:21:21.938
Feature A feature is an important part of something.

02:21:21.998 --> 02:21:25.779
The cell phone has many features.

02:21:25.839 --> 02:21:31.160
Instance An instance is an example of something.

02:21:31.220 --> 02:21:34.712
I have never experienced an instance of hate.

02:21:34.772 --> 02:21:36.582
Have you?

02:21:36.642 --> 02:21:42.724
Involve To involve means to be actively taking part in something.

02:21:42.784 --> 02:21:47.425
The whole family was involved in playing the game.

02:21:47.485 --> 02:21:54.178
Medicine Medicine is something you take to feel better or treat an illness.

02:21:54.239 --> 02:21:58.390
The doctor gave me medicine for my called.

02:21:58.450 --> 02:22:03.592
Mix A mix is different things put together.

02:22:03.652 --> 02:22:09.269
The green mix we made in science class spilled onto the table.

02:22:09.329 --> 02:22:11.443
Organize.

02:22:11.503 --> 02:22:15.894
To organize is to plan or get ready for an event.

02:22:15.954 --> 02:22:22.996
Make a list to help you organize the things you need.

02:22:23.056 --> 02:22:26.757
A period is an amount of time when something happens.

02:22:26.817 --> 02:22:33.829
In one period in Europe, there were many nights.

02:22:33.889 --> 02:22:37.469
If people populate an area, they live there.

02:22:37.529 --> 02:22:40.460
Billions of people populate the Earth.

02:22:40.480 --> 02:22:43.723
To produce.

02:22:43.783 --> 02:22:47.146
To produce something is to make or grow it.

02:22:47.206 --> 02:22:51.640
This tree produces apples every year.

02:22:51.700 --> 02:22:53.832
Range.

02:22:53.892 --> 02:22:57.786
A range is a number or a set of similar things.

02:22:57.846 --> 02:23:01.882
I saw a range of cars to choose from.

02:23:01.942 --> 02:23:04.217
Recognize.

02:23:04.278 --> 02:23:08.722
To recognize something is to know it because you have seen it before.

02:23:08.782 --> 02:23:13.776
I recognized an old friend for many years ago.

02:23:13.836 --> 02:23:15.968
Regular.

02:23:16.028 --> 02:23:21.294
If something is regular, it happens often and in equal amounts of time.

02:23:21.354 --> 02:23:25.642
Our regular lunch time is around noon.

02:23:25.702 --> 02:23:58.702
sign a sign is a notice giving information directions a warning etc the sign indicated that today would be a bad day tip a tip is a pointed end of something the tip of his pen was very sharp tradition a tradition is something people have been doing for a long time Marriage is a tradition all over the world.

02:23:58.762 --> 02:24:00.832
Trash.

02:24:00.892 --> 02:24:05.466
Trash is waste material or unwanted or worthless things.

02:24:05.526 --> 02:24:07.627
Please take out the trash.

02:24:07.687 --> 02:24:09.809
It smells bad.

02:24:09.868 --> 02:24:11.900
Wide.

02:24:11.960 --> 02:24:16.182
If something is wide, it is large from side to side.

02:24:16.242 --> 02:24:20.885
The door was as wide as my arms.

02:24:20.945 --> 02:24:24.265
Joe's Pond.

02:24:24.325 --> 02:24:27.474
Joe made the world a better place.

02:24:27.534 --> 02:24:30.575
He got the idea to do that at school.

02:24:30.635 --> 02:24:32.746
He watched a video there.

02:24:32.806 --> 02:24:34.786
It was about a factory.

02:24:34.846 --> 02:24:39.498
This factory produced a lot of trash and put it in a river.

02:24:39.558 --> 02:24:42.528
The trash and water were a bad mix.

02:24:42.588 --> 02:24:46.990
People populated the area by the river and drank its water.

02:24:47.050 --> 02:24:48.850
This made them sick.

02:24:48.910 --> 02:24:53.442
Many of them needed medicine and made regular visits to doctors.

02:24:53.502 --> 02:24:56.213
But the video wasn't all bad news.

02:24:56.273 --> 02:25:00.574
It showed ways to pick up trash and why it's important to do this.

02:25:00.634 --> 02:25:04.065
It said people can make a difference to their environment.

02:25:04.125 --> 02:25:09.607
The video's important features made Joe associate trash with hurting people.

02:25:09.667 --> 02:25:12.398
One day, Joe walked through a park.

02:25:12.458 --> 02:25:15.769
He recognized some of the problems from the video.

02:25:15.829 --> 02:25:19.800
One instance of these problems was the trash in the pond.

02:25:19.860 --> 02:25:21.901
It was full of plastic cups.

02:25:21.961 --> 02:25:23.862
There was too much trash.

02:25:23.922 --> 02:25:26.452
Joe didn't want it to hurt anyone.

02:25:26.512 --> 02:25:29.423
He told his grandfather about the park.

02:25:29.483 --> 02:25:35.005
His grandfather said, you know, it's a tradition in our family to help people.

02:25:35.065 --> 02:25:37.956
That's why we give food to poor people.

02:25:38.016 --> 02:25:41.307
Maybe you can help people by cleaning the park.

02:25:41.367 --> 02:25:44.489
Cleaning the bark would involve hard work.

02:25:44.549 --> 02:25:47.912
Joe decided to organize a group to help him.

02:25:47.972 --> 02:25:50.724
He chose a wide area of the bark.

02:25:50.784 --> 02:25:52.765
It had the most trash.

02:25:52.825 --> 02:25:55.576
He asked his family and friends to come.

02:25:55.636 --> 02:25:59.169
On Saturday, he gave everyone a sharp stick.

02:25:59.229 --> 02:26:00.710
They wondered why.

02:26:00.770 --> 02:26:04.703
He said, you use the stick's tip to pick up trash.

02:26:04.763 --> 02:26:06.414
This makes it easier.

02:26:06.474 --> 02:26:08.436
They worked for six weeks.

02:26:08.496 --> 02:26:10.797
Different people helped each time.

02:26:10.857 --> 02:26:13.089
But Joe was always there.

02:26:13.149 --> 02:26:17.342
In that period of time, Joe saw a range of results.

02:26:17.402 --> 02:26:19.664
There was no trash in the water.

02:26:19.724 --> 02:26:21.446
People could swim in it.

02:26:21.507 --> 02:26:24.068
Joe knew that was a good sign.

02:26:24.128 --> 02:26:29.173
He was happy because he helped his environment.

02:26:29.233 --> 02:26:32.366
Unit 26.

02:26:32.426 --> 02:26:38.742
Word List Advice Advice is an opinion about what to do.

02:26:38.802 --> 02:26:41.845
I don't know how to study for my exams.

02:26:41.905 --> 02:26:44.776
Can you give me some advice?

02:26:44.836 --> 02:26:46.967
Along.

02:26:47.027 --> 02:26:53.010
Along means to move from one part of a road, river, etc. to another.

02:26:53.070 --> 02:26:59.322
Walk along this tunnel for 10 minutes and you'll see a door on the left.

02:26:59.382 --> 02:27:01.574
Attention.

02:27:01.634 --> 02:27:06.189
Attention is the notice, thought, or consideration of someone.

02:27:06.249 --> 02:27:11.206
His work got the attention of two of his coworkers.

02:27:11.266 --> 02:27:13.328
Attract.

02:27:13.388 --> 02:27:18.691
To attract means to make a person or thing come closer or be interested.

02:27:18.751 --> 02:27:22.193
The magnet attracted the metal.

02:27:22.253 --> 02:27:24.324
Climb.

02:27:24.384 --> 02:27:29.368
To climb means to use your hands and feet to go up on something.

02:27:29.428 --> 02:27:33.431
The girls climbed to the top of the mountain.

02:27:33.491 --> 02:27:35.482
Drop.

02:27:35.542 --> 02:27:39.504
To drop is to fall or allow something to fall.

02:27:39.564 --> 02:27:44.058
A small amount of water dropped from the bottle.

02:27:44.118 --> 02:27:46.158
Final.

02:27:46.218 --> 02:27:49.630
If something is final, it is the last part.

02:27:49.690 --> 02:27:55.434
In the final part of the film, the man and the woman got married.

02:27:55.494 --> 02:27:57.515
Further.

02:27:57.575 --> 02:28:01.818
Further is used to say something is from a distance or time.

02:28:01.878 --> 02:28:08.692
The escalator is further along than I thought.

02:28:08.752 --> 02:28:12.574
To imply something is to suggest it without saying it.

02:28:12.634 --> 02:28:20.258
The man implied that he wanted the job, but he didn't say so.

02:28:20.318 --> 02:28:23.950
To maintain means to make something stay the same.

02:28:24.010 --> 02:28:28.002
The balls maintain constant movement.

02:28:28.062 --> 02:28:30.150
Neither.

02:28:30.210 --> 02:28:34.148
You use neither to connect two negative statements.

02:28:34.208 --> 02:28:40.640
Neither the pass on the left nor the pass on the right will lead us home.

02:28:40.700 --> 02:28:42.920
Otherwise.

02:28:42.980 --> 02:28:46.852
Otherwise means different or in another way.

02:28:46.912 --> 02:28:49.062
It's good to stay active.

02:28:49.122 --> 02:28:51.973
Otherwise you'll gain weight.

02:28:52.033 --> 02:28:59.198
Physical If something is physical, it is related to your body and not your mind.

02:28:59.258 --> 02:29:03.052
Biking is good for your physical health.

02:29:03.112 --> 02:29:05.144
Prove.

02:29:05.204 --> 02:29:08.646
To prove something is to show that it is true.

02:29:08.706 --> 02:29:12.908
My teacher proved the answer on the board.

02:29:12.968 --> 02:29:15.130
React.

02:29:15.190 --> 02:29:20.302
To react is to act in a certain way because of something that happened.

02:29:20.363 --> 02:29:24.192
James reacted badly to the news.

02:29:24.252 --> 02:29:26.350
Ride.

02:29:26.410 --> 02:29:29.532
To ride something is to travel on it.

02:29:29.592 --> 02:29:38.106
You can ride an animal, a bike, etc. I will ride a roller coaster for the first time today.

02:29:38.166 --> 02:29:40.376
Situated.

02:29:40.436 --> 02:29:44.618
If something is situated somewhere, it is in that place.

02:29:44.678 --> 02:29:49.041
The whiteboard is situated between the two men.

02:29:49.100 --> 02:29:51.382
Society.

02:29:51.442 --> 02:29:55.436
Society is people and the way that they live.

02:29:55.496 --> 02:30:00.210
Society expects people to be good and honest.

02:30:00.270 --> 02:30:02.352
Standard.

02:30:02.412 --> 02:30:06.524
A standard is what people consider normal or good.

02:30:06.584 --> 02:30:11.998
This older model TV is below our store standards.

02:30:12.059 --> 02:30:14.220
Suggest.

02:30:14.280 --> 02:30:18.832
To suggest something means to give an idea or plan about it.

02:30:18.892 --> 02:30:23.702
He suggested that we go to see his boss.

02:30:23.762 --> 02:30:27.310
Archie and his donkey.

02:30:27.370 --> 02:30:29.781
Old Archie needed some money.

02:30:29.841 --> 02:30:32.062
He decided to sell his donkey.

02:30:32.122 --> 02:30:34.804
So he and his son Tom went to town.

02:30:34.864 --> 02:30:37.596
It was situated many miles away.

02:30:37.656 --> 02:30:40.088
Soon, they met a woman.

02:30:40.148 --> 02:30:41.678
Where are you going?

02:30:41.738 --> 02:30:42.809
She asked.

02:30:42.869 --> 02:30:45.170
To town, said Archie.

02:30:45.230 --> 02:30:49.096
Any smart person would ride the donkey, she said.

02:30:49.157 --> 02:30:50.872
What are you implying?"

02:30:50.932 --> 02:30:52.075
Archie asked.

02:30:52.135 --> 02:30:53.759
I'm very smart.

02:30:53.819 --> 02:30:55.853
Archie wanted to look smart.

02:30:55.913 --> 02:30:58.278
So he climbed onto the donkey.

02:30:58.338 --> 02:31:01.380
Then they continued in the direction of the town.

02:31:01.440 --> 02:31:04.679
Further along the road, they met a farmer.

02:31:04.739 --> 02:31:06.510
Hello, said Archie.

02:31:06.570 --> 02:31:08.560
We want to sell this donkey.

02:31:08.620 --> 02:31:10.211
Do you want to buy it?

02:31:10.271 --> 02:31:13.422
I don't need a donkey, said the farmer.

02:31:13.482 --> 02:31:16.734
But if you want my advice, don't ride it.

02:31:16.794 --> 02:31:19.705
The donkey needs to be in good physical condition.

02:31:19.765 --> 02:31:22.046
Good idea, said Archie.

02:31:22.106 --> 02:31:24.157
Tom, I want you to ride it.

02:31:24.217 --> 02:31:25.507
You're lighter.

02:31:25.567 --> 02:31:28.689
Neither you nor your son should ride it.

02:31:28.749 --> 02:31:30.480
It looks very tired.

02:31:30.541 --> 02:31:34.133
You should carry the donkey, suggested the farmer.

02:31:34.193 --> 02:31:36.284
You're right, said Archie.

02:31:36.344 --> 02:31:37.686
Come on, Tom.

02:31:37.746 --> 02:31:40.178
We'll carry it for the final few miles.

02:31:40.238 --> 02:31:44.691
The donkey was very heavy, and they couldn't maintain a good speed.

02:31:44.751 --> 02:31:47.398
They didn't arrive until late in the evening.

02:31:47.458 --> 02:31:50.325
At last, they walked into the town.

02:31:50.385 --> 02:31:53.818
But there they attracted the attention of some teenage boys.

02:31:53.878 --> 02:31:56.020
They laughed at Tom and Archie.

02:31:56.080 --> 02:31:58.301
They started to throw stones at them.

02:31:58.361 --> 02:32:00.622
The donkey reacted by kicking.

02:32:00.682 --> 02:32:03.224
Tom and Archie dropped the donkey.

02:32:03.284 --> 02:32:06.338
It fell on the ground, and they ran away.

02:32:06.398 --> 02:32:08.498
Archie lost his donkey.

02:32:08.559 --> 02:32:10.880
He went home with no money.

02:32:10.940 --> 02:32:13.302
What does this story teach us?

02:32:13.363 --> 02:32:16.673
We cannot please everyone in our society.

02:32:16.734 --> 02:32:19.063
Don't take everyone's advice.

02:32:19.123 --> 02:32:21.054
But set your own standards.

02:32:21.114 --> 02:32:24.805
Prove to everyone that you can make decisions by yourself.

02:32:24.866 --> 02:32:30.128
Otherwise, you may end up with nothing at all.

02:32:30.188 --> 02:32:33.360
Unit 27.

02:32:33.420 --> 02:32:34.940
Word list.

02:32:35.000 --> 02:32:36.652
Actually.

02:32:36.712 --> 02:32:40.103
Actually means, in fact, or really.

02:32:40.163 --> 02:32:45.702
My dad looks a little mean, but actually, he's very kind.

02:32:45.762 --> 02:32:47.900
Bite.

02:32:47.961 --> 02:32:53.302
Bite is the act of using your teeth to cut and tear into something.

02:32:53.362 --> 02:32:57.734
The boy took a big bite out of his hamburger.

02:32:57.794 --> 02:32:59.794
Coast.

02:32:59.854 --> 02:33:03.276
The coast is the land by an ocean.

02:33:03.336 --> 02:33:07.408
I stayed on the southern coast of Australia.

02:33:07.468 --> 02:33:09.518
Deal.

02:33:09.578 --> 02:33:13.238
A deal is an agreement that you have with another person.

02:33:13.298 --> 02:33:18.270
I made a deal with the other company to give us some money.

02:33:18.330 --> 02:33:20.422
Desert.

02:33:20.482 --> 02:33:25.044
The desert is an area of land without many plants or water.

02:33:25.104 --> 02:33:29.135
Not many plants grow in the desert.

02:33:29.196 --> 02:33:31.347
Earthquake.

02:33:31.407 --> 02:33:34.778
An earthquake is a shaking movement of the ground.

02:33:34.838 --> 02:33:38.751
The building shook during the earthquake.

02:33:38.811 --> 02:33:40.932
Effective.

02:33:40.992 --> 02:33:44.346
If something is effective, it works well.

02:33:44.406 --> 02:33:48.689
Swimming is an effective way to stay healthy.

02:33:48.749 --> 02:33:50.850
Examine.

02:33:50.910 --> 02:33:54.453
To examine something is to look at it carefully.

02:33:54.513 --> 02:33:58.306
The doctor examined my eyes today.

02:33:58.366 --> 02:34:00.418
False.

02:34:00.478 --> 02:34:03.940
If something is false, it is not correct.

02:34:04.000 --> 02:34:09.726
If you think the answer is false, press the red button.

02:34:09.786 --> 02:34:13.960
A gift is something you give someone.

02:34:14.020 --> 02:34:18.202
Dave received many gifts for Christmas.

02:34:18.262 --> 02:34:20.334
Hunger.

02:34:20.394 --> 02:34:23.916
Hunger is the feeling that you get when you need to eat.

02:34:23.976 --> 02:34:28.938
After playing all day long, he was filled with hunger.

02:34:28.998 --> 02:34:31.099
Imagine.

02:34:31.159 --> 02:34:34.971
To imagine something is to think of it in your mind.

02:34:35.031 --> 02:34:39.696
Sally imagined herself winning lots of money.

02:34:39.756 --> 02:34:41.858
Journey.

02:34:41.918 --> 02:34:44.631
A journey is a long trip.

02:34:44.691 --> 02:34:49.555
I went on a journey across the country with my parents.

02:34:49.615 --> 02:34:51.696
Puzzle.

02:34:51.756 --> 02:34:55.360
A puzzle is something that is hard to understand.

02:34:55.420 --> 02:34:59.062
The question was a puzzle to him.

02:34:59.122 --> 02:35:01.114
Quite.

02:35:01.174 --> 02:35:05.838
Quite is used to say that something is complete or very much.

02:35:05.898 --> 02:35:10.249
I think typing on a keyboard is quite easy.

02:35:10.309 --> 02:35:12.398
Rather.

02:35:12.458 --> 02:35:16.810
Rather is used when you want to do one thing but not the other.

02:35:16.869 --> 02:35:21.220
I would rather have the red one than the blue one.

02:35:21.280 --> 02:35:23.551
Specific.

02:35:23.611 --> 02:35:27.742
If something is specific, it is precise or exact.

02:35:27.802 --> 02:35:32.054
Please choose a specific place on the map.

02:35:32.114 --> 02:35:34.104
Tour.

02:35:34.164 --> 02:35:38.155
A tour is a short trip in which you see many sites.

02:35:38.215 --> 02:35:42.789
I took a tour of Asia and Europe.

02:35:42.849 --> 02:35:47.253
A trip is a journey to a certain place.

02:35:47.314 --> 02:35:51.256
Can take a trip to the city yesterday.

02:35:51.316 --> 02:35:53.407
Value.

02:35:53.466 --> 02:35:57.108
If something has value, it is worth a lot of money.

02:35:57.168 --> 02:36:02.311
Matthew found a treasure of very high value.

02:36:02.371 --> 02:36:06.263
The spider and the bird.

02:36:06.323 --> 02:36:09.516
There was once a very big spider.

02:36:09.576 --> 02:36:13.238
If a bug got into his web, he would examine it.

02:36:13.298 --> 02:36:16.782
However, he didn't eat the bug right away.

02:36:16.842 --> 02:36:19.694
He asked the bug a question first.

02:36:19.754 --> 02:36:22.597
It was always quite a difficult puzzle.

02:36:22.657 --> 02:36:26.240
If the bug's answer was correct, he let it go.

02:36:26.300 --> 02:36:28.312
If not, he ate it.

02:36:28.372 --> 02:36:33.225
One day, a small bird on a journey flew into the spider's web.

02:36:33.285 --> 02:36:36.337
The spider couldn't imagine eating a bird.

02:36:36.397 --> 02:36:40.230
It was so big, but his hunger was too great.

02:36:40.290 --> 02:36:45.763
He said to the bird, if you cannot give me a specific answer, I will eat you.

02:36:45.823 --> 02:36:47.364
The bird laughed.

02:36:47.425 --> 02:36:48.906
I could eat you.

02:36:48.966 --> 02:36:51.478
But the bird was actually scared.

02:36:51.538 --> 02:36:55.372
She had used all her energy trying to get out of the web.

02:36:55.432 --> 02:37:00.036
And a spider's bite can be very effective in killing animals.

02:37:00.096 --> 02:37:02.717
Please don't eat me, the bird said.

02:37:02.778 --> 02:37:05.199
I would rather make a deal with you.

02:37:05.260 --> 02:37:07.321
Okay," the spider said.

02:37:07.381 --> 02:37:10.512
If your answer is right, I will let you go.

02:37:10.572 --> 02:37:13.114
If not, you must give me a gift.

02:37:13.174 --> 02:37:15.725
It must be something of great value.

02:37:15.785 --> 02:37:19.407
The bird said, you can pick anything you want to eat.

02:37:19.467 --> 02:37:21.128
I will find it for you.

02:37:21.188 --> 02:37:22.838
The spider agreed.

02:37:22.899 --> 02:37:25.400
Where can you take a trip to the coast?

02:37:25.460 --> 02:37:29.912
The desert and the mountains at the same time, the spider asked.

02:37:29.972 --> 02:37:33.383
The bird asked, does this place have earthquakes?

02:37:33.443 --> 02:37:36.004
But the spider did not say anything.

02:37:36.064 --> 02:37:38.664
I can see those places when I fly.

02:37:38.724 --> 02:37:41.015
Is the sky the right answer?

02:37:41.075 --> 02:37:43.166
False said the spider.

02:37:43.226 --> 02:37:45.056
The answer is Hawaii.

02:37:45.116 --> 02:37:47.697
Now you must find some bugs for me.

02:37:47.757 --> 02:37:50.618
The spider climbed on the bird's back.

02:37:50.678 --> 02:37:53.188
They flew and ate bugs together.

02:37:53.248 --> 02:37:55.609
They took a tour of the forest.

02:37:55.669 --> 02:37:58.770
Then the bird took the spider home.

02:37:58.830 --> 02:38:06.484
From that day on, they were friends and they never tried to eat each other again.

02:38:06.544 --> 02:38:11.006
Unit 28, word list.

02:38:11.066 --> 02:38:12.676
Band.

02:38:12.736 --> 02:38:16.088
A band is a group of people who play music.

02:38:16.148 --> 02:38:19.630
My brother is in a rock band.

02:38:19.690 --> 02:38:21.791
Barely.

02:38:21.851 --> 02:38:26.106
Barely means by the smallest amount, almost not.

02:38:26.166 --> 02:38:31.033
I barely had enough money to pay for my bus ticket.

02:38:31.093 --> 02:38:33.184
Boring.

02:38:33.244 --> 02:38:36.596
If something is boring, it is not fun.

02:38:36.657 --> 02:38:40.189
I think the internet is boring.

02:38:40.249 --> 02:38:42.330
Cancel.

02:38:42.391 --> 02:38:48.544
To cancel means to decide that an event or a request will not happen.

02:38:48.604 --> 02:38:53.484
She canceled the rest of her plans because of the rain.

02:38:53.544 --> 02:39:00.602
Driveway A driveway is a short private road that leads to a person's home.

02:39:00.662 --> 02:39:05.194
The long driveway led us to their new house.

02:39:05.254 --> 02:39:18.928
Garbage Garbage is waste material like unwanted or spoiled food, bottles, paper, etc. The boy cleaned up the garbage around his house.

02:39:18.988 --> 02:39:26.207
Instrument An instrument is something designed to do a certain task, like music.

02:39:26.267 --> 02:39:30.648
My favorite musical instrument is the piano.

02:39:30.708 --> 02:39:37.790
List A list is a record of information printed with an item on each line.

02:39:37.850 --> 02:39:42.132
My mom makes a list of groceries to buy.

02:39:42.191 --> 02:39:47.722
Magic Magic is the power to do impossible things.

02:39:47.782 --> 02:39:53.104
The magician used magic to pull a rabbit out of his hat.

02:39:53.164 --> 02:39:59.225
Message A message is a set of words that you send to someone.

02:39:59.285 --> 02:40:03.526
I left a message for you in the envelope.

02:40:03.586 --> 02:40:05.687
Notice.

02:40:05.747 --> 02:40:09.328
To notice something is to see it for the first time.

02:40:09.388 --> 02:40:12.478
Did you notice the view?

02:40:12.538 --> 02:40:14.509
Own.

02:40:14.569 --> 02:40:17.416
To own something means to have it.

02:40:17.476 --> 02:40:19.604
That thing belongs to you.

02:40:19.664 --> 02:40:23.296
My grandfather owns that house.

02:40:23.356 --> 02:40:25.416
Predict.

02:40:25.476 --> 02:40:28.999
To predict something is to say that it will happen.

02:40:29.059 --> 02:40:33.261
She predicted that I would get married next year.

02:40:33.322 --> 02:40:35.474
Professor.

02:40:35.534 --> 02:40:39.106
A professor is a person who teaches in college.

02:40:39.166 --> 02:40:44.080
Mike Science Professor knows a lot about physics.

02:40:44.140 --> 02:40:51.078
Rush To rush is to go somewhere or do something very quickly.

02:40:51.137 --> 02:40:54.820
Nancy Rush to finish her homework.

02:40:54.880 --> 02:41:00.926
Schedule A schedule is a plan that tells you when to do things.

02:41:00.985 --> 02:41:04.698
What is your class schedule for today?

02:41:04.758 --> 02:41:10.884
Share To share something is to give some of it to another person.

02:41:10.944 --> 02:41:14.416
Jimmy shared his apple with me.

02:41:14.476 --> 02:41:21.870
Stage A stage is a place where actors or musicians act or sing.

02:41:21.930 --> 02:41:25.722
A large screen was on the stage.

02:41:25.782 --> 02:41:30.654
Storm A storm is very bad weather.

02:41:30.714 --> 02:41:33.186
There is a lot of rain or snow.

02:41:33.246 --> 02:41:37.378
Did that storm wake you up last night?

02:41:37.438 --> 02:41:43.976
Within You use within to say that something is inside another thing.

02:41:44.036 --> 02:41:48.606
Within the box, there was a pizza.

02:41:48.666 --> 02:41:54.355
The Party Cody's family moved to a new house.

02:41:54.415 --> 02:41:57.060
His dad got a new job as a professor.

02:41:57.120 --> 02:42:00.953
Cody liked his new tone, but he missed his grandparents.

02:42:01.013 --> 02:42:04.306
For his birthday, Cody wanted to have a party.

02:42:04.366 --> 02:42:08.638
His dad said, yes, we could even have a band play.

02:42:08.698 --> 02:42:12.781
On the day of the party, Cody woke up and rushed to get ready.

02:42:12.841 --> 02:42:15.602
He started to check his list of things to do.

02:42:15.662 --> 02:42:17.664
He was so excited.

02:42:17.724 --> 02:42:20.106
But then he noticed something terrible.

02:42:20.166 --> 02:42:23.593
There was snow on the ground and lots of it.

02:42:23.653 --> 02:42:26.089
Dad yelled.

02:42:26.149 --> 02:42:29.411
How can the band play their instruments outside?

02:42:29.471 --> 02:42:32.993
Dad said, we'll move the stage inside.

02:42:33.053 --> 02:42:38.155
It barely fit within the garage because there were some boxes and garbage there.

02:42:38.216 --> 02:42:41.568
But when they finished, they got a call from the band.

02:42:41.628 --> 02:42:44.169
They did not want to come in the snowstorm.

02:42:44.229 --> 02:42:47.869
Dad said, let's get someone to perform magic.

02:42:47.929 --> 02:42:50.649
But no one would come because of the snow.

02:42:50.709 --> 02:42:55.142
Finally Dad said, Cody, there's too much snow.

02:42:55.203 --> 02:42:57.284
We need to cancel the party.

02:42:57.344 --> 02:43:00.377
Yes sir, Cody said sadly.

02:43:00.437 --> 02:43:04.270
It's going to be a boring birthday, he predicted.

02:43:04.330 --> 02:43:07.202
Cody wanted to share his birthday with someone.

02:43:07.262 --> 02:43:09.634
He wanted to be at his old home.

02:43:09.694 --> 02:43:11.936
He wanted to see his grandparents.

02:43:11.996 --> 02:43:14.228
But then something got his attention.

02:43:14.288 --> 02:43:16.812
He noticed a car in the driveway.

02:43:16.872 --> 02:43:19.844
His grandparents owned a car like that.

02:43:19.904 --> 02:43:21.524
Cody was right.

02:43:21.584 --> 02:43:24.326
His grandparents came for his birthday.

02:43:24.386 --> 02:43:26.306
Happy birthday, Cody!

02:43:26.366 --> 02:43:29.897
We're sorry we're late, but there was so much snow.

02:43:29.957 --> 02:43:31.978
It made us go off schedule.

02:43:32.038 --> 02:43:34.619
We tried to leave a message to tell you.

02:43:34.679 --> 02:43:36.880
Cody told them what happened.

02:43:36.940 --> 02:43:39.611
I'm sorry, said Grandpa.

02:43:39.671 --> 02:43:42.302
I was sad, Cody said.

02:43:42.362 --> 02:43:44.072
But I'm not anymore.

02:43:44.132 --> 02:43:46.268
I'm so happy to see you.

02:43:46.328 --> 02:43:48.973
Dad brought out Cody's birthday treat.

02:43:49.033 --> 02:43:50.913
It was his favorite type.

02:43:50.974 --> 02:43:53.554
A Sunday with whipped cream on top.

02:43:53.614 --> 02:43:57.106
Then Cody told his grandparents about the new town.

02:43:57.166 --> 02:44:01.578
It was his best birthday ever.

02:44:01.638 --> 02:44:04.729
Unit 29.

02:44:04.789 --> 02:44:18.877
Word List Advertise To advertise is to tell people about something on TV, radio, etc. They used a rabbit to help them advertise their product.

02:44:18.937 --> 02:44:21.108
Assign.

02:44:21.168 --> 02:44:25.382
To assign something to someone is to tell them to do it.

02:44:25.442 --> 02:44:29.695
I assigned the worker an important task.

02:44:29.755 --> 02:44:31.856
Audience.

02:44:31.916 --> 02:44:36.400
An audience is a group of people who watch something together.

02:44:36.460 --> 02:44:40.393
There was a large audience at the game.

02:44:40.453 --> 02:44:42.624
Breakfast.

02:44:42.684 --> 02:44:45.708
Breakfast is the first meal of the day.

02:44:45.768 --> 02:44:49.831
I eat breakfast at 8 every morning.

02:44:49.891 --> 02:44:52.253
Competition.

02:44:52.313 --> 02:44:57.046
A competition is a contest to see who is the best at something.

02:44:57.106 --> 02:45:01.601
You want the running competition over the weekend.

02:45:01.661 --> 02:45:03.742
Cool.

02:45:03.802 --> 02:45:07.646
If the weather is cool, it is a little bit cold.

02:45:07.706 --> 02:45:11.324
The weather is cool in the fall.

02:45:11.384 --> 02:45:13.489
Gain.

02:45:13.549 --> 02:45:17.040
If you gain something, you get more of it.

02:45:17.100 --> 02:45:20.720
I gain some weight over the summer.

02:45:20.780 --> 02:45:23.031
Importance.

02:45:23.091 --> 02:45:28.392
Importance means the quality or condition of being needed or valued.

02:45:28.452 --> 02:45:32.993
The IPs are people of great importance.

02:45:33.053 --> 02:45:35.204
Knowledge.

02:45:35.264 --> 02:45:38.764
Knowledge is information that you have about something.

02:45:38.824 --> 02:45:43.292
A music teacher should have good knowledge of music.

02:45:43.352 --> 02:45:49.382
Major If something is major, it is big or important.

02:45:49.442 --> 02:45:51.763
I have a major problem.

02:45:51.823 --> 02:45:55.634
My boss wants me to redo my project.

02:45:55.694 --> 02:46:01.868
Mean Mean describes someone who is unkind or cruel.

02:46:01.928 --> 02:46:05.219
My coworker is a very mean person.

02:46:05.279 --> 02:46:08.320
He gets angry very quickly.

02:46:08.381 --> 02:46:14.699
Prefer If you prefer something, you want it more than something else.

02:46:14.759 --> 02:46:20.226
I prefer to take the path that will lead me to a bright future.

02:46:20.286 --> 02:46:22.397
President.

02:46:22.457 --> 02:46:25.458
A president is the leader of a country.

02:46:25.518 --> 02:46:30.619
The president of our country made an important announcement.

02:46:30.680 --> 02:46:32.850
Progress.

02:46:32.910 --> 02:46:37.871
Progress is the act of getting closer to doing or finishing something.

02:46:37.931 --> 02:46:42.372
Our company made financial progress this year.

02:46:42.432 --> 02:46:44.577
Respect.

02:46:44.637 --> 02:46:48.793
Respect is a good opinion of someone because they are good.

02:46:48.853 --> 02:46:52.604
I have great respect for firemen.

02:46:52.664 --> 02:46:54.676
Rich.

02:46:54.736 --> 02:46:57.778
If you are rich, you have a lot of money.

02:46:57.838 --> 02:46:59.278
He's rich.

02:46:59.338 --> 02:47:02.420
He can buy anything he wants.

02:47:02.480 --> 02:47:04.570
Skill.

02:47:04.630 --> 02:47:09.323
A skill is the knowledge and ability that allows you to do something well.

02:47:09.383 --> 02:47:14.222
A snowboarder must have the right skills to do well.

02:47:14.282 --> 02:47:16.390
Somehow.

02:47:16.450 --> 02:47:21.714
Somehow means, in a way or by some means, which is not known.

02:47:21.774 --> 02:47:27.078
He somehow had to find a way to reach the life preserver.

02:47:27.138 --> 02:47:29.230
Strength.

02:47:29.291 --> 02:47:32.832
Strength is the physical power that you have.

02:47:32.892 --> 02:47:38.087
Exercising will increase your strength and give you more power.

02:47:38.147 --> 02:47:40.118
Vote.

02:47:40.178 --> 02:47:44.766
To vote is to officially choose between two or more things.

02:47:44.826 --> 02:47:49.934
I voted for Billy to be our class president.

02:47:49.994 --> 02:47:53.756
How the world got light.

02:47:53.816 --> 02:47:56.909
The president of Darkland was a pig.

02:47:56.969 --> 02:47:59.025
A very bad pig.

02:47:59.085 --> 02:48:02.161
He was a pig of major importance.

02:48:02.221 --> 02:48:05.562
He was rich, and he had a lot of strength.

02:48:05.622 --> 02:48:09.334
But he was mean to all the animals in darkland.

02:48:09.394 --> 02:48:12.775
He kept all of the world's light in a bag.

02:48:12.835 --> 02:48:15.826
He preferred to keep the world cool and dark.

02:48:15.886 --> 02:48:19.067
He wanted to stop the progress of the city.

02:48:19.127 --> 02:48:21.748
The animals couldn't work in the dark.

02:48:21.808 --> 02:48:24.149
He didn't have any respect for them.

02:48:24.209 --> 02:48:27.050
Light is too good for them, he said.

02:48:27.110 --> 02:48:29.051
Only I should have light.

02:48:29.111 --> 02:48:34.113
But the animals needed light, so they decided to hold a competition.

02:48:34.173 --> 02:48:38.144
They wanted to find the smartest animal in darkland.

02:48:38.204 --> 02:48:41.716
That animal had to steal light from the president.

02:48:41.776 --> 02:48:45.087
They advertised the competition everywhere.

02:48:45.147 --> 02:48:47.138
All the animals gained.

02:48:47.198 --> 02:48:50.408
The animals all showed off their skills.

02:48:50.468 --> 02:48:55.700
The audience watched and then voted for the animal with the most knowledge.

02:48:55.760 --> 02:48:59.041
The winner was a tall bird named Raven.

02:48:59.101 --> 02:49:02.222
They assigned him the job of getting light.

02:49:02.282 --> 02:49:06.594
The next morning, Raven ate breakfast and then left his home.

02:49:06.654 --> 02:49:09.395
How will I gain light from the president?

02:49:09.455 --> 02:49:10.705
Thought Raven.

02:49:10.765 --> 02:49:13.636
He needed to trick the President somehow.

02:49:13.696 --> 02:49:16.366
Then Raven had an idea.

02:49:16.426 --> 02:49:19.737
Raven could make his voice sound like anything.

02:49:19.797 --> 02:49:22.648
Raven walked up to the President's door.

02:49:22.708 --> 02:49:25.538
He made the sound of a crying baby.

02:49:25.598 --> 02:49:27.899
He cried very loudly.

02:49:27.959 --> 02:49:30.529
Soon the President opened the door.

02:49:30.589 --> 02:49:33.620
Be quiet, the President yelled.

02:49:33.680 --> 02:49:36.681
Right then, Raven quickly made his move.

02:49:36.741 --> 02:49:40.002
He flew by the pig and found the soft bag.

02:49:40.062 --> 02:49:41.612
He took it outside.

02:49:41.672 --> 02:49:43.952
The sun was inside the bag.

02:49:44.012 --> 02:49:47.433
Raven flew high and put the sun in the sky.

02:49:47.493 --> 02:49:49.694
The president was very mad.

02:49:49.754 --> 02:49:51.284
Raven tricked him.

02:49:51.344 --> 02:49:54.285
But the other animals were very happy.

02:49:54.345 --> 02:50:01.085
At last, they had blind, all because of Raven's smart thinking.

02:50:01.145 --> 02:50:04.204
Unit 30.

02:50:04.264 --> 02:50:05.775
Word List.

02:50:05.835 --> 02:50:07.465
Above.

02:50:07.525 --> 02:50:11.986
If something is above, it is at a higher level than something else.

02:50:12.046 --> 02:50:16.458
He straightened the sign that was above the crowd.

02:50:16.518 --> 02:50:18.608
Ahead.

02:50:18.668 --> 02:50:22.719
If something is ahead of something else, it is in front of it.

02:50:22.779 --> 02:50:26.830
The blue car drove on ahead of us.

02:50:26.890 --> 02:50:28.970
Amount.

02:50:29.030 --> 02:50:32.362
An amount is how much there is of something.

02:50:32.422 --> 02:50:37.026
Can I use my card to pay for the entire amount?

02:50:37.086 --> 02:50:43.632
Belief A belief is a strong feeling that something is correct or true.

02:50:43.693 --> 02:50:48.997
A preacher or priest should have a strong belief in God.

02:50:49.057 --> 02:50:54.441
Center The center of something is the middle of it.

02:50:54.502 --> 02:50:59.466
The center of a dartboard is the most important spot.

02:50:59.526 --> 02:51:06.410
Common If something is common, it happens often or there is much of it.

02:51:06.470 --> 02:51:10.582
It is common for snow to fall in the winter.

02:51:10.642 --> 02:51:12.743
Cost.

02:51:12.803 --> 02:51:17.325
To cost is to require expenditure or payment.

02:51:17.386 --> 02:51:21.768
These designer shoes cost more than the regular ones.

02:51:21.828 --> 02:51:24.069
Demonstrate.

02:51:24.129 --> 02:51:27.892
To demonstrate something is to show how it is done.

02:51:27.952 --> 02:51:32.178
She demonstrated her plan to her coworkers.

02:51:32.239 --> 02:51:34.385
Different.

02:51:34.445 --> 02:51:39.730
Different describes someone or something that is not the same as others.

02:51:39.790 --> 02:51:45.124
Each of my sisters has a different hairstyle from one another.

02:51:45.184 --> 02:51:47.256
Evidence.

02:51:47.316 --> 02:51:51.920
Evidence is a fact or thing that you use to prove something.

02:51:51.980 --> 02:51:57.256
You use the pictures as evidence that UFOs are real.

02:51:57.316 --> 02:52:03.800
Honesty Honesty means the quality of being truthful or honest.

02:52:03.860 --> 02:52:07.962
A courtroom should be a place of honesty.

02:52:08.023 --> 02:52:14.716
Idiom An idiom is a phrase with a meaning different from its words.

02:52:14.776 --> 02:52:20.618
The idiom when pigs fly means that something will never happen.

02:52:20.678 --> 02:52:27.780
Independent If something is independent, it is not controlled by something else.

02:52:27.840 --> 02:52:32.680
She chose to live an independent life in the country.

02:52:32.740 --> 02:52:34.930
Inside.

02:52:34.990 --> 02:52:39.712
Inside means the inner part, space, or side of something.

02:52:39.772 --> 02:52:43.683
The inside of the box was empty.

02:52:43.743 --> 02:52:45.974
Master.

02:52:46.034 --> 02:52:49.725
A master is a person who is very good at something.

02:52:49.785 --> 02:52:54.036
My brother is a master of Taekwondo.

02:52:54.097 --> 02:52:56.164
Memory.

02:52:56.224 --> 02:52:59.183
A memory is something you remember.

02:52:59.243 --> 02:53:05.124
The memory of my first time in the city will always be the best.

02:53:05.185 --> 02:53:07.275
Proper.

02:53:07.335 --> 02:53:10.366
If something is proper, it is right.

02:53:10.426 --> 02:53:14.928
It is not proper to throw your garbage on the road.

02:53:14.988 --> 02:53:17.088
Scan.

02:53:17.148 --> 02:53:21.089
To scan something is to look at it very carefully.

02:53:21.149 --> 02:53:25.084
You must scan each person closely.

02:53:25.144 --> 02:53:30.762
Section A section is a part of something larger.

02:53:30.822 --> 02:53:35.737
The green section of the graph is the most important part.

02:53:35.797 --> 02:53:42.544
Surface The surface of something is the top part or outside of it.

02:53:42.604 --> 02:53:47.478
The surface of the moon is very rough.

02:53:47.538 --> 02:53:54.394
Cats and Secrets In English, there is a common idiom.

02:53:54.454 --> 02:53:56.696
Let the cat out of the bag.

02:53:56.756 --> 02:53:58.646
It means to tell a secret.

02:53:58.706 --> 02:54:01.178
But where did this idiom start?

02:54:01.238 --> 02:54:03.479
It came from a section of England.

02:54:03.539 --> 02:54:10.312
Long ago, people there went from town to town to sell things like vegetables, clothes and pigs.

02:54:10.373 --> 02:54:12.894
They had strong beliefs about honesty.

02:54:12.954 --> 02:54:14.815
They didn't like lying.

02:54:14.875 --> 02:54:18.908
One day, a man went to the section center to sell things.

02:54:18.968 --> 02:54:21.420
I have a baby pig for sale.

02:54:21.480 --> 02:54:24.062
It won't cost much," he said.

02:54:24.122 --> 02:54:26.314
He held the animal above his hand.

02:54:26.374 --> 02:54:29.636
His style was different from honest people's style.

02:54:29.696 --> 02:54:32.768
He was a master of tricking people in lying.

02:54:32.828 --> 02:54:35.970
A woman named Beth scanned his pig.

02:54:36.030 --> 02:54:39.071
He offered her the pig for one gold coin.

02:54:39.131 --> 02:54:41.362
That was a very small amount.

02:54:41.422 --> 02:54:43.284
Beth gave him the coin.

02:54:43.344 --> 02:54:45.201
He put it in his pocket.

02:54:45.261 --> 02:54:48.098
He walked ahead of Beth to get the pig.

02:54:48.158 --> 02:54:51.970
He gave her a closed bag and said, Here's your pig.

02:54:52.030 --> 02:54:54.432
He then left very quickly.

02:54:54.492 --> 02:54:57.044
Beth looked at the bag's surface.

02:54:57.104 --> 02:54:58.644
It was moving.

02:54:58.704 --> 02:55:01.166
She opened it to let the pig out.

02:55:01.226 --> 02:55:03.467
A cat was inside.

02:55:03.527 --> 02:55:05.258
He tricked me.

02:55:05.318 --> 02:55:08.080
That isn't proper, she said.

02:55:08.140 --> 02:55:11.154
Later the men returned to trick more people.

02:55:11.214 --> 02:55:14.708
Beth saw him and the memory of the cat came back.

02:55:14.768 --> 02:55:16.439
She told her friends.

02:55:16.499 --> 02:55:17.960
They stopped him.

02:55:18.020 --> 02:55:20.371
But no one knew what to do next.

02:55:20.431 --> 02:55:25.383
Someone said, we need an independent and fair person to decide that.

02:55:25.443 --> 02:55:27.024
They went to the judge.

02:55:27.084 --> 02:55:29.685
Beth told him about the cat in the bag.

02:55:29.745 --> 02:55:32.636
The judge asked, is there evidence?

02:55:32.696 --> 02:55:35.498
Can you demonstrate how he did it?

02:55:35.558 --> 02:55:38.290
Look in his bag, said Beth.

02:55:38.350 --> 02:55:41.613
She opened it and let a cat out of the bag.

02:55:41.673 --> 02:55:45.014
They learned the man's secret, and he went to jail.

02:55:45.074 --> 02:55:50.497
That's how the idiom, let the cat out of the bag, came to mean to tell a secret.